PVD("cambodia_ndp_2014-2018",{"docs":["","CMB NDP 2014 2018"],"s":{"1":[[1,"48","5","National Contingency Plan for Disaster Response","Development of a National Contingency Plan (NCP) for the disaster response aim at minimizing the impact of potential disasters.",""],[1,"48","6","Climate Change Strategic Plan for Disaster Risk Management Sector","Development of a strategic plan on climate change for disaster risk management sector and incorporation into the national strategic plan on climate change adaptation of the National Committee on Climate Change.",""],[1,"48","7","Annual Contribution to the AHA Centre Fund","the National Committee for Disaster Management (NCDM) has implemented the agreement on the establishment of ASEAN Coordinating Centre for Humanitarian Assistance on Disaster Management (AHA Centre) by contributed the amount of USD 30,000 to the AHA Centre Fund on the annual basis which commenced from the fiscal year 2012.",""],[1,"48","8","Provincial Contingency Planning for Disaster Response","In closed collaboration with the organization partners, the Provincial Contingency Plan (PCP) for responding at provincial level had been developed by 11 flood-prone provinces.",""],[1,"48","11","Disaster Risk Reduction Mainstreaming in Education Curriculum","Mainstreaming the disaster risk reduction into education sector by developing the textbook and incorporating into school curriculum at grade 4 and 8.",""],[1,"48","11","Disaster Risk Reduction Integration in MAFF and MOWRAM Project Plans","The disaster risk reduction has also mainstreamed into the project plans of the MAFF and MOWRAM.","MAFF | MOWRAM"],[1,"48","11","Disaster Management Integration into Safe Village and Sangkat-Commune Policy Guideline","the disaster management activities have been integrated into the safety village, Sangkat-commune policy guideline.",""],[1,"150","16","National Action Plan for Disaster Risk Reduction 2014-2018","RGC will implement the \"National Action Plan for Disaster Risk Reduction 2014-2018\" through participation from all concerned parties in the government, development partners, private sector, and civil society organizations.",""],[1,"150","17","Disaster Risk Reduction Mainstreaming Programme","Continuing to mainstream disaster risk reduction into policies, plans, and sustainable development programs at all levels.",""],[1,"150","18","Legal Framework and Coordination Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthening the legal framework, legal instruments, standard operation procedures, and policy guidelines, and establishing a mechanism in accordance with the actual requirement, by connecting local levels with regional and global levels.",""],[1,"150","19","Capacity Building for Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Adaptation Officials","Strengthening capacity of national and sub-national officials, particularly at the community levels, on disaster-risk reduction, climate change adaptation, and hazard resilience.",""],[1,"150","20","Disaster Risk Reduction Integration in Disaster Management Programs","Integrating disaster-risk reduction into the preparation and implementation of disaster preparedness, emergency response and recovery programs to minimize disaster losses, and encourage full participation of RGC institutions, civil society organizations, and the private sector.",""],[1,"151","1","Strengthening the National Committee for Disaster Management","RGC will strengthen the role of the National Committee for Disaster Management in coordinating and implementing \"National Action Plan and Strategy on Disaster Risk Reduction 2014-2018\"",""],[1,"151","2","Strengthen Disaster Management Institutions","Strengthen Disaster Management Institutions at the National, Sub-national, and Local Community Levels, to ensure the effectiveness of disaster-risk reduction by:",""],[1,"151","3","Disaster Management Law Reform","Improving and finalizing the law on disaster management.",""],[1,"151","4","Disaster Management Mechanism Strengthening","Establishing and strengthening disaster management mechanisms by defining the organization and functioning of the national, sub-national, and local levels.",""],[1,"151","5","Disaster Risk Reduction Policy and Legal Framework Development","Developing policy guidelines, legal instruments and the legal framework to support disaster risk reduction activities.",""],[1,"151","6","Disaster Risk Reduction Mainstreaming","Mainstreaming disaster risk reduction into policy guidelines and development plans at all levels.",""],[1,"151","7","Disaster Risk Assessment, Monitoring, and Early Warning System Improvement","Enhancing Disaster Risk Assessment and Monitoring and Improving Early Warning System by:",""],[1,"151","8","National, Sub-National, and Local Risk Assessment","Conducting risk-assessment at the national, sub-national, and local levels.",""],[1,"151","9","Vulnerability and Hazard Mapping","Developing vulnerability and hazard maps.",""],[1,"151","10","Disaster Database Management System Development","Developing the disaster database management system.",""],[1,"151","12","Early-Warning System for Hazard-Prone Communes","Setting up an Early-Warning System (EWS) on hazards for Sangkat/commune, particularly communities exposed to hazards.",""],[1,"151","13","Emergency Operation Centers Establishment","Establishing Emergency Operation Centers (EOC) at national and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"151","14","Technological Research Capacity for Hazard Forecasting","Developing capacities in technological research for forecasting natural hazards and other hazards.",""],[1,"151","15","Data Improvement for Assessment, Monitoring, and Early Warning","Improving existing data for further assessment, monitoring and early warning in conformity with the regional and international sectoral bodies.",""],[1,"151","16","Hazard Assessment Information Management Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening capacity of recording, analyzing, disseminating, and exchanging information for hazard assessment and monitoring.",""],[1,"151","18","Hazard, Vulnerability, and Capacity Information Dissemination","Collecting, compiling, and disseminating knowledge and information on hazards, vulnerabilities, and capacities to the people for building the culture of prevention and disaster resiliency.",""],[1,"151","19","Disaster Risk Information Provision","Providing simple and understandable information on disaster risk to people at the risk of getting exposed to hazards.",""],[1,"151","20","Sangkat/Commune Disaster Risk Reduction Planning","Developing Sangkat/commune disaster risk reduction plans.",""],[1,"151","21","Disaster Risk Reduction Stakeholder Partnership Strengthening","Strengthening cooperation and promoting partnership among relevant stakeholders, including professionals involved in socio-economic activities for disaster risk reduction.",""],[1,"151","22","Space Technology and Satellite Map Interpretation Services","Accessing new information, space technology and other services, including the interpretation of satellite maps, and putting them to use.",""],[1,"151","23","Khmer Disaster-Risk Terminology Translation for Training Materials","Making the standard international terminologies on disaster-risk available in Khmer, for utilization in specialized institutions as training materials.",""],[1,"151","24","Disaster Risk Reduction Curriculum Integration","Integrating disaster the risk-reduction concept and disaster prevention program into school and higher education institution curricula.",""],[1,"151","25","Disaster Risk Reduction Training Modules and Curricula Development","Developing training modules and curricula on disaster risk reduction for the different levels (planners, emergency managers, and administrative officials).",""],[1,"151","26","Climate Vulnerability and Hazard Assessment Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening technological and scientific capacities to assess vulnerabilities and hazard-prone areas in relation to the climate change.",""],[1,"151","27","National and Sub-national Disaster Risk Reduction Forums","Establishing national and sub-national forums for disaster risk reduction.",""],[1,"152","3","Mainstreaming Disaster Risk Reduction into Climate Change Adaptation Strategy","Mainstreaming disaster risk reduction related to climate change into the disaster risk reduction and climate change adaptation strategy.",""],[1,"152","4","Disaster Risk Reduction Mainstreaming Across Key Sectors","Mainstreaming the disaster risk reduction plan into the health, education, agriculture, forestry and fishery, and rural development sectors.",""],[1,"152","6","Disaster Recovery Planning and Socio-Psychology Training Programme","Strengthening disaster recovery plans, to include socio-psychology training programs, in minimizing the adverse impact on the victims, particularly women and children, in post-disaster times.",""],[1,"152","7","Emergency Response Preparedness Strengthening","Strengthening preparedness for Effective Emergency Response at the National, Sub- National and Local Community Levels by:",""],[1,"152","8","Emergency Preparedness and Contingency Planning","Developing preparedness plan for emergency response and updating the contingency plan to be effective at all levels.",""],[1,"152","9","Emergency Response Coordination Teams","Forming the emergency response coordinating teams.",""],[1,"152","10","Search and Emergency Rescue Teams","Forming search and emergency rescue teams.",""],[1,"152","11","Disaster Assessment Coordination Teams","Forming disaster assessment coordinating teams.",""],[1,"152","12","Disaster Management Coordination Procedure Development","Developing a coordinating procedure in accordance with ASEAN Coordinating Centre for Humanitarian Assistance on Disaster Management (AHA Centre) and implementing the ASEAN Agreement on Disaster Management and Emergency Response (AADMER).",""],[1,"152","13","Disaster Preparedness Simulation and Response Exercise","Undertaking a disaster preparedness simulation exercise, including the real exercise, to ensure rapid and timely response and providing relief to the affected localities.",""],[1,"152","15","Construction of Safe Areas with Basic Sanitation and Shelter","Constructing safe areas, equipped with bathrooms, latrines, and shelters for humans and animals.",""],[1,"194","17","Disaster Management and Response Strengthening","Strengthen disaster management and response.",""]],"2":[[1,"194","15","Oral Health, Hygiene, Sanitation, and Food Safety Promotion","Promote oral health, hygiene and sanitation, and food safety.",""],[1,"200","2","Homestead Food Production and Nutrition Awareness Initiative","Increase the local availability and accessibility of diversified food (through homestead food production) and raise awareness on nutritional values of local agricultural products to the community.",""],[1,"200","3","Child and Maternal Nutrition Improvement Programme","Improve child and maternal nutrition through increasing the extent to which women and their new baby born are covered along the first 1000 days of life through scaling up existing delivery mechanisms, improving the quality of nutrition care and counselling in the health system, increasing access to safe and nutritious complementary foods, and expanding nutrition education through media campaigns and community based programes.",""],[1,"200","4","Mandatory Micronutrient Fortification of Staples and Condiments","Expand fortification of staples and condiments with micronutrients, including making fish and soy sauce with iron mandatory to counteract the high levels of child and maternal anaemia.",""],[1,"200","5","Nutrition Service Demand Support through Social Protection","Improve food access for the poor and vulnerable, including people living with HIV/AIDS; enhance demand for nutrition services through social protection instruments.",""],[1,"200","6","Sanitation Access and Hygiene Promotion Initiative","Improve access to sanitation, promote safe hygiene practices and increase knowledge of the importance of good sanitation and hygiene.",""],[1,"200","7","Smallholder Farming Diversification and Market Linkage Programme","Intensify and diversify small holder farming systems and improve linkages to markets.",""],[1,"200","8","Secure Land Access for Poor and Food-Insecure Households","Enhance sustainable and secure access to land for the poor and food-insecure.",""],[1,"200","9","Common Property Fishery and Forestry Resource Management","Improve access to and sustainable use of common property fishery and forestry resources.",""],[1,"200","10","Employment and Income Support for Food-Insecure Households","Enhance employment and income opportunities for the food-insecure, targeting vulnerable populations.",""],[1,"200","11","Disaster Preparedness and Climate Resilience for Food-Insecure Households","Reduce vulnerability of the food insecure population and protect them against risk by improving disaster preparedness and mitigation and enhance resilience of households against effects of climate change.",""],[1,"200","12","Food Security and Nutrition Mainstreaming in Social Protection Strategy","Mainstream access to food security and improved nutrition as an objective for the social protection strategy.",""],[1,"200","14","Child and Maternal Nutrition Action and Investment Plan","Developing a nutrition action plan and investment plan to improve child and maternal nutrition.",""],[1,"200","15","Community-Based Nutrition Program","Designing a community based nutrition program across sectors and implement through sub-national government levels.",""],[1,"200","16","Integrated Maternal and Child Nutrition Services Scale-Up","Commit to scaling up integrated interventions that promoting optimal use of nutrition 'specific' services, ultimately leading to enhanced maternal and child nutrition status (management of acute malnutrition, micronutrient supplementation, complementary feeding campaign, nutrition message during ANC and PNC).",""],[1,"200","17","Nutrition Policy and Sub-Decree Enforcement","Enforce policies and sub-decree to ensure optimal nutritional status (breast-milk substitute sub-decree, iodized salt sub-decree).",""],[1,"200","18","Public-Private Partnership for Nutrition-Specific Services","Initiate innovative public-private partnership to support government nutrition 'specific' services.",""],[1,"200","19","Nutrition Policy and Guideline Improvement","Develop or improve policies, guidelines to improve effectiveness of nutrition 'specific' interventions and nutrition 'sensitive' services.",""],[1,"201","1","Evidence-Based Policy Research Support","Support research to increase evidence based policies (micronutrient, obesity, thalassemia data, and impact of innovative solutions through private-public partnership).",""],[1,"201","2","Joint WASH and Nutrition Collaboration","Support joint-collaboration WASH/Nutrition, early childhood education/Nutrition, and maternity in the workplace/Nutrition.",""],[1,"201","3","Nutrition Capacity Strengthening for Central and Local Governments","Strengthen capacity of central and local governments on nutrition to provide basic nutrition 'specific' services.",""],[1,"201","4","Strengthen CARD Policy Guidance and FSN Coordination","Strengthening CARD's role as the institution providing policy guidance and enhance coordination and integration of FSN related work into RGC institutions in both national and sub-national planning process.",""],[1,"201","5","Strengthening the TWG-SP&FSN Coordination Mechanism","Strengthening the TWG-SP&FSN to effectively coordinate projects and programs based on the priorities outlined in the NSFSN across sectors and enhance harmonization and alignment of development partner's support for FSN in Cambodia.",""],[1,"201","6","Food Security and Nutrition Program Coordination Mechanism","Ensuring effective coordination of FSN programs between departments of ministries, civil society organizations, development partners and the private sector at province, district and commune level.",""],[1,"201","7","NSFSN Indicator Framework Revision and Consolidation","Revising and consolidating the indicator framework for the NSFSN based on a set of indicators and realistic targets aligned with all relevant existing sector strategies and plans.",""],[1,"201","8","NSFSN Monitoring, Evaluation, and Reporting Mechanism","Establishing appropriate M&E procedures and reporting mechanism in order to ensure effective implementation of the NSFSN and to provide evidence-based feedback for the further development of programs and interventions.",""],[1,"201","9","FSN Information Integration and Knowledge Management System","Strengthening the integration and harmonization of FSN information and knowledge management in Cambodia to present coherent and consolidated FSN information to decision makers and targeting FSN intervention.",""],[1,"201","10","Food Security and Nutrition Coordination and Data Analysis Capacity Strengthening","Continuation the operation of Food Security and Nutrition Management Task Force (FSN-MTF) and Food Security and Nutrition Data Analysis Team (FSN-DAT) and strengthen their capacities for FSN related data analysis and provide predictable resources for this task to enhance sustainability.",""],[1,"201","11","CARD SP&FSN Information System Integration and Maintenance","Ensuring the integration and operation of CARD's SP&FSN Information System (SP&FSN IS) website and update its content regularly.",""],[1,"201","12","FSN Information Products for Planning and Decision-Making","Promote the use of FSN information products for planning and decision making at national and decentralized levels.",""],[1,"201","13","FSN Training Curriculum Revision and Decentralized Training Scale-Up","Revising FSN training curricula for national and decentralized levels based on impact assessment and scale up training at decentralized level.",""],[1,"201","14","FSN Human Resource Development Plan","Developing and implement FSN human resource development plan to enhance overall capacities for FSN coordination and policy oversight at national level.",""],[1,"201","16","Infant and Young Child Feeding Promotion","Promote modern infant and young child feeding practices, in particular breast-feeding and complementary feeding.",""],[1,"201","17","Vitamin A Supplementation and Deworming Coverage Expansion","Improve Vitamin A supplementation and deworming coverage, by targeting hard to reach areas.",""],[1,"201","18","Multiple Micronutrient Food Supplementation Expansion","Increase the coverage of multiple micro-nutritious food supplementation (e.g. multiple micro-nutrient powders for children, fish and soy sauce fortification with iron, iodized salt).",""],[1,"201","19","Integrated Outreach and Community-Based Nutrition Services","Strengthen integrated outreach services and community-bases services, including growth monitoring and screening, and nutrition counseling.",""],[1,"201","20","Severe Acute Malnutrition Management Scale-Up","Scale-up management of severe acute malnutrition with complication.",""],[1,"201","21","Nutrition-Related Regulatory Enforcement","Enforce implementing nutrition-related regulations, such as restricting advertisements of breast milk substitutes.",""],[1,"202","1","Food Fortification for Nutrition Improvement","MOP will promote nutrition through fortifying micro-nutrients in food with following activities:","MOP"],[1,"202","2","National Policy on Technical Regulations and Micronutrient Fortification Guidelines","Formulating a national policy on technical regulations and guideline on micro-nutrients fortification in food and promotion of effective utilization of existing legal regulations.",""],[1,"202","3","Micronutrient Food Fortification Expansion","Expanding the micro-nutrient fortification in other food and ensuring the safety quality and quantity with the demand.",""]],"3":[[1,"88","3","Continued National Development Agenda Implementation","The government is of the opinion that Cambodia continues to be committed to further implementing the national development agenda and priorities to move forward the core principles of NPP and MDG beyond 2015.",""],[1,"114","2","Rectangular Strategy Phase III","The 4 strategic rectangles of the Strategy will be maintained with expanded scope, refined and reprioritized sides, and improved and more effective policies and mechanisms.",""],[1,"114","5","Mainstreaming of Cross-Cutting Issues in the Plan","Among the key cross-cutting issues that this plan will attempt to bring within its fold are, gender (this is an on-going commitment in the interests of equity, justice and efficiency), environment, natural resources and green growth (this is a necessity at all levels, to save our common heritage, disaster management (this is becoming an increasing necessity)",""],[1,"241","6","National Strategic Development Plan Alignment Framework","The NSDP's purpose is to ensure that the actions, programs and projects of all ministries, agencies and sub-national authorities are aligned to implement the prioritised policies of the RGC outlined in the Rectangular Strategy.",""]],"4":[[1,"18","12","Public Administration Reform and Decentralisation","These are: (iii) public administration reforms (including decentralisation and de- concentration);",""],[1,"22","13","Governance Action Plans for Reform Coordination","Governance Action Plans (GAPs) is to facilitate coordination among national and sectoral reforms in the context of successive.",""],[1,"22","16","Special Operating Agency and Single Window Expansion","Establishing Special Operating Agency (SOA) including the introduction of a public service database and the expanded scope of the \"single window\" mechanism to 24 municipal/district/khan office.",""],[1,"22","17","Administrative and Organizational Restructuring","Restructuring the administration system and other organizational structures at the capital, province, municipality, district and khan levels in accordance with the Law on Management of the Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts and Khans.",""],[1,"22","18","Sub-national Financial Management System Development","Developing and establishing the sub-national financial management system in compliance with the Law on Financial Regime and Property Management of Sub- national Administrations.",""],[1,"23","8","Public Services Delivery Policy Implementation","The Policy on Public Services Delivery has been approved and is being implemented.",""],[1,"24","1","Sub-national Administration Coaching, Mentoring, and Training Support","The RGC also continued the provision of coaching and mentoring services to SNA Councils and Organizational Development (OD) process.",""],[1,"24","2","Functional Mapping and Function Transfer to SNAs","Five Ministries completed their functional mapping exercises and are making decisions about which functions to transfer to SNAs, either permanently or on a pilot basis.","Five Ministries"],[1,"24","2","Pilot Design for SNA Function Transfers","at least two pilots are currently being designed.",""],[1,"24","3","District and Municipality Capacity Development Programme","These funds support an extensive and active capacity development program, including organizational development, training, and coaching and mentoring of councillors.",""],[1,"24","3","Commune and Sangkat Local Development Financing","Resources, through the CS Fund, equivalent to 2.8% of recurrent revenues have continued to enable Communes and Sangkat to implement their local development priorities.",""],[1,"24","4","Delegation of Civil Service Management Powers to Sub-national Administrations","In terms of enabling SNAs to manage their own personnel, two key instruments were (i) an amendment to the law on the establishment and functioning of the Council of Ministers (which has been approved by the King) and (ii) a draft sub-decree on the delegation of power to SNA for the management, appointment, movement and termination of civil servants working at Sub-national levels.",""],[1,"24","5","Social Accountability Strategic Plan for Sub-National Democratic Development","Social Accountability Strategic Plan for Sub-National Democratic Development was approved by NCDD.",""],[1,"24","6","Planning Systems and Procedures Update","Planning systems and procedures have been updated, and, as a matter of routine, all SNAs have 5-year development plans and 3-year investment programs; CS plans continue to be developed and coordinated through District Integration Workshops.",""],[1,"24","8","One Window Service Office Expansion","the MOI is also preparing to open new 13 OWSOs in municipalities and Khan in Phnom Penh in 2014.","MOI"],[1,"24","8","District Ombudsman Office Establishment","The District Ombudsman Office is an independent and neutral institution that receives and mediates complaints made by citizen in relation to service delivery of district/musicality/Khan administration.","MOI"],[1,"25","3","Subnational Authority Human Resource Autonomy Reform","SNAs will need to be provided more autonomy to restructure their offices, attract, hire, fire, discipline, reward, manage and develop human resources.",""],[1,"25","4","Strengthening SNA Accountability and Oversight","Strengthening horizontal and vertical SNA accountabilities is an important IP3 objective.",""],[1,"25","4","Review of Council and Board Governance Arrangements","Relationships between councils and Boards of Governors needs review",""],[1,"25","4","Strengthening Councillor Oversight of Central Government Service Delivery","councillors' oversight role with respect to Central Government service delivery functions needs strengthening",""],[1,"25","4","Development and Inspection of Policies and Standards","the Central Government will need to increasingly develop and inspect policies and standards.",""],[1,"25","5","Mechanisms to Encourage SNA Innovation and Initiative","Mechanisms to encourage SNAs to be more innovative and to take more initiative within the scope of their poverty alleviation mandate need further development.",""],[1,"26","8","Decentralization and De-concentration Reform Programme","The MOI has been engaged in three major roles: (i) managing the sub-national public administration institutions; (ii) ensuring internal security of the nation, and public order through the National Police Forces (NFP); and (iii) leading and coordinating the implementation of RGC's Decentralization and De-concentration Reform Programme (D&D).","MOI"],[1,"41","1","Decentralized Construction Permit Issuance","Decentralized/delegated function to the municipality, district, and khan so they have authority to issue a permission letter for construction and for other services relating to the construction work with the size smaller than or equivalent to 500 sqm at the one window service office in the 23 municipalities/districts/khans.",""],[1,"49","3","Decentralization of Public Services","RGC has adopted a multi-pronged approach to foster rural development and empower local communities to plan and manage development.",""],[1,"49","4","Rural Development Priority Sector Budget Allocation and Disbursement Mechanism","Since 2007, Rural Development is a priority sector among other priority sectors of the RGC under the Public Financial Management Reform Program (PFMRP), which is now Step 2, for budget allocations and timely disbursements.",""],[1,"49","5","Rural Policy and Regulatory Framework Development","Institutional and human resource capacity development have been progressing though the development of policy and regulatory framework under the following regulations:",""],[1,"99","27","Administrative Management Law Implementation","Implement the new Law on Administrative Management of The Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts, and Khans",""],[1,"99","27","National Program for Subnational Democratic Development","national program for subnational democratic development",""],[1,"100","1","Sub-national Capacity Building and Functional Devolution","3. Strengthen capacities at sub-national levels, Hands-on training programs to sub-national staff. 4. Accelerate functional assignment/ delegation of authority to sub-national governance institutions, incl. financial devolution.",""],[1,"100","3","National-Subnational Coordination and Jurisdiction Clarification","Establish better coordination & communication between national and sub-national authorities, identify jurisdictions more clearly.",""],[1,"107","3","District and Municipal Capacity-Building Reform","The immediate focus of Cambodia's local government reform efforts is on establishing and developing the capacity of Districts and Municipalities as institutions for both local governance and local development.",""],[1,"107","3","Local Government Reform Policy and Legal Framework","This will consist of: (1) a policy and legal environment that shapes and supports the reforms set out in the Organic Law",""],[1,"107","3","Autonomous and Capable Sub-National Administration Strengthening","This will consist of: (2) the encouragement of autonomous and capable SNAs (having financial and human resources)",""],[1,"107","3","National Oversight Framework for Sub-National Authorities","This will consist of: (3) a framework and system of oversight, including legal, regulatory and strategic instruments, exercised by national authorities with the capacity to enforce them, replacing the current system of administrative control, and thereby allowing SNAs to exercise their autonomy and to be accountable for the results of their actions within an overall national framework.",""],[1,"107","4","SNA Autonomy and Innovation Support Framework","Promote SNA autonomy and innovation; develop an institutional environment which promotes SNA and community initiatives that address pressing development needs.",""],[1,"107","5","SNA Accountability and Governance Strengthening","Promote SNA accountability (vertical and horizontal; political, administrative and social); promote participation, civic engagement, transparency, responsiveness and good governance; strengthen the representative function of councillors and SNA policy and regulatory functions.",""],[1,"107","6","Oversight and Compliance System Strengthening","Develop and strengthen oversight processes and compliance systems that both ensure value for money and provide the autonomy SNAs require.",""],[1,"107","7","SNA Service Delivery Improvement","Improve SNA service delivery procedures, systems, processes and performance.",""],[1,"107","8","SNA Governance and Checks-and-Balances Strengthening","Improve SNA deliberative, administrative, and management systems; strengthen the system of intra-SNA checks and balances between legislators and executives.",""],[1,"107","9","Decentralization of Central Government Functions","Transfer central government functions to local governments in order to bring decision making and accountability closer to the people; revise structures and staffing arrangements in SNAs, and between SNAs and central government, to make them more efficient.",""],[1,"107","11","Fiscal Transfers and Own-Source Revenue Support for SNAs","Ensure SNAs have ample financial resources, both through conditional and unconditional central government fiscal transfers as well as by generating own source revenues; own source revenues are also envisioned as a mechanism to promote SNA autonomy and to strengthen accountability with citizens.",""],[1,"121","29","National Program for Democratic Development at the Sub-national Level","RGC will further promote the implementation of decentralization and de- concentration reforms through the 'National Program for Democratic Development at the Sub-national Level 2010-2019', by focusing on:",""],[1,"122","2","Enforcement of the Law on Financial Regime and Property Management of Sub-national Administrations","Enforce the Law on Financial Regime and Property Management of Sub-national Administrations, especially the gradual transfer of functions and resources within some priority sectors from the national to the sub-national levels.",""],[1,"122","3","Sub-national Capacity Development and Council Strengthening","Improve human and institutional capacity development at the sub-national levels and strengthening the roles and responsibilities of the sub-national councils with focus on the planning systems at sub-national administration level, by defining clear mechanisms for results-monitoring and evaluation, as well as in conformity with the law.",""],[1,"122","4","Strengthening Unified Sub-National Administration Coordination","Strengthen the efficiency of a unified sub-national administration in coordinating all activities of the public administration by imparting the supervisory role to the sub-national administration.",""],[1,"122","5","National Program on Sub-National Democratic Development","NCDD of Ministry of Interior (MOI) has developed a National Program on Sub-National Democratic Development with the following commitments:","Ministry of Interior (MOI)"],[1,"122","6","Transfer of Central Government Functions to Sub-National Authorities","Key Central Government functions will be transferred to SNAs, together with corresponding resources (revenue, finance, personnel, property, and capacity for managing and fulfilling the respective functions), powers, and duties to carry out those functions.",""],[1,"122","7","SNA Own-Source Revenue Collection and Fiscal Transfer Reform","SNAs collection of own source revenues and new fiscal transfer mechanisms will increase, thus expanding service delivery and improving accountability.",""],[1,"122","9","SNA Accountability and Councilor Authority Reform","SNA vertical and horizontal accountabilities will be improved and councilors will have increased decision-making authority.",""],[1,"122","10","SNA Organizational and Institutional Improvement","SNA organizational/institutional will be improved.",""]],"5":[[1,"130","14","Stakeholder Partnership and Development Coordination","The RRC has strengthened partnerships with all the stakeholders in development, including the development partner community, the private sector, and the civil society, based on basic laid down principles and global commitments, to assure ownership of the RGC in leading the national development process.",""],[1,"131","2","Inclusive Development Partnership and Results Monitoring Framework","effective development partnerships must accommodate a diversity of actors and innovative modalities, embracing the differentiated contribution made by each toward common goals of the country in an inclusive partnership.",""],[1,"131","3","Results-Based Planning, Partnership, and Monitoring Frameworks","the adoption of approaches that support planning, partnership and monitoring.",""],[1,"131","4","Development Partnership and Resource Mobilization","Continuing to strengthen partnership in development with all stakeholders in order to mobilize financial resources from all sources for the country's development based on the principle of ownership and leadership of the cooperation initiatives by the Royal Government.",""],[1,"131","5","Strategy on Development Cooperation and Partnership 2014-2018","Preparing and implementing the \"Strategy on Development Cooperation and Partnership 2014-2018\".",""],[1,"132","2","Annual Government-NGO Consultative Meeting","Conducting an annual consultative meeting between the Government and NGOs while at the same time promoting the enactment of the law on associations and NGOS through broader consultation with all concerned stakeholders to ensure efficiency, transparency, and accountability of their operations.",""],[1,"132","3","Cambodia Development Forum Consolidation","Continuing to strengthen Cambodia Development Cooperation Forum, Government- Private Sector Forum, Consultative Meeting between Government and NGOs, and Bilateral Consultation mechanisms, with the aim to transform all these fora into a \"Cambodia Development Forum\" which will serve as a unified platform for dialogue between the Royal Government and all its stakeholders, including development partners, private sector and NGOs as well as other relevant stakeholders, to discuss development issues in the country.",""],[1,"212","1","Partnership Expansion and Development Resource Mobilization","RGC will continue strengthening and broadening the types and scopes of partnerships of ministries, institutions and agencies, with different development partners (DPs), (national and international) NGOs, and other civil society stakeholders to maximize the benefits for the people of Cambodia.",""],[1,"212","2","Public Financial Management Reform Program Harmonization and Coordination Measures","RGC is taking concrete actions to further strengthen and refine the harmonization of planning [along with monitoring and evaluation (M&E)], public investment expenditures, and development-cooperation-financing, among RGC institutions within the framework of its Public Financial Management Reform Program.",""],[1,"215","14","Budget Support Delivery Linked to Performance Targets","the government hopes to see the development partners take urgent actions to deliver their development cooperation financial resources through 'budget support', linked to measurable qualitative and quantitative performance targets in each of the chosen sectors.",""],[1,"215","15","Strengthen Government Ownership and Leadership of Development Priorities","It will enhance government ownership and leadership of development priorities, policies and programs.",""],[1,"216","2","In-Country Oversight and Accountability Mechanism for External Funds","It will enhance in-country oversight and accountability through nationally established or recognized institutions for the receipt and use of external funds.",""],[1,"216","3","Budget Support as Preferred External Assistance Mechanism","RGC will continue to highlight the importance of moving towards \"budget support\" as the most preferred mechanism for providing external support to its development partners.",""],[1,"216","4","Sector-Wide and Programme-Based Aid Harmonization Support","RGC urges its development partners to provide support to the development of sector-wide or programme-based approaches for the key sectors of the economy and to deliver their assistance in a coordinated manner to implement the sector-wide programs for achieving cohesion and synergy and avoid overlap and/or duplication.",""],[1,"216","4","Strengthening of Sectoral Technical Working Groups","RGC also recognizes that the operations of the sectoral Technical Working Groups (TWG) need to be reviewed and strengthened to carry out the task of aid harmonization.",""],[1,"216","5","Strengthening and Simplifying Technical Working Group Mechanism","RGC will work with its development partners to strengthen the existing TWG mechanism to enhance efficiency, especially on technical cooperation for the development of human resources and institutional capacity, and to strengthen cooperation among the different stakeholders.",""],[1,"216","6","Technical Working Group Membership Limitation Rule","Limiting the membership of international development partners in a single TWG to those who deliver financial or technical support to the concerned sector.",""],[1,"216","7","Technical Working Group Participation Strengthening","To improve the quality and level of discussion at the Technical Working Groups, RGC would like to see the participation of personnel who are technically qualified to provide advice and support to the sector.",""],[1,"216","8","Meeting Agenda Circulation and Minutes Management","Prepared agenda items with specific details are to be circulated in advance, and minutes of the last meetings maintained, circulated and retrieved when required.",""],[1,"216","9","Development Partner Alignment and Resource Reallocation for Priority Policies","RGC will continue to urge its development partners to strive to ensure that their assistance is fully aligned to achieving the NSDP 2014-2018's priority policies at a detailed operational level and not just at the broad thematic level.",""],[1,"217","1","Inter-Institutional Task Force for Planning and Development Cooperation Coordination","A Task Force comprised of four key RGC institutions-chaired by Ministry of Planning-has been established within the framework of the RGC Public Financial Management Reform Programme (PFMRP).","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"217","2","Review of Planning, Public Investment, and Development Cooperation Coordination Mechanisms","Review the roles of RGC institutions and the mechanisms and approaches pertaining to the planning process, and the process for managing, coordinating and implementing public investment expenditures and development cooperation resources.",""],[1,"217","3","Public Investment and Development Cooperation Harmonization Measures","Propose measures to harmonize public investment expenditures and allocation and utilization of development cooperation resources to ensure consistency between these two processes in order to prepare a sound and inclusive National Budget Expenditure Plan that is consistent with the Rectangular Strategy Phase III, the National Strategic Development Plan, and Sectoral Strategies as outlined in the Action Plan on Harmonization, Alignment and PFMRP.",""],[1,"218","1","Development Cooperation Resource Alignment and Disbursement Review Mechanism","To ensure a better alignment of the development cooperation resources with RGC's public investment priorities, the data collected annually by RGC from development partners on actual and planned disbursements of their assistance will be analyzed by ministry/agency and each ministry/agency will be provided this information to: (i) review and verify that the information on disbursements are reported for their ministry/agency, and (ii) provide feedback on programs/projects financed that are aligned with NSDP priorities and those that are not.",""],[1,"220","4","Multi-Stakeholder Development Partnership Coordination","Engaging all development constituencies (development partners, private sector, sub- national agencies, others) in an effective partnership, coordinated under the leadership of the government.",""],[1,"242","3","Inclusive National Strategic Development Planning Process","the Ministry of Planning (MOP) has taken concrete steps to ensure active participation from the line ministries and agencies as well as sub-national authorities in the planning process.","Ministry of Planning (MOP)"]],"6":[[1,"99","12","Cadastral Survey and Land Rights Security Programme","Step up cadastral exercises to know how much surplus arable land (& other resources) exists, Ensure land rights, Demine more areas, Implement surplus arable land policy in equitable manner, Provide wherewithal for modern farming in new/cleaned up areas, Safety nets.",""],[1,"100","4","Land Arbitration Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthen arbitration mechanisms esp. for land.",""],[1,"100","10","Land Titling Intensification","Intensify land-titling.",""],[1,"116","1","Land Reform","other reform programs including public financial management reform, land reform, and forestry and fisheries reform",""],[1,"140","2","Land Reform and Land Management Strengthening","RGC will intensify land reforms, focusing on strengthening the management, organization, utilization and distribution of lands",""],[1,"140","3","Comprehensive Land Policy Formulation","Further promoting the formulation of a comprehensive land policy entitled \"White Paper on Land\".",""],[1,"140","5","Accelerated Land Registration and Titling Programme","Accelerating land registration and issuance of land titles including for state lands, private lands and indigenous community lands through regular land registration process and further implementing the \"Old Policy-New Action\" policy giving priority to land titling in dispute-free areas in order to guarantee security of title and ensure confidence in land ownership.",""],[1,"140","6","Land Management and Land Use Database Development","Further promoting the establishment of the database of land management and land use to provide the basis for the proper planning of land use and land classification under the following categories: agriculture, industry, tourism, rural areas, town, residential areas and protected areas, with the view to rationalize land use and avoid inappropriate use or conversion of land.",""],[1,"140","10","Land Dispute Settlement Mechanisms","Resolving land disputes in an effective, transparent and just manner in accordance with existing law and regulations through either court or out-of-court land dispute settlement mechanisms.",""],[1,"141","3","Land Measurement and Titling Programme","Measuring land and giving land titles to the people within the framework of the implementation of the \"Old Policy-New Action\", related to the 3 types of state lands: forest concessions, economic land concessions, and confiscated land.",""],[1,"141","4","State Land Encroachment Prevention Measure","Prevent state land from further encroachment after the 07th of May, 2012.",""],[1,"141","5","Accelerated Land Registration and Dispute Resolution","Speeding up of all types of land registration(to reach at least 6 to 7 million parcels throughout the country) and accelerating land dispute resolution to achieve the target plans of land registration accordingly 52% by 2014, 57% by 2015 and 70% by 2018.",""],[1,"141","6","Land Law and Related Legislation Reform","Drafting and finalizing a new land law and other related legislations such as Pre- emption law, Secularization Law, Law on Land Tax, land measurement and land sub-division.",""],[1,"141","7","Comprehensive Land Policy Adoption","Draft of Comprehensive land policy is ready for sending to council of minister",""],[1,"141","8","National Land and Property Valuation Policy and Mapping System","Draft and adopt the National Policy on Land and Properties Valuation System and related legal policy documents for implementation, as well as to develop maps for valuating properties in accordance with the practical situation of the country.",""],[1,"141","9","National Land Information System Policy and Legal Regulations","Drafting and getting approval of national policy on land information system and legal regulations.",""],[1,"141","10","One-Window Cadastral Service Policy","Drafting and adopting the policy for establishing a one window cadastral service system.",""],[1,"141","11","Study of Land Possession Rights for Farmers","Study the status of land possession rights that can be granted to farmers for legal possession and seasonal cultivation around Tonle Sap Lake and low-land areas covered under the Mekong River's water scheme.",""],[1,"141","12","Indigenous Community Land Title Registration","Continue registering land titles for indigenous communities.",""],[1,"141","13","Commune Boundary Demarcation Technical Support","Providing technical support for setting commune (administrative boundaries) where the demarcations are not clear.",""]],"7":[[1,"98","2","Institutional Capacity and Public Service Governance Improvement","Improving the institutional capacity and governance at both national and sub-national levels and ensuring effectiveness and efficiency of public services to better serve the people.",""],[1,"99","9","Governance and Public Administration Reform Package","Predictable governance, Functional courts with access to justice for all, Transparent laws, Land laws implemented, Land cadaster speeded up, Civil administration made more responsive, Reforms in govt. staff, Better salary for government staff, Operation and Maintenance (O&M) expenses (for government work). Responsive, accountable and transparent decentralized services, functions, budgets and staff.",""],[1,"116","1","Public Administration Reform","the Royal Government has firmly implemented key reform programs, including: (3) public administration reform",""],[1,"116","1","Public Financial Management Reform","other reform programs including public financial management reform, land reform, and forestry and fisheries reform",""],[1,"120","3","Implementation of the National Program for Administrative Reform Core Strategies","RGC will further focus on implementing the three core strategies of the National Program for Administrative Reform through:",""],[1,"120","7","Coordinated Governance Reform Implementation","These 3 strategies of the Royal Government closely interlinked and will be implemented in coordination with other reforms such as the reform of public financial management and de- concentration and decentralization to strengthen good governance.",""]],"8":[[1,"12","3","Rectangular Strategy Implementation Framework","RS provides a development framework, which will be implemented through the next five-year period.",""],[1,"98","18","Inter-sectoral Results Framework for Plan Implementation","A possible Results Framework (RF) is, therefore, developed with a view to explicate the nature of the existing interdependence and the compulsions of having to work together, to obtain best results from the efforts put in, and finally identify bottlenecks that might arise in the implementation process (Box 3.1).",""],[1,"99","14","National and Sub-national Monitoring and Evaluation Improvement","Improve M&E at national and sub-national systems.",""],[1,"100","19","Strengthen Monitoring and Evaluation Systems","Strengthen M&E at all levels (national/sub-national), esp. the database",""],[1,"107","12","Planning, Monitoring and Reporting System Strengthening","Strengthen planning, monitoring and reporting systems and better link plans to budgets.",""]],"9":[[1,"87","4","Population Policy Mainstreaming and Capacity Strengthening","The National Committee for Population and Development (NCPD) and other line ministries and agencies have been working to strengthen its human resources for integrating population-related issues in the development planning processes at all levels for planners and policy makers.","The National Committee for Population and Development (NCPD) | other line ministries and agencies"],[1,"88","10","Population Data and Policy Analysis Capacity Strengthening","Capacity and resources for data collection, analysis/interpretation and policy analysis of population issues need to be strengthened at all levels.",""],[1,"207","6","Population Policy Integration into Socio-Economic Planning","RGC will continue its efforts to integrate the population policy into socio-economic policy, plans and programs at all levels.",""],[1,"207","7","Demographic Dynamics Management Strengthening","RGC during the Fifth Legislature will pay attention to further strengthening the management of the demographic dynamic, aimed at enhancing the quality of human capital.",""],[1,"208","2","National Population Policy Review and Update","Reviewing the existing National Population Policy (NPP) and updating it based on the perspectives of changing population dynamics.",""],[1,"208","3","Capacity Building for Policymakers and Planners on Population and Poverty Analysis","Enhancing the capacity of policymakers, parliamentarians, planners, and development program managers at the national and sub-national levels, to take into account data and analysis on key population and poverty issues.",""],[1,"208","4","Guidelines for Integrating Population and Living Standards Variables","Formulating guidelines for integrating population and living standards variables in the design of all development programs.",""],[1,"208","5","Capacity Building for Planning Officers on Population Integration","Strengthening capacity of planning officers at the national and sub-national levels to integrate population issues in planning processes.",""],[1,"208","7","Disaggregated Population Data Development and Dissemination","Developing and widely disseminating disaggregated population data at the national and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"208","8","Household and Population Survey Implementation","Continuing work on carrying out CSES, CDHS and CIPS in a timely manner.",""],[1,"208","10","Integrated Data Utilization and Population Variables Guidelines","Formulating guidelines on the integrated data utilization and population variables to support sustainable development programs at both national and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"208","11","Population and Reproductive Health Advocacy Materials Development","Preparing a comprehensive training manual and other advocacy materials on population, RH, gender, poverty and development linkages.",""],[1,"208","12","University Training on Population, Reproductive Health, Gender, and Development Linkages","Training on population, RH, gender, living standards, and development linkages, to students in universities.",""],[1,"208","13","Population Needs and Problems Research","Conducting research population-related needs and problems based on changing population dynamics to the RGC and other relevant institutions.",""]],"10":[[1,"99","14","Citizen Engagement and Accountability System","Raise accountability: through citizen engagement and formal accountability system",""],[1,"121","5","User Feedback and Recourse Mechanisms","Conduct research and establish user feedback and recourse mechanisms.",""],[1,"210","20","Social Accountability Measures","Promote social accountability measures.",""]],"11":[[1,"57","22","Information and Communication Technology Regulatory and Capacity Strengthening","The strategic objective of the Royal Government of the Fourth Legislature was to promote the development of a modern and high quality information and communication technology by strengthening the regulatory framework, building institutional capacity, modernizing technical equipment base, fostering competition, strengthening the efficient use",""],[1,"58","3","Postal Service Improvement Programme","Effort has been made to improve the post services: (1) reduced the duration of delivery, (2) operated Express Mail Service in the capital and provinces, (3) expanded post services to all urban areas, (4) established a management system to track and trace post.",""],[1,"58","4","Open Post Policy","The Ministry of Post and Telecommunication (MPTC) has implemented an open post policy.","Ministry of Post and Telecommunication (MPTC)"],[1,"58","14","Telecom Satellite Project","A telecom satellite project is in progress for sovereignty, national security, as well as benefits of social economy.",""],[1,"59","9","State Media Technical Renovation and Digital Modernization","Technical facilities of the state media outlets, i.e. National Radio, National TV and National News Agency, need renovations and modernization, especially a shift from analogue to digital.",""],[1,"168","12","Telecommunications and ICT Legal Framework Reform","Promoting the adoption of the Law on Telecommunication and the preparation of related laws including those on Cyber-crime and e-commerce as deemed necessary for the effective management of the information and communication technology sector.",""],[1,"168","13","Telecommunications and ICT Regulatory Reform","Stepping up the implementation and preparation of additional regulations for the telecommunication sector and information and communication technology sector.",""],[1,"168","14","Supervisory Institutions and Institutional Coordination Strengthening","Strengthening the role of supervisory institutions and enhancing institutional coordination to develop and manage this sector with transparency and efficiency.",""],[1,"170","5","Telecommunications Strategy Regulatory Amendment","Amendment the telecommunication strategy regulation based on new technical development based on international regulatory reform of International Telecommunication Union - ITU.",""],[1,"170","7","Sectoral Regulatory Preparation and Implementation Monitoring","Promote preparing regulations on each sector and monitor implementation.",""],[1,"170","9","Telecommunications Records Management Office","Prepare and operate the office to maintain relevant documents on telecommunications.",""],[1,"170","17","Regulatory Framework Strengthening","To strengthen the regulatory framework, MPTC will be continuing working on:","MPTC"],[1,"170","24","Telecommunications Law","A Law on Tele Communication.",""],[1,"170","25","Radio Communication Law","A Law on Radio Communication.",""]],"12":[[1,"168","10","Information and Telecommunications Sector Development","RGC during the Fifth Legislature will further develop the information and telecommunication technology sector as a modern, state-of-the-art and high quality service in accordance with international standards, and provide service at competitive rates, with nationwide coverage, for the public to use and benefit from the service.",""],[1,"168","11","National ICT Sector Development Policy","Preparing the national policy for the development of information and communication technology sector with due consideration of all social and economic aspects.",""],[1,"168","15","National Broadband Planning Order","Preparing and implementing the National Broadband Planning order to help promote innovation, human resource development, competition, enhancement of economic productivity as well as greater participation from the public in socio-economic development.",""],[1,"168","16","Backbone Infrastructure Expansion and Efficiency Improvement","Expanding the coverage and strengthening the efficiency of the backbone infrastructure, particularly by encouraging greater use of this infrastructure and further expanding to areas with high economic and tourism potential as well as remote areas without or with limited telecommunication services.",""],[1,"168","19","Private Sector ICT Investment Promotion","Encouraging the private sector to invest in the modern and state-of-the-art technology including broadband Internet, cloud technology and software development to enhance the quality and efficiency of information and communication technology.",""],[1,"169","1","Telecommunication Service Expansion and Fee Reduction","Ministry of Post and Telecommunications (MPTC) will expand telecommunication services and reduce fees by:","Ministry of Post and Telecommunications (MPTC)"],[1,"169","37","Telecom Optic Cable Network Infrastructure Expansion","Build and develop infrastructure backbone of the telecom optic cable network to all provinces and districts where there is economic and tourist potential, and participate to implementing the ASEAN Master Plan, 2015.",""],[1,"170","1","ASEAN-Cambodia Internet Exchange System Development","Develop ASEAN-Cambodia Internet Exchange System.",""],[1,"170","2","Broadband Policy Implementation and IPv6 Transition","Implement the Broad Band Policy for expanding services and change from Internet Protocol Version 4 to Internet Protocol Version 6.",""],[1,"170","3","Submarine Cable Optical Network Development","Prepare Submarine Cable optic network.",""],[1,"170","4","Universal Service Obligation for Rural ICT Access","Prepare to install Universal Service Obligation - USO, for service in rural area and community where ICT are not available.",""],[1,"170","21","National Broadband Policy","A National Broad Band Policy.",""],[1,"170","22","Universal Telecommunication Obligation Policy","A Universal Telecommunication Obligation Policy.",""],[1,"170","23","Telecommunication Development Policy","A Telecommunication Development Policy.",""],[1,"173","4","Modern Telecommunications Network Expansion","expand the modern telecommunication network to make services available at reasonably low rates;",""]],"13":[[1,"121","4","ICT-Enabled Public Service Delivery","Promote the use of ICT to enhance the delivery of public services.",""]],"14":[[1,"168","17","ICT Literacy and Human Resource Development Programme","Promoting human resource development to respond to the fast growing modern technologies and enhance public literacy level in information and communication technology aimed at more efficient use and deriving maximum benefit from this sector by strengthening all levels of education curricula, training of government officials and encouraging the private sector to participate in enhancing public's literacy in information and communication technology.",""],[1,"170","13","National Institute of Post, Telecommunication, Information and Communication Technology Development","Build up National Institute of Post, Telecommunication, Information, and Communication Technology.",""],[1,"170","14","E-Government Development Initiative","Developing e-government.",""],[1,"170","15","National Information Infrastructure and Government Video Conferencing Improvement","Improving and managing national information infrastructure, government video conferences.",""],[1,"170","16","Computer Programs and Content Development","Developing computer programs and contents.",""],[1,"172","14","ICT Software Capacity Strengthening","Securement of ICT-based Technology: Reinforces the software capacity in order to swift the ICT paradigm to software base from hardware base.",""]],"15":[[1,"169","2","Postal Service Quality Improvement and Network Efficiency","Improving the service quality and make post network efficient:",""],[1,"169","3","Track and Trace System Continuation","Continue the track and trace system at Counter Automation at the capital/provincials, municipalities, districts and khans.",""],[1,"169","4","International Postal System Management Expansion","Continue expanding the International Postal System Management at capital/ provinces, municipalities, districts and khans.",""],[1,"169","5","Commercial Advertising in the Media","Continue commercial advertisement in the media.",""],[1,"169","9","Postal Route Drug Trafficking Prevention Cooperation","Cooperate with authorities to prevent drug traffic through the postal route.",""],[1,"169","10","Postal System Loss and Damage Reduction","Prevent/minimize losses or damages in the postal system.",""],[1,"169","11","Postal Business Information Systems Upgrade","Manage postal business at international standards using comprehensive information systems.",""],[1,"169","12","Use of the Universal Postal Union International Financial System","Put to use International Financial System (IFS) of Universal Postal Union (UPU).",""],[1,"169","13","Mobile Scanner Deployment for Express Mail Service","Put Mobile Scanner on all Express Mail Service (EMS).",""],[1,"169","14","Business Management Information Systems","Manage business through Management Information Systems (MIS).",""],[1,"169","16","Postal Code Expansion","Expand postal code use within the country.",""],[1,"169","17","Customs Law Amendment Participation","Participate in Customs Law Amendment relevant to tax posts.",""],[1,"169","20","Postal Bank Services Cooperation with Private Banks","Put into use, postal bank services that cooperate with private banks.",""],[1,"169","21","International Financial System Deployment","Put into use International Financial System (IFS) of Universal Postal Union (UPU).",""],[1,"169","22","Business Expansion to Urban and Rural Areas","Expand business to both urban and rural areas.",""],[1,"169","23","Postal Employee Business Skills Training","Continue training postal employees in postal business skills in provinces.",""],[1,"169","27","P.O. Box Expansion and Standardization","Increase P.O. Boxes and match them with international standards.",""],[1,"169","33","Business Service Office Construction and Repair","Build and repair offices at provinces, municipalities, districts and Khans as a business service offices.",""],[1,"170","18","National Postal Policy and Strategy","A National Policy and Postal Strategy.",""],[1,"170","19","Universal Postal Obligation Sub-Decree","A sub-decree on Universal Postal Obligation.",""],[1,"170","20","Postal Law Amendment","Amending the Postal Law.",""]],"16":[[1,"18","12","Legal and Judicial Reform","These are: (ii) legal and judicial reforms;",""],[1,"19","7","Legal and Justice Reform Acceleration","the RGC of the Fourth Legislation was committed to accelerating the Legal and Justice Reform through:",""],[1,"19","8","Legal and Justice Reform Implementation","Continuing the implementation of seven strategic objectives of Legal and Justice Reform:",""],[1,"20","1","Judicial Services Strengthening","Strengthening judicial services, including judicial power and prosecutorial services.",""],[1,"20","2","Alternative Dispute Resolution Mechanism Expansion","Enlargement of alternative dispute resolution mechanisms.",""],[1,"20","3","Legal and Judicial Sector Institutional Strengthening","Strengthening of Legal and Judicial sector institutions to fulfil their mandates.",""],[1,"20","8","Legal Awareness and Training Programme","Continuing organizing programs and disseminating knowledge on laws and procedures to the people, and providing legal training to increase awareness and implementation for law enforcement officials.",""],[1,"20","9","Judges and Prosecutors Capacity Building","Strengthening the capacity building of judges and prosecutors.",""],[1,"20","13","Alternative Dispute Resolution Promotion","Continuing the promotion of alternative dispute resolution mechanisms.",""],[1,"20","24","Juvenile Justice Law Reform","Draft Law on Juvenile Justice.",""],[1,"20","26","Legal Education and Dissemination for Justice Officials","MOJ has widely disseminated fundamental Laws and Laws related to promoting the cause of protecting women and children to judges, prosecutors, court clerks, justice officers and officials, a total of 9,200 participants in both the capital and provincials.","MOJ"],[1,"21","3","Justice Sector Human Resources Training Programme","MOJ focused on improving law and court service delivery by providing 39 trainings on fundamental laws, laws related to protect women and children, and other skills to judges, prosecutors, court clerks, justice officers and officials, in both capital and provinces.","MOJ"],[1,"21","4","Model Court Working Group and Court Register Standardization","According to Legal and Judicial Reform Policy, MOJ set up a Model Court Working Group.","MOJ"],[1,"21","5","Alternative Dispute Resolution Mechanisms and Legal Services Centres","Mechanisms for alternative dispute resolution to reduce the backlog of cases at the provincial court and to expedite dispute resolution for the citizen and the poor have been implemented by the Ministry of Justice and the Ministry of Interior (MOI).","Ministry of Justice | Ministry of Interior (MOI)"],[1,"71","13","Juvenile Justice Draft Law","The draft law on juvenile justice is under process with the office of the Council of Ministers.",""],[1,"116","1","Legal and Judicial Reform","the Royal Government has firmly implemented key reform programs, including: (2) legal and judicial reform",""],[1,"116","3","Fundamental Laws Development and Adoption Priority","The development and adoption of all fundamental laws has been and will continue to be a high priority of the Royal Government.",""],[1,"117","21","National Assembly-Senate Relations Strengthening Initiative","Strengthening National Assembly-Senate Relations: MONASRI has selected: (1) 11 priority laws (Land Law, Forestry Law, Fishery Law, Environment Law, Natural Management Law, Law on Domestic Violence and Protection of Victims, Law on",""],[1,"118","1","Public Legal Awareness Dissemination Campaign","to disseminate to citizens, in both the Capital City and provinces, in the purpose of raising public awareness of the laws, their rights and obligation to maintain stability, social order, and the rule of law;",""],[1,"118","1","Draft Law Finalization and Legal Document Update","Finalizing the draft law on inspection and new legal documents as needed.",""],[1,"118","4","Legal and Judicial Reform Strategy","RGC will continue implementing the legal and judicial reform strategy to achieve its strategic objectives.",""],[1,"118","4","Public Legal Awareness and Law Enforcement Training Programme","RGC will continue organizing programs to disseminate knowledge of laws and procedures to the public and provide legal training to law-enforcement officials with the aim of improving awareness and proper enforcement of the laws.",""],[1,"118","5","Legal and Judicial Reform Action Program","RGC will continue to actively implement and deepen key reforms included in the action program for the implementation of legal and judicial reform strategy with special attention on: (1) Further promoting the adoption of key legislations concerning judiciary including the Law on the Statute of Judges and Prosecutors, the Law on Organization and Function of Courts and Prosecution, Amendment to the Law on the Organization and Function of the Supreme Council of Magistracy, as well as the development of new laws required for state governance and Cambodia's membership in the ASEAN Economic Community to be established by 2015 and the World Trade Organization; (2) Further strengthening of professional capacity and responsibility of judges and prosecutors; (3) Further promoting the establishment of court administration attached to tribunals at all levels; (4) Further equipping the tribunals with appropriate means to perform their functions; (5) Further implementing law dissemination",""],[1,"119","1","Legal Aid Support for the Poor","Further extending cooperation and support to the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia to provide legal assistance to the poor for defending their rights and interests in the court system;",""],[1,"119","1","Out-of-Court Settlement Mechanism Promotion","Further promoting the out-of-court settlement mechanisms.",""],[1,"119","3","Law and Judicial Reform Strategy Implementation","Implementing of Law and Judicial Reform Strategy to achieve seven Strategic Objectives:",""],[1,"119","8","Judicial and Prosecutorial Services Strengthening","Strengthening the judicial services, including judicial and prosecutorial services.",""],[1,"119","9","Alternative Dispute Resolution Mechanisms Promotion","Further promoting alternative dispute resolution mechanisms.",""],[1,"119","10","Legal and Judicial Sector Institutional Strengthening","Strengthening of Legal and Judicial sector institutions to fulfill their mandates.",""],[1,"119","13","Strengthening and Expanding Legal Dissemination on Women, Children, and Human Trafficking","Strengthening and enlargement dissemination law and legislations both of national and international which related to women and children and human trafficking.",""],[1,"119","16","Training on Fundamental Laws and Legal Skills for Law Enforcement and Legal Professionals","Enlargement training on fundamental laws, legislation both of national and international which related to woman and children and other skills to law enforcement officials, officials and Legal professionals.",""],[1,"119","17","Judges and Prosecutors Capacity Building Programme","Enlargement and strengthening capacity building of Judges and Prosecutors.",""],[1,"119","18","Alternative Dispute Resolution Mechanisms Expansion and Strengthening","Enlargement and strengthening Alternative dispute resolution mechanisms.",""],[1,"119","19","Court Register Expansion and Strengthening Project","Enlargement and strengthening court register (Project of model court).",""],[1,"119","20","Court Register Information System","Introducing court register data by information system.",""],[1,"119","21","Judicial Information Access Enhancement","Enhancing access to judicial information, including on court decisions and proceedings, periodic administrative reports and administrative information regarding pending cases, including status and scheduling information.",""],[1,"119","23","Alternatives to Detention for Children","Promoting and strengthening the use of alternatives to detention measures, especially for children.",""],[1,"119","24","Legal Aid Services for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","Strengthening legal aid services for the poor and the vulnerable, especially for children.",""],[1,"119","27","Judicial Decision Quality Improvement","Enhancing the quality of judicial decisions, including on pre-trial detention.",""],[1,"119","31","Judicial Infrastructure Expansion and Improvement","Enlargement and improving infrastructure in MOJ and municipal and provincial courts.",""],[1,"120","1","Expansion of Municipal and Provincial Court Infrastructure","Increasing Justice Services by enlargement municipal and provincial court infrastructures including regional appeal court, special court of first instance, and special chamber of higher court and creating all municipal and provincial court in Kingdom of Cambodia.",""],[1,"124","3","Right to Obtain Justice Project","MOI will continue implementing the Right to Obtain Justice Project between the MOI and Ministry of Justice (MOJ).","MOI | Ministry of Justice (MOJ)"]],"17":[[1,"76","2","Education Sector-Wide Approach Implementation","The Ministry of Education Youth and Sports (MOEYS) had prepared and implemented a sector-wide approach, reflected in the Education Strategic Plan of 2009-2013.","Ministry of Education Youth and Sports (MOEYS)"],[1,"76","4","Equitable School Access and Teacher Deployment Programme","Ensure equitable access to education by building more schools closer to people's homes, building dormitories (especially for girls), providing operational budgets, and appointing sufficient numbers of qualified teachers.",""],[1,"76","5","Education Quality and Efficiency Improvement Programme","Improve the quality and efficiency of education by increasing the supply of learning materials, library materials and laboratories, continually reforming the curricula, increasing study hours, and providing more scholarships to the poorer students.",""],[1,"76","6","Institutional Capacity Development for Officials and Education Providers","Institutionally develop and build knowledge and skills of officials by providing a strong legal, regulatory and policy structure supported by a capacity development of education providers at all levels.",""],[1,"76","8","Education Quality and Relevance Improvement Programme","The government's focus is on improving the quality and effectiveness of education through promoting early grade reading skills, developing basic life-skills training programs, allowing students to select subjects of their choice, improving the relevance of the curriculum and textbooks, designing evaluation standards for student achievement, and improving the supply of learning materials and textbooks.",""],[1,"77","4","Early Childhood Education Expansion Programme","Improving access to early childhood education programs for the age-group 0-5 years, building the capacity of pre-school teachers through better pre- and in-service training, and increasing the awareness of parents and communities about the value of early childhood education.",""],[1,"77","5","Home-Based Care and Community Resource Centre Expansion","Increase access to home-based care and Community Resource Centres along with training programs for mothers and community teachers.",""],[1,"77","5","Training Programme for Mothers and Community Teachers","Increase access to home-based care and Community Resource Centres along with training programs for mothers and community teachers.",""],[1,"77","7","Bilingual Education Expansion","Expand bilingual education, scholarships and school meals programs, and accelerated learning and re-entry programs, through non-formal education and integration of disabled children into formal schooling.",""],[1,"77","7","Scholarships and School Meals Programme","Expand bilingual education, scholarships and school meals programs, and accelerated learning and re-entry programs, through non-formal education and integration of disabled children into formal schooling.",""],[1,"77","7","Accelerated Learning and Re-entry Programme","Expand bilingual education, scholarships and school meals programs, and accelerated learning and re-entry programs, through non-formal education and integration of disabled children into formal schooling.",""],[1,"77","7","Non-formal Education Expansion","Expand bilingual education, scholarships and school meals programs, and accelerated learning and re-entry programs, through non-formal education and integration of disabled children into formal schooling.",""],[1,"77","7","Inclusive Schooling for Disabled Children","Expand bilingual education, scholarships and school meals programs, and accelerated learning and re-entry programs, through non-formal education and integration of disabled children into formal schooling.",""],[1,"77","9","Secondary Education Expansion and Scholarship Support","Expand secondary education, a focus on reducing gender gap and ensuring completion of lower-secondary education; increase the number of scholarships for students from poorer families (especially girls); expand the number of lower-secondary schools through upgrading some primary schools.",""],[1,"77","11","Targeted Programs to Reduce Out-of-School Children","Measures to reduce the number children out of school with a specific focus on children from indigenous communities, children with disabilities, and children from poorer families, through targeted programs.",""],[1,"77","13","National Student Assessment and Curriculum Quality Framework","Initiate a national framework to ensure quality mechanisms that can assess student achievement; strengthen regular classroom testing; initiate student assessment in Grade 3and gradually expand it to Grades 6 and 8;and enhance the quality and relevance of learning through curriculum and textbook review.",""],[1,"77","15","Higher Education Vision Document for STEAM Priority Programs","Prepare a vision document for higher education with focus on priority programs [science, technology, engineering, arts and mathematics (STEAM)] to the level of ASEAN quality-assurance standards.",""],[1,"77","17","Textbook Distribution and Supply Improvement","Review and improve the distribution and management of textbooks; and ensure a supply of new textbooks, curriculum and teacher-guides in remote areas.",""],[1,"77","19","Deployment of Qualified Teachers to New Secondary Schools","Deploy qualified teachers at the newly established upper- and lower- secondary schools, especially in remote areas.",""],[1,"78","1","In-Service Teacher Training and Performance Appraisal System","teachers in mathematics and science through in-service training, and initiate a staff performance appraisal system.",""],[1,"78","3","School Leadership and Education Office Capacity-Building Programme","Training to develop the capacity of school principals and officials at the Provincial Office of Education and the District Office of Education; strengthen the capacity of District Training and Monitoring Teams for supporting and advising schools.",""],[1,"78","5","Technical Education and Science Enrollment Expansion","Increase the enrolment on technical education, technology and science, and being ready to participate for regional integration in 2015 and respond to labour market needs and increasing job opportunities.",""],[1,"78","7","School Physical Education and Sports Promotion","Promote physical education and sport activities in schools and promote the activities of sports associations, sports clubs and the sports physical infrastructure.",""],[1,"185","3","Education for All Policy Implementation and Education Quality Improvement","During the Fifth Legislature RGC will further promote implementing of 'Education for All' policy, further promoting improvement in the quality and effectiveness of education services, and further developing the capacity of educational institutions and staff.",""],[1,"185","4","Education Policy and Strategy Update","Further improving education policies and strategies, especially updating the Education Strategic Plan, Master Plan on ITC in Education and Policy on Research Development in Education, with the objective to build and develop a high quality, and capable human resource with high standards of work ethics in all areas, and to proactively meet the need of socio-economic development and strengthen Cambodia's competitiveness within the regional and global frameworks based on pro-active approach.",""],[1,"185","5","Mainstream Scientific and Technological Knowledge in Curricula","mainstreaming scientific and technological knowledge and its applications in academic curriculums at all levels especially in high school, vocational and technical training and higher education",""],[1,"185","6","Education Access Expansion and School Construction Programme","Increasing equitable access to education through further promoting the construction of elementary schools to reach remote villages, locating at least one secondary school in each commune subject to geographic conditions, and at least one university or its branch in each province subject to capacity constraints and specific circumstances in deploying teachers to all those establishments.",""],[1,"185","7","Institutional Development and Capacity Building for Education Administration","Continuing institutional development and capacity building through the development of legal framework and strengthened implementation of laws and regulations, organizational structure and skills training for education officials.",""],[1,"185","8","Educational Quality and Effectiveness Improvement Programme","Increasing quality and effectiveness of educational services at all academic levels in particular, technical and skill training for both public and private institutions in accordance with international standards; meeting domestic development needs through: training and re-training of teachers, improvement in curriculums, strengthened inspection and management capacity, improved teacher motivation to increase their teaching capacity, better quality of examinations at all academic levels, encouraging",""],[1,"186","7","Education Strategic Plan Implementation","the Royal Government will continue to implement the Education Strategic Plan (ESP), putting emphasis on ensuring that all Cambodian children and youth have equal opportunity for access to basic education, both formal and informal, without discrimination.",""],[1,"186","8","Education Sector Plan 2014-2018","Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports (MOEYS) has responded to the outcomes expected in the NSDP 2014-2018 by preparing the ESP 2014-2018, aiming at providing quality education to more children in all levels.","Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports (MOEYS)"],[1,"186","8","Sub-sector Education Planning Framework","MOEYS has prepared a sub-sector plan based ESP (Early Childhood Education (ECE), primary, secondary, higher, non-formal, youth and sports) that will allow for a focus on the access, relevance and quality needs at each level of a child's learning.","Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports (MOEYS)"],[1,"186","8","Education Quality Assurance Framework","There is strong focus on building a quality assurance framework and providing more opportunity to build relevant skills.",""],[1,"187","1","Expansion of School Infrastructure and Teacher Provision","MOEYS needs to build more schools and provision of adequate teachers.","MOEYS"],[1,"187","2","Universal Kindergarten Completion for Grade 1 Entry","Ensure that all children entering grade 1 have completed kindergarten.",""],[1,"187","3","Equitable Access Expansion for Children and Youth","Increase the number of children and youth that have access to all education levels with a focused attention on equity and access for the most disadvantaged areas and groups of children.",""],[1,"187","4","Expanded Access to 12-Year Education and Post-Secondary Pathways","Increase opportunities for children to finish 12 years education with a good knowledge and reasoning and logic skills, who can further build on these skills (and knowledge) through technical training, higher education and other means.",""],[1,"187","6","Curriculum Reform for General and Technical Education","Undertake a curriculum reform of the general and technical education in line with the international best practices.",""],[1,"187","7","Teacher Training Curriculum Revision and In-Service Teacher Training","Revise the teacher training curriculum in line with the revised curriculum and undertake in-service teachers training.",""],[1,"187","8","Instructional Hours Implementation and Learning Materials Provision","Ensure effective implementation of instructional-hours with adequate provision of qualified and trained teachers at all levels as well as textbooks and learning materials.",""],[1,"187","9","National Student Learning Assessment System","Systematically monitor the student learning achievements by conducting national assessments at grades 3, 6 and 8 and prepare for participation in the regional and international assessment programs.",""],[1,"187","10","Effective Leadership and Management of Education Staff","Policy 3: Ensuring effective leadership and management of education staff: Educational services are provided effectively and flexibly.",""],[1,"187","12","Early Childhood Care and Education Expansion Program","Early childhood care and education (ECCE) expansion program as the foundation for providing the next generation of healthy, skilled and knowledgeable citizens able to contribute to the social and economic development.",""],[1,"187","13","School Establishment and Development Program","School establishment and development program, assuring all children access primary learning and significantly increasing access to secondary education - school construction with water, sanitation and health facilities, and in particular a substantial increase in the number of (complete) lower secondary schools, by upgrading and expanding the existing primary schools; pre-service and in-service teacher training; textbooks and library packages provision; school principal training; laboratory for science, computers and foreign languages; workshops for apprentice learning.",""],[1,"187","14","School Quality Assurance and Quality Framework Programme","School quality system and quality assurance program for preschool, primary and secondary schools.",""],[1,"187","15","Student Assessment Systems Strengthening Program","National and international student assessment systems strengthening program - strengthening regular classroom tests and national assessment tests; reforming national examinations; and preparing to participate in Program for International Student Assessment (PISA).",""],[1,"188","1","Scholarship Program for Primary and Secondary Education","Scholarship program -Expanding primary and secondary education and targeting, monitoring and evaluating the program",""],[1,"188","3","Teacher Performance Management and Appraisal Program","Teacher performance management and appraisal program for quality teaching - Assessment, appraisal, promotion and professional development.",""],[1,"188","5","Results-Based Management Program","Results-based management program - Develop, build capacity, and change the culture of work for it to be outcome-based; and budget and monitor the system at national and sub national levels.",""],[1,"188","6","Education Financial Management Reform and Financing Program","Education financial management reform and financing program - Build capacity for budget formulation and execution, strengthen audit and procurement performance; decentralize budgets in schools; and improve financial management.",""],[1,"188","7","Literacy and Lifelong Learning Program","Literacy and Lifelong learning program- MOEYS's innovative non-formal education equivalency programs, and defined mechanisms for literacy and lifelong learning, will continue to be offered and developed.","MOEYS"],[1,"188","8","Cross-Sector and Sector Coordination Program","Cross-sector and sector coordination program - Establish cohesive and coherent operating mechanisms for all sub-sectors.",""],[1,"188","10","Home-Based Care and Community Resource Center Expansion","Increase the access to home-based care and Community Resource Centers along with training programs for mothers and community teachers.",""],[1,"188","11","Secondary Education Expansion and Scholarship Support","Expand secondary education, a focus on reducing gender-gap, and ensuring completion of lower secondary education; increase the number of scholarships for students from poor families, especially girls; and expand the number of lower secondary schools through upgrading existing primary schools.",""],[1,"188","12","Out-of-School Children Reduction Measures","Measures to reduce the number children out of school with focus on indigenous children, children with disabilities, and children from poor families.",""],[1,"188","13","National Student Assessment Framework","Initiate developing a national framework to put in place mechanisms to assess student achievement.",""],[1,"188","13","Regular Classroom Testing and Grade 3 Student Assessment","Strengthen regular classroom testing and initiate student assessment in Grade 3, with a view to expanding to Grades 6 and 8.",""],[1,"188","13","Curriculum and Textbook Review for Learning Quality","Improve the quality and relevance of learning through reviewing curricula and textbooks.",""],[1,"188","15","Textbook Distribution and Supply Improvement","Improve the coverage of the distribution of textbooks; and ensure supply of new textbooks, curriculum and teacher guides in remote/rural areas.",""],[1,"188","16","Teacher Deployment to New Secondary Schools","Deploy teachers at the newly established upper and lower secondary schools, especially in remote/rural areas.",""],[1,"189","1","In-Service Teacher Training and Staff Performance Appraisal System","mathematics and science through in-service training, and initiate a staff performance appraisal system.",""],[1,"189","3","Decentralization and Devolution Reform for Education Service Delivery","Implement D&D reforms to enhance effectiveness of the provision of educational services to beneficiaries at the sub-national level by transferring the identified functions to the respective bodies and engaging them in planning, management, implementation and monitoring.",""],[1,"189","4","School Leadership and Education Administration Capacity Building","Train to develop the capacity of the school principal, officials at the Provincial Office of Education, and the District Office of Education.",""],[1,"189","4","District Training and Monitoring Team Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity of District Training and Monitoring Teams for supporting and advising schools.",""],[1,"189","5","Non-Formal Education and Equivalency Programmes","Develop and implement innovative non-formal education programmes including equivalency to target out of school youth and adults to acquire literacy and technical skills to contribute to social, cultural and economic development.",""]],"18":[[1,"100","13","Expansion of Secondary Schools, Higher Education, and TVE","8. Expand secondary schools, higher education, TVE.",""],[1,"100","14","Target Group Skills Formation Programs","Initiate target group programs for skill formation.",""],[1,"100","15","Technology Import and Indigenization Initiative","Import and indigenize technologies.",""],[1,"100","16","Technical University Establishment","Open a technical university.",""],[1,"128","11","Investment in Quality Education and Technical and Vocational Training","Increase investments to promote quality education, especially technical and vocational training, to accelerate job creation and industry.",""],[1,"154","4","Basic Vocational Training Centers Expansion","Establish basic vocational training centers in all provinces.",""],[1,"180","5","Human Resources and Skills Development Programme","Further developing human resources, focusing on the technical capacity to respond to the needs of socio-economic development, especially through promotion of skills and professional training and retraining including apprenticeships, while encouraging private sector participation to promote higher productivity and incomes for both workers and employers.",""],[1,"180","6","Education and TVET Framework and Standards Streamlining","Streamlining the education and technical and vocational training sectors especially in developing their frameworks and standards to facilitate student transfers from technical and vocational training to higher education.",""],[1,"181","7","Labor Institute Establishment","Establish an institute on labor for providing training to officials and students, conducting research studies, and analyzing the conditions of labor, remuneration and skills.",""],[1,"182","1","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Expansion and Equity Initiative","Enhance and expand the service of technical and vocational education and training with equity:",""],[1,"182","2","TVET Expansion Programme","Expand the system of technical and vocational education and training (TVET) to ensure TVET training reaches all people in capitals and provinces.",""],[1,"182","3","Skill Training Programs via the Special Foundation","Continue holding skill-training programs via the special foundation of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, to further stage 3.",""],[1,"182","4","Training Quality Improvement for Certificate and Diploma Courses","Improve the quality of training at both certificate and diploma courses.",""],[1,"182","5","Education Curriculum Quality Improvement","Improve the quality of the education curriculum at all levels to ensure that Cambodian workers have the ability to compete with those from other ASEAN countries.",""],[1,"182","6","Curriculum Inclusion of Entrepreneurship and English Communication","Include entrepreneurship and communication (English) into the study curriculum.",""],[1,"182","7","Cambodian Qualification Framework Finalization and Royal Decree Preparation","Finalize the draft of the Cambodian Qualification Framework and prepare a Royal Decree on the introduction of this framework.",""],[1,"182","8","Qualification Framework Alignment","Ensure consistency between the Cambodian Qualification Framework and the ASEAN qualification framework.",""],[1,"182","9","Local and ASEAN Skills Competitions","Organize local skill competitions and participate in ASEAN skills competitions.",""],[1,"182","10","National Capacity Standards for Competition Development","Continue developing national capacity standards for competition, particularly in the sectors of construction, mechanics, business services, and ICT.",""],[1,"182","11","Recognition Criteria Reform for TVET Study Curricula","Improve the criteria for recognizing the study curricula in the technical and vocational education and training institutions.",""],[1,"182","13","TVET Information Systems Development and Maintenance","Develop and maintain information systems related to technical and vocational education and training.",""],[1,"182","14","Multilateral Skills Management Coordination","Promote multilateral approaches in the management of skills via the active participation of the RGC, private sector, and trade unions.",""],[1,"182","15","Priority Skills Development for Vulnerable Groups","Provide priority to women, disabled persons, vulnerable persons and school dropouts to improve their skills.",""],[1,"182","16","Dormitory Construction in TVET Institutions","Build dormitory buildings in various technical and vocational education and training establishments in capital and provinces.",""],[1,"182","17","Public-Private Partnership for TVET Quality Improvement","Strengthen partnership between the state and the private sector to enhance the quality of technical and vocational education and training.",""],[1,"182","19","Public-Private Partnerships for TVET Curriculum Alignment","Promote public-private partnerships to ensure that the curriculum of TVET responds to the market demand.",""],[1,"182","20","Skills Gap Research Study","Conduct research study on the skill gaps: what is provided versus what is required.",""],[1,"182","21","Maintenance of IT-Based TVET Management Information System and Labor Market Information System","Maintain IT-based TVET-MIS, and Labor Market Information System (LMIS).",""],[1,"186","3","National Education and Technical and Vocational Training Policy","Promoting the formulation and implementation of a national policy on education and technical and vocational training aimed at enhancing worker productivity, addressing and reducing youth unemployment, increasing people's income and ensuring equity.",""],[1,"186","4","Education and TVET Quality Strengthening Reform","Further strengthening the quality of education and technical and vocational training, and the development of technical and soft skills for youth, especially team work, discipline and professional ethics at workplaces through: the reform of training curricula and programs, strengthening national qualification standards framework, establishment of national competency standards, and monitoring and testing of competency, skill recognition, development and contest",""],[1,"188","2","National Qualifications Framework Implementation for TVET Quality Improvement","Technical and Vocational Education program - Implementing the national qualifications framework to improve quality of technical and vocational education and institutionalizing coordination among and between different stakeholders.",""]],"19":[[1,"185","5","Research and Development Promotion Programme","promoting R&D including the introduction of a research network model linking universities, public institutions and industry",""],[1,"188","4","Higher Education Development Program","Higher education development program - Undertake systematic reforms of the higher education system to bring higher education into line with regional and international standards; improve the quality of the system by requiring all higher education institutions to meet agreed minimum standards monitored by Accreditation Committee of Cambodia (ACC); significant focus on teaching and research in science, technology, engineering, arts and mathematics (STEAM) subjects; review and guidelines for fee control; substantial increase in merit-based scholarships in subjects reflecting labor market demands; and a student loan scheme.",""],[1,"188","14","Higher Education Vision and Quality Assurance Strengthening","Prepare a 'Vision' on higher education and focus on priority programs (science, technology, engineering, arts and mathematics - STEAM); link to the ASEAN quality assurance standards; and strengthen the Accreditation Committee of Cambodia (ACC) mechanism.",""]],"20":[[1,"190","6","Health Sector Strategic Plan Implementation and Updating","RGC during the Fifth Legislature will continue implementing and updating Health Sector Strategic Plan 2008-2015 to promote sustainable development of the health sector, aimed at improved sanitation, health, nutrition and well-being of the Cambodian people particularly the poor and the vulnerable (including women and children).",""],[1,"190","7","Health Sector Policy and Governance Strengthening","Developing and improving health sector policies and strategies; strengthening and improving regulatory framework especially for private health services; promoting good governance and strengthening health institutions at all levels; enhancing awareness among physicians, health workers, and health staff and service users about patient rights; promoting private sector partnerships in delivering health services; and encouraging community participation in health sector development.",""],[1,"190","8","Health Sector IT Infrastructure and Database System Development","Further developing supporting infrastructure in health sector through IT application and extension in order to strengthen the health sector database system.",""],[1,"190","9","Expansion of Health Infrastructure and Outreach Services","Further increasing access to health services through expanded coverage and outreach of public health service by bringing them closer to the public through further expansion of health infrastructure including construction of referral hospitals, health centers and health posts according to geographic and demographic conditions, and providing them with facilities, equipment, medicines and medical staff with appropriate skills.",""],[1,"190","11","Health Workforce Training and Rural Deployment Programme","Further enhancing the quality of health services through strengthening clinical techniques and management capacity of physicians, medical staff and health officials, by focusing on: (1) Improved quality of basic, advanced and specialized training; (2) Strengthened enforcement of professional ethics; and (3) Deployment of more physicians, pharmacists, dentists, mid-wives, nurses and medical assistants to all public health centers especially in rural areas, while giving priority to admitting students from the rural areas to undertake studies in national and regional health education institutions including the provision of adequate incentives and accommodation when deployed in rural areas.",""],[1,"190","12","Hygiene Awareness and Sanitation Improvement Initiative","Further enhancing awareness about hygiene and improving sanitary conditions among population aimed at maintaining good health and reducing prevalence and spread of diseases.",""],[1,"192","5","Health Facility Service Delivery Improvement","Increase delivery in health facilities assisted by trained health personnel.",""],[1,"192","16","Monitoring and Supportive Supervision for Health and Nutrition Services","Strengthen monitoring and supportive supervision for sexual, reproductive, maternal, newborn, infant, child health and nutrition services.",""],[1,"192","17","Midwife Deployment in Health Centers","Deploy midwives in all health centers.",""],[1,"194","10","Early Detection and Primary Prevention for Acute Event Management","Promote early detection, provide primary prevention, and manage acute events (including palliative treatment, care and rehabilitation services).",""],[1,"194","22","Public Health Risk Awareness Campaign","Increase awareness of risk factors of non-communicable and chronic diseases and, and other public health problems amongst general population.",""],[1,"194","24","Public Health Intervention Resource Expansion","Increase resources for non-communicable/chronic diseases and other public health interventions, including road accident, environmental health, disaster preparedness and management.",""],[1,"195","2","Coordination Mechanisms for Public Health Interventions","Establish networks and mechanisms to coordinate non-communicable and other public health interventions at national and sub-national level.",""],[1,"195","4","Expansion of Ophthalmology Services","Expand coverage of ophthalmology services, including prevention, treatment and care at the public health facility (including blindness).",""],[1,"195","10","Training for Health Center Management Committees and Village Health Support Groups","Provide training to Health Center Management Committees and Village Health Support Groups.",""],[1,"195","11","Health Services Expansion and Quality Improvement","Expand coverage and improve the quality of health services, including development of health infrastructures, effective and efficient procurement and supply management (including CMS date information system) and provision of medical equipment.",""],[1,"195","14","Health Information Systems Strengthening","Ensure availability, timely and high quality health and health related information for evidence-based policy formulation, decision-making, program implementation, performance monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"195","15","Governance and Health Regulation Strengthening","Strengthen good governance, leadership, management and accountability mechanism in the context of decentralization and de-concentration, and develop and enforce laws and health regulations for both public and private sector.",""],[1,"195","16","Regular Health Coverage Plan Update","Update the health coverage plan (determining number and location of Operational District, Referral Hospital, Health Center and Health Post) regularly in the context of decentralization and de-concentration by taking economy of scale into account.",""],[1,"195","17","Expansion of Public Service Delivery Mechanisms","Expand public service delivery mechanisms such as Special Operating Agency, and Public Administrative Enterprises.",""],[1,"195","18","Medical Supplies and Equipment Provision for Health Facilities","Ensure that sufficient medical supplies, basic equipment, and means of transportation are in place according to Minimum Package of Activity and Complementary Package of Activity Guidelines.",""],[1,"195","19","High-Tech Medical Equipment and Technology Investment","Increase investment in high-tech medical equipment and medical technology.",""],[1,"196","1","Paramedical Services Capacity Strengthening","Improve organization, management and technical capacity of paramedical services including laboratory and blood service facilities.",""],[1,"196","2","Health Sector Quality Accreditation System","Develop quality accreditation system and apply consistent standards of quality across entire health sector (public, private and non-profit).",""],[1,"196","3","Health Facility Infection Control and Medical Waste Management","Implement infection control measures, and improve medical waste management practice at health facility.",""],[1,"196","4","Health Facility Quality Incentive Scheme","Establish incentive for leveraging quality, such as bonuses and recognition/awards for health facility.",""],[1,"196","5","Physical Asset Management System Improvement","Improve physical asset management systems, including maintenance of medical equipment, buildings, means of transportation and Information Communication Technology equipment.",""],[1,"196","6","Health Infrastructure Improvement Programme","Improve physical health infrastructures, including building Health Center, Health Post, maternity waiting room, and hospital buildings, and drainage system, electricity and improved water sources at health facility, especially in remote areas.",""],[1,"196","7","Health Budget Expansion and Resource Mobilization","Increase national budget for health and mobilize funds from other sources.",""],[1,"196","8","Development Partner Funding Alignment and Coordination for Health Priorities","Align development partners funding to support the national health priority interventions, and strengthen coordination of development partner assistances.",""],[1,"196","9","Budget Execution and Public Financial Management Reform","Improve budget execution and strengthen public financial management, including public procurement.",""],[1,"196","15","Pre-service Clinical Skills Training","Invest in better clinical skills through pre-service training with more focus on clinical and public health practices.",""],[1,"196","16","Continuing Education and Management Training Programme","Develop continuing education, including management training.",""],[1,"196","17","Health Training Institution Accreditation System","Development and implement accreditation systems for public and private health training institutions.",""],[1,"196","18","Health Workforce Professional Accreditation and Registration System","Implement professional accreditation and registration system for health workforce in public and private sectors.",""],[1,"196","19","Health Sector Human Resource Planning Alignment","Align human resource planning and personnel management with health sector planning and the Health Coverage Plan.",""],[1,"196","21","Health Data Governance Strengthening","Strengthen existing legislation, regulations and procedures related to health data, recording, reporting, storage, retrieval, and dissemination.",""],[1,"196","22","Health Information System Supervision and Feedback Improvement","Improve Health Information System supervision and feedback, focused on data quality and performance standard adherence.",""],[1,"197","1","Patient Record Management System Strengthening","Strengthen patient record management system, including expansion of Patient Medical Registration, storage and retrieval systems, application of International Classification of Diseases (ICD 10).",""],[1,"197","2","Private Health Facility Participation in the Health Information System","Expand participation in Health Information System by private health facilities.",""],[1,"197","4","Health System Research Agenda Development and Updating","Develop and update agenda for health system research.",""],[1,"197","5","Civil Registration and Vital Statistics System Strengthening","Support strengthening of civil registration and vital statistics system that record vital events such as births, deaths and causes of death.",""],[1,"197","6","Private Sector Licensing and Accreditation Reform","Strengthen law and institutional regulatory mechanisms for licensing the private sector, followed by implementation of an accreditation system, as a step-up after compliance to licensing requirements.",""],[1,"197","7","Regular Update of Medium- to Long-Term Planning Instruments","Develop and update medium to long term plans on regular basis, including the Health Strategic Plan, Budget Strategic Plan, Public Investment Program, Annual Operational Plan, etc.",""],[1,"197","8","Health Commodity Logistics and Supply System Strengthening","Strengthen logistic and supply systems to ensure availability of and timely delivery of drugs and health commodities at health facility.",""],[1,"197","9","Public-Private Partnership in Health Promotion","Promote public and private partnership in health.",""],[1,"197","10","Pharmaceutical Product Registration System Strengthening","Strengthen registration systems for pharmaceutical products: modern and traditional medicines, medical devices, medical equipment, and cosmetics.",""],[1,"197","11","Ministry of Health Stewardship Capacity Strengthening","Enhance MOH's stewardship capacities (oversight, regulatory functions, legislation and policy development), and strengthen organizational structures and health service delivery in the context of D&D.","MOH"],[1,"197","12","Strengthen Health Center Management Committees and Village Health Support Groups","Enhance local governance and community monitoring of health services efficiency through strengthening Health Center Management Committees and Village Health Support Groups, and promoting community awareness on client's rights and provider's rights/duties.",""],[1,"197","12","Community Awareness on Health Service Rights and Duties","Enhance local governance and community monitoring of health services efficiency through strengthening Health Center Management Committees and Village Health Support Groups, and promoting community awareness on client's rights and provider's rights/duties.",""],[1,"197","13","Ministry of Health Planning and Monitoring Framework","The key planning tools for carrying out the above functions are MOH's Three-Year Rolling Plan linked to the Budget Strategic Framework and Public Investment Program, and MOH's Annual Operational Plan and program-based budget.","MOH"],[1,"197","13","Health Sector Progress Review and Evaluation System","MOH will prepare annual progress reviews, a mid-term review followed by end-cycle evaluation to report on the impact of the HSP2 in improving the health status of the targeted populations.","MOH"]],"21":[[1,"82","4","International Health Regulations Implementation Strengthening","Cambodia has been continuing to strengthen the implementation of International Health Regulations 2005, aimed at preventing and controlling communicable diseases outbreak.",""],[1,"82","4","National Emerging Disease Surveillance System Strengthening","The surveillance systems for Avian Influenza and other emerging diseases have been strengthened nationwide and at the international entry gates.",""]],"22":[[1,"80","16","Supplementary Nutrition and Child Health Services","These include, provision of micronutrient to children, pregnant and post-delivery women; child deworming; counselling for breast feeding and young infant feeding; training of community trainers; and providing services for managing severe and acute malnutrition.",""],[1,"81","2","Boosted Continuum of Prevention, Care and Treatment","Cambodia is now implementing the 'Boosted' Continuum of Prevention Care and Treatment to address the need of Most-at-Risk Populations (MARPs)",""],[1,"81","2","Boosted Linked Response for Mother-to-Child HIV Transmission Reduction","and the Boosted Linked Response to reduce mother to child transmission.",""],[1,"81","3","Police Community Partnership Initiative","the Police Community Partnership Initiative (PCPI) that will support effective HIV interventions for MARPs especially in 32 hot spots ODs.","National AIDS Authority | MOI"],[1,"81","4","MOEYS Strategic Plan for HIV Response","MOEYS has been trying to mobilise resources to implement the MOEYS Strategic Plan for HIV and Response 2012-2013 to address mainly in-and out-of-school youth","MOEYS"],[1,"81","4","Workplace HIV Prevention Promotion","MOLVT continues to promote HIV in the workplaces with greater involvement of employers and employee as part of HIV sensitive approach","MOLVT"],[1,"84","4","Participation in National Nutrition Coordination Bodies","MOH has participated in entities such as, the National Council for Nutrition (based at the Ministry of Planning), and the Technical Working Group on Food Security and Nutrition.","MOH | Ministry of Planning"],[1,"88","3","Population Health Investment Program","Cambodia has made great strides in reducing poverty through implementing its National Strategic Development Plan with focus on investments in population programs: in particular, on reproductive, maternal and child health (including family planning), and adhering to reproductive rights that promote choice.",""],[1,"191","1","Reproductive, Maternal, Infant and Child Health Service Improvement","Further improving reproductive, maternal and infant/children health including their nutrition status through enhancing quality and effectiveness of reproductive, maternal, infant and children healthcare services by focusing on: expanded coverage of child delivery by professional mid-wives and physicians, maternal emergency and newborn baby care services, and consultation services on birth spacing options; increased coverage of children's vaccination especially vaccinations against measles and tetanus; provision of mineral supplements and proteins to infants during the initial 1,000 days after birth and special care services for those with severe malnutrition; and provision of reproductive education and healthcare services to the youth.",""],[1,"191","4","Public Health Partnership Strengthening","Further strengthening cooperation with development partners and other concerned stakeholders aimed at enhancing public health services, particularly for important health programs such as reproductive healthcare and women and children nutrition programs.",""],[1,"191","12","Sexual and Reproductive Health Services Expansion","Increase accessibility and coverage of sexual and reproductive health services for all including young women, men and adolescents.",""],[1,"191","13","Maternal and Newborn Health Services Improvement","Improve quality, accessibility and coverage of antenatal care, delivery, postnatal care, baby care and emergency obstetric and neonatal services, and prevention of HIV transmission from mother to child.",""],[1,"191","14","Immunization and Integrated Childhood Illness Services Improvement","Improve quality, accessibility and coverage of immunization and integrated management of childhood illness (pneumonia and diarrhea diseases).",""],[1,"191","15","Nutrition Services Quality and Coverage Improvement","Improve quality, assess and coverage of nutrition services to reduce insufficiency of protein-energy and micronutrient among women and infants.",""],[1,"192","2","Sexual and Reproductive Health Services Expansion","Increase demand for and access to sexual reproductive health services, information, counseling and services including contraception, safe abortion and comprehensive abortion care, adolescent-friendly services and victims of gender based violence.",""],[1,"192","3","Reproductive Health Commodity Security System","Ensure reproductive health commodity security system.",""],[1,"192","6","Maternal Emergency Obstetric and Newborn Care Expansion","Improve maternal care through increased number of Basic and Comprehensive Emergency Obstetric and Newborn Care units staffed by skilled birth attendants and supported by an operational referral system.",""],[1,"192","7","Antenatal and Postnatal Care Package Promotion","Promote use of antenatal and postnatal care packages, including nutrition counseling and promotion and distribution of iron folic acid.",""],[1,"192","8","Maternal and Neonatal Death Surveillance System Strengthening","Strengthen maternal and neonatal death surveillance system.",""],[1,"192","11","Routine Immunization Coverage and New Vaccine Introduction","Maintain high coverage of routine vaccine immunization and introduce new vaccines for target populations, especially children< one year-old.",""],[1,"192","12","Cold Chain Management and Vaccine Supply System Strengthening","Strengthen cold chain management and vaccine supply system.",""],[1,"192","13","Integrated Management of Childhood Illness and HIV/AIDS and STI Protocol Implementation","Implement the Integrated Management of Childhood Illness and HIV/AIDS and Sexually Transmitted Infection protocols for children under 5 years.",""],[1,"192","15","Sexual and Maternal and Child Health Service Improvement","Improve the quality of services and information on sexual, reproductive, maternal, newborn, infant and child health.",""]],"23":[[1,"82","7","Food Safety Training and Supervision Programme","Food safety is being promoted through the following main activities: training of trainers in food safety, educating restaurant/cafeteria owner and managers and food processing factory owners, managers and cooks, about food hygiene.",""],[1,"82","7","Regular Food Seller and Restaurant Supervision","Supervision to food sellers and restaurants in Phnom Penh and provinces is conducted regularly.",""],[1,"84","9","Private Sector Regulatory Strengthening Mechanism","Regulatory mechanism for the private sector needs to be further strengthened.",""]],"24":[[1,"203","3","Health Equity Fund Expansion","expanded coverage of the equity fund",""],[1,"203","3","Community Health Insurance Provision","provision of health insurance to local communities",""],[1,"203","3","Voluntary Health Insurance for Informal Workers","extending voluntary health insurance schemes targeting those in the informal economy",""],[1,"204","3","Health Equity Fund Scale-Up","Scaling up health equity funds as a means to improve health protection for the poor.",""]],"25":[[1,"192","25","Expansion of Quality HIV Testing Services","Expand quality HIV testing services (including counseling) to all health facilities, using HIV finger-prick test; ensure availability of HIV test kits.",""],[1,"192","26","Expansion of Facility-Based ART Services","Increase coverage of facility-based ART services, and ensure availability of Anti- Retroviral drugs and other consumables.",""],[1,"193","1","HIV Testing and Antiretroviral Treatment Funding Expansion","Increase the national budget and development partners' funding for provision of HIV testing and Anti-Retroviral Treatment services.",""],[1,"193","2","HIV Counseling, Testing, and ART Network Training","Provide training/refresher-training on HIV counseling and testing (including HIV finger- prick test) and network meetings on Anti-Retroviral Treatment.",""],[1,"193","3","Sentinel Surveillance and Bio-Behavioral Survey Programme","Regularly conduct sentinel surveillance, including HIV sentinel and integrated bio- behavior sentinel surveys.",""],[1,"193","4","HIV Testing and Counseling Policy Development","Develop policy on implementation of HIV testing and counseling services to ensure equitable and easy access to services, particularly by those most at risk.",""],[1,"193","5","Strategic Plan for HIV/AIDS and Sexually Transmitted Infections Prevention, Care and Treatment","Update, implement and monitor the Strategic Plan for HIV/AIDS and Sexually Transmitted Infections prevention, care and treatment 2014-2020 to assure alignment with the Cambodia 3.0 Conceptual Framework for Elimination of New HIV Infections in Cambodia by 2020.",""],[1,"193","6","HIV Treatment Guidelines and SOP Development","Continue under the leadership of the National Center for HIV/AIDS, Dermatology, and STIs (NCHADS) to finalize guidelines for pediatric and adult anti-retroviral treatment and continue development of standard operating procedures for the Boosted Continuum of Prevention, Care and Treatment.","National Center for HIV/AIDS, Dermatology, and STIs (NCHADS)"],[1,"193","7","Integration of Sexual and Reproductive Health and HIV Services","Enhance integration of SRH and HIV services to ensure key populations and PLHIV have access to contraception, safe abortion, safe motherhood and other relevant services.",""],[1,"193","8","HIV/AIDS and Harm Reduction Linkage Programme","Ensure effective linkages between HIV/AIDS and harm reduction programmes (e.g., need & syringes, methadone) for people who use drugs and are at risk of HIV.",""],[1,"193","9","Free Tuberculosis Services","Provide tuberculosis services free of charges for all, including detection, smear examination, diagnosis and treatment.",""],[1,"193","10","Collaborative Tuberculosis-HIV/AIDS Co-infection Response","Promote collaborative efforts to address combined Tuberculosis-HIV/AIDS co infection.",""],[1,"193","11","Tuberculosis Laboratory Diagnostics and Quality Assurance Support","Provide supplies and equipment for a variety of laboratory diagnostic, monitoring and quality assurance/quality control procedures, ensure providers are trained and competent in tuberculosis diagnostics, treatment monitoring and adherence.",""],[1,"193","12","Community Participation in Community-Based DOTS","Seek community participation in Community-based Directly Observed Treatment (DOTS).",""],[1,"193","13","Public-Private Partnership Improvement in Mixed-DOT","Improve public and private partnership in mixed-DOT.",""],[1,"193","14","Multi-Drug-Resistant Tuberculosis Detection and Management","Improve detection, management of multi-drug-resistant Tuberculosis.",""],[1,"193","15","Tuberculosis Drug Supply Assurance","Ensure availability of first and second line Tuberculosis drugs.",""],[1,"193","16","Malaria Detection, Early Diagnosis and Treatment Access Improvement","Improve access to malaria detection, early diagnosis and treatment.",""],[1,"193","17","Treatment Access and Drug Quality Regulation","Improve access to treatment and prevent application of mono-therapy and substandard drugs in both public and private sector.",""],[1,"193","18","Malaria Prevention and Mosquito Control Measures","Increase access to preventive measures, especially prevent transmission of artemisinin- resistant malaria parasite through mosquito control.",""],[1,"193","19","Community Awareness and Behavioral Change for Malaria Control","Promote community awareness and behavioral change among population at risk, and contain artemisinin resistant parasites.",""],[1,"193","20","Vector Control Commodity Supply Assurance","Ensure adequate stocks of abate/Bti for both rounds (in May and August) in high-risk areas, and ensure adequate and timely supplies of insecticides.",""],[1,"193","21","Dengue Diagnosis and Treatment Capacity Improvement","Improve clinical capacity for diagnosis and treatment of dengue.",""],[1,"193","22","Community Health Education and Dengue Prevention Mobilization","Mobilize communities for health education and dengue prevention.",""],[1,"193","23","Integrated Vector Management and Epidemic Preparedness Programme","Improve integrated vectors management including epidemic preparedness and outbreak response.",""],[1,"194","1","Regular Helminthiasis Chemotherapy","Provide regular chemotherapy for helminthiasis to the population at risk.",""],[1,"194","3","Emerging and Re-emerging Infectious Disease Prevention and Control","Prevent and control of emerging and remerging infectious diseases, including timely and effective response to diseases outbreaks.",""],[1,"194","4","Clinical Management, Disease Surveillance, and Vector Control Training","Provide training on clinical management and disease surveillance and victors control.",""],[1,"194","5","Rapid Response Team Disease Surveillance and Response Capacity Building","Strengthen capacity of Rapid Response Teams in disease surveillance and response through training in Applied Epidemiology.",""],[1,"194","6","International Health Regulations Implementation Reinforcement","Reinforce implementation of International Health Regulations.",""],[1,"194","7","Cambodian Early Warning Systems Maintenance","Maintain Cambodian Early Warning Systems, including sentinel surveillance for Influenza- Like Illness and SARS at all levels.",""],[1,"197","3","National Disease Surveillance and Outbreak Response Strengthening","Improve national disease surveillance system, diagnosis, case notification and timely outbreak response.",""],[1,"197","15","National HIV and AIDS Multisectoral Response Coordination","National AIDS Authority (NAA) is the sole and high government authority to lead, manage, coordinate and facilitate the national multispectral and comprehensive response to HIV and AIDS in Cambodia.",""],[1,"197","16","HIV Prevention and Early Treatment Strengthening","the 100% condom policy and condom promotion have to be strengthened with the initiation of new scientific approach such as pre and post exposure prophylaxis, positive prevention and early anti-retroviral therapy etc.",""],[1,"198","1","AIDS Law and Policy Review","The AIDS law and AIDS related law and policy should be reviewed.",""],[1,"198","2","Expanded Early Antiretroviral Therapy Coverage","the early anti-retroviral therapy coverage should be expanded",""],[1,"198","2","New ART Initiation Criteria Based on CD4 Count","the application of new criteria of initiation of ART based on number of CD4 less than 500/mm3should be initiated",""],[1,"198","2","Improved Quality of Life for People Living with HIV","the quality of life of PLHIV should be improved",""],[1,"198","3","National Monitoring and Evaluation System Strengthening","The national monitoring and evaluation system should be strengthen and improved including HIV sentinel surveillance, behavioral surveillance etc. through quality data and information management, publication and dissemination.",""],[1,"198","4","Targeted HIV Prevention, Treatment and Support Programme","NAA will implement strategies, programs and projects to further reduce the number of new HIV infections by focusing on targeted prevention interventions; increase coverage and quality of care, treatment and support for people living with and affected by AIDS; and alleviate the socio-economic and human impact of AIDS on the individual, family, community and society.","NAA"],[1,"198","6","Expansion of Comprehensive Care and Support Interventions","Increase coverage of effective interventions for comprehensive care and support and develop additional interventions.",""],[1,"198","8","Strengthen HIV and AIDS Response Leadership","Strengthen leadership of government institutions and NGOS for the implementation of the national response to HIV and AIDS at both national and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"198","9","Supportive Legal and Public Policy Environment for HIV and AIDS Response","Ensure a supportive legal and public policy environment for the national response to HIV and AIDS.",""],[1,"198","10","Monitoring, Evaluation and Research Information System","Increase the availability of information for policy makers and program planners through monitoring, evaluation and research.",""],[1,"198","11","HIV and AIDS Resource Mobilization and Allocation Strengthening","Increase and ensure the sustainability and efficiency of the mobilization and allocation of resources for the response to HIV and AIDS at both national and sub-national levels.",""]],"26":[[1,"100","18","Health Surveillance Strengthening","13. Promote greater health surveillance.",""]],"27":[[1,"27","5","National Drug Control Policy Implementation","NACD is responsible for implementation the RGC's drug control policy.",""],[1,"27","6","Drug Demand Reduction Cooperation and Public Awareness","NACD increased cooperation with Ministries, Provincial and Municipal Drugs Control Committees, the local and international development partners, and other stakeholders.","Ministries | Provincial and Municipal Drugs Control Committees | the local and international development partners | other stakeholders"],[1,"27","7","Drug Awareness Integration into Educational Curriculum","Integration of the awareness on the dangerous drugs into educational curriculum",""],[1,"28","2","Drug Supply Reduction and Precursor Control","NACD increased cooperation with ministries/Institutions and law enforcement agencies to crack down on the offences in production, trafficking, distribution of precursor chemical diversions.",""],[1,"28","5","Drug Addict Treatment Subsidy Support","The Royal government decided to provide drug addicts with subsidies who are under treatment in the rehabilitation centres governed by Ministry of Social Affairs Veteran and Youth Rehabilitation.","Ministry of Social Affairs Veteran and Youth Rehabilitation"],[1,"28","7","Community-Based Treatment and Rehabilitation Services","Adopted community based on treatment and rehabilitation to carried out by mental health and drug services of the Ministry of Health.","Ministry of Health"],[1,"28","18","International Cooperation Strengthening and Expansion","NACD has continued to everlastingly strengthen and expand the cooperation with international community in many forms:",""],[1,"71","13","Drug Abuse Victim Rehabilitation Policy","Prepared policy for rehabilitation to victims of drug abuse and juveniles who fell on the wrong side of the law and encouraged treatment and rehabilitation of the victims of such abuse.",""],[1,"124","7","Implementation of the 3-Year National Plan on Drug Control","The National Authority for Combating Drugs (NACD), will continue to efficiently implement the 5 strategies pans of the 3-Year National Plan on Drug Control.",""],[1,"125","1","Drug Abuse Prevention Awareness and Education Programme","Education, awareness raising, prevention and saying no to drugs: increasing public awareness of the harmful effects and the impact of illicit drugs upon society.",""],[1,"125","1","Drug and HIV/AIDS School Curriculum Integration","Facilitate with relevant ministries and institutions to promote and integrate the program of education on illicit drug and HIV/AIDS from the abuse of drugs into the school curricula of both in formal and non-formal education systems.",""],[1,"125","1","Drug Abuse Prevention Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","Promote and prepare mechanism for monitoring and evaluation of drug abuse prevention activities to ensure the future effectiveness.",""],[1,"125","2","Community-Based Drug User Treatment Services","Community based treatment for drug users through drugs and health services of the Ministry of Health.","Ministry of Health"],[1,"125","2","Methadone Maintenance Treatment Programme","Methadone maintenance treatment program in Cambodia.",""],[1,"125","2","Drug Abuse Treatment, Rehabilitation and Reintegration Policy","Development of a drug abuse treatment, rehabilitation and reintegration draft policy.",""],[1,"125","2","Drug Treatment and Rehabilitation Center Establishment","The establishment of the structure of the center for drug treatment, rehabilitation and reintegration of drugs addicts.",""],[1,"125","2","Community Drug Counseling Team","The creation of a counseling team at the community level.",""],[1,"125","2","Capacity Building for Drug Treatment and Rehabilitation Centers","Increasing the capacities of drug treatment, rehabilitation centers.",""],[1,"125","7","Strengthening National and Sub-National Drug Control Mechanisms","Strengthening mechanism of drug control at national and sub-national level: strengthening the structure of the NACD within national and sub-national level.",""],[1,"125","7","Creation of Technical Working Groups for Drug Control","Promote the creation of other Technical Working Groups that would be more necessary on the activities of drugs control.",""],[1,"125","7","Incentive Policy for Drug Control Performance","Develop the policy to encourage the officials and other agencies with a remarkable achievement to fight against drugs.",""]],"28":[[1,"83","3","Health Disaster Preparedness and Flood Response","MOH, Provincial Health Departments, Operational Districts, Referral Hospitals and Health Centres have been prepared to respond to disasters.","MOH | Provincial Health Departments | Operational Districts | Referral Hospitals and Health Centres"],[1,"83","11","Pro-Poor Health Financing Schemes","MOH has implemented a number of pro-poor health financing schemes.","MOH"],[1,"83","12","Health Sector Personnel and Operations Database","MOH has also developed and operated a database for personnel, training, drug management, health coverage plan, annual operational plans, etc.","MOH"],[1,"84","3","Health Sector Coordination and Collaboration Mechanisms","Coordination and collaboration in the health sector has been strengthened though the MOH's Technical Working Group, and the Provincial Technical Working Group for Heath.","MOH"]],"29":[[1,"203","3","Health Sector Sanitation and Epidemic Prevention Measures","Making further interventions in the health sector aimed at improving the sanitary conditions, enhancing prevention of epidemics and other health risks",""],[1,"203","3","Maternal, Infant, and Child Health and Nutrition Support","promoting wellbeing of mothers, infants and children by paying attention to correcting malnutrition",""],[1,"203","12","Cash Transfers for Poor Pregnant Women and Young Children","Scaling up cash transfers program to poor pregnant women and young children and strengthening early-childhood development, health, and nutrition service delivery, would be instrumental in improving nutritional and cognitive skills.",""],[1,"203","12","Early Childhood Development, Health, and Nutrition Service Delivery Strengthening","Scaling up cash transfers program to poor pregnant women and young children and strengthening early-childhood development, health, and nutrition service delivery, would be instrumental in improving nutritional and cognitive skills.",""]],"30":[[1,"202","7","Micronutrient Food Fortification Promotion","Encouraging micro-nutrient fortification in food such as Vitamin A to Zinc.",""],[1,"202","8","Food Fortification Quality Control and Assurance","Promoting the quality control and quantity assurance of food fortified with micro- nutrients such as iodized salt, fish and soy sauce fortified with iron, etc. both domestic and exported products.",""]],"31":[[1,"65","14","CEDAW Recommendation Implementation Coordination","MOLVT disseminated and allocated duties for implementation of the 42 point recommendations of the convention on elimination of all forms of discrimination against women (CEDAW).","MOLVT"],[1,"71","4","MOSVY Gender Working Group","Created MOSVY Gender Working Group.",""],[1,"84","2","Gender Working Group Capacity-Building and Supervision","MOH has provided training to members of the Gender Working Group in provinces and municipalities to increase their understanding of health within the overall gender framework.","MOH"],[1,"85","8","Women in Development Centres","These efforts include establishing Women in Development Centres (WDC) in 13 provinces, which play an important role in delivering business development services to women.",""],[1,"85","10","Vocational Skills Development for Women","Strengthening vocational skills for women based on the market demand.",""],[1,"85","11","Micro, Small and Medium Enterprise Development","Developing micro, small and medium enterprises.",""],[1,"205","5","Gender Mainstreaming and Women's Empowerment Initiative","Continue to mainstream on gender at national and sub-national levels, promote the role of women in society, eliminate all discriminations against women and continue to mainstream women in public life.",""],[1,"208","15","Implementation of Domestic Violence and Human Trafficking Laws","The government is implementing the Law on Prevention of Domestic Violence and Protection of the Victim and the Law on Suppression of Human Trafficking and Sexual Exploitation.",""],[1,"208","15","Women's Rights Advocacy and Policy Support","In the economic sector, the RGC has advocated for the rights of women workers through advocacy and policy interventions.",""],[1,"208","15","Women's Skills and Decision-Making Capacity Building","Women are now being equipped with skills and they have the capacity to participate in decision-making.",""],[1,"208","17","Women’s Vocational and Entrepreneurship Skills Programme","Promoting the role of women in the economy through strengthening vocational training programs, equipping them with technical and entrepreneurial skills, and empowering them.",""],[1,"209","1","Women’s Leadership Promotion in the Public Sector","Promoting the role of women in public sector through increasing the sex ratio in line ministries and strengthening their ability to pursue leadership.",""],[1,"209","2","National Action Plan to Prevent Violence Against Women","Promoting implementation of \"National Action Plan to Prevent Violence Against Women\" aimed at eliminating violence against women.",""],[1,"209","5","Gender Mainstreaming in Government Initiatives","Further mainstreaming gender in government initiatives",""],[1,"209","6","CEDAW and Gender Equality Commitments Implementation","RGC during the Fifth Legislature will continue to implement CEDAW, other relevant conventions, regional commitments relating to gender equality and women's rights",""],[1,"209","6","Women’s Employment and Representation Promotion","RGC will strive to increase the ratio of women at all government levels, by providing employment opportunities for women, using advocacy at the village and commune levels throughout the country",""],[1,"209","7","Gender Mainstreaming Across Development Programmes and Sectors","RGC will continue to implement the gender equality policy through mainstreaming gender in all development programmes and sectors in order to reduce women's poverty and vulnerability especially disabled women and minority women.",""],[1,"209","7","Women's Economic Empowerment Initiative","Specifically, the RGC will put strong focus on women's economic empowerment, gender and climate change and green growth, women's decision making in public and political spheres, legal protection for women and girls, women's health, and education for women and girls.",""],[1,"209","7","Women's Political Participation and Decision-Making Support","Specifically, the RGC will put strong focus on women's economic empowerment, gender and climate change and green growth, women's decision making in public and political spheres, legal protection for women and girls, women's health, and education for women and girls.",""],[1,"209","7","Legal Protection for Women and Girls","Specifically, the RGC will put strong focus on women's economic empowerment, gender and climate change and green growth, women's decision making in public and political spheres, legal protection for women and girls, women's health, and education for women and girls.",""],[1,"209","7","Women's Health Improvement Initiative","Specifically, the RGC will put strong focus on women's economic empowerment, gender and climate change and green growth, women's decision making in public and political spheres, legal protection for women and girls, women's health, and education for women and girls.",""],[1,"209","9","Gender Wage Employment Equality Measures","RGC aims to eliminate gender disparities in wage employment, specifically in the agriculture, industry, and service sectors.",""],[1,"209","10","Women’s Skills Training and Scholarship Support","Provision of skills training for jobs for women: by providing technical and vocational training programs based on market demands for women, strengthening business development services of the Women in Development Centers (WDC), and increasing scholarship for women and girls.",""],[1,"209","11","Women-Led MSME Development Support","Promoting and enhancing MSMEs led by women: by delivering micro, small and medium enterprise development service and continuing to give relevant policy interventions to ensure that they have the capacity to lead and grow their enterprises and move from the informal to the formal sector.",""],[1,"209","12","Gender Mainstreaming in Rural and Agricultural Development Programmes","Gender mainstreaming in rural and agricultural development programes will ensure that rural women in on-farm and off-farm activities, poorest and vulnerable women in particular, are able to diversify their economic activities, increase their productivity, and expand livelihood opportunities.",""],[1,"210","19","Women’s Participation in Education Service Delivery and Management","Increase the participation of women in all areas of education service delivery and management, and promote gender responsive social behaviour.",""],[1,"211","5","Gender Mainstreaming Capacity Building for Development Agencies","Building the capacity of state and non-state development agencies in gender mainstreaming in environment and climate change policies, programes and national environmental action plans.",""]],"32":[[1,"202","9","Social Protection System Strengthening and Integration","The Royal Government of the Fifth Legislature will continue strengthening the social protection system to be more interconnected and coordinated and consolidate it as an integrated, consistent, and efficient system covering both the public and private sectors, including a clear cut division of roles distinguishing between policymaking, regulation and operations.",""],[1,"202","10","Social Protection Policy Framework and Strategy Update","Improving the social protection policy framework and strategy, including the update of \"National Social Protection Strategy for the Poor and Vulnerable 2011-2015\" and other related documents such as \"Financial Sector Development Strategy 2011- 2020\"so as to be more consistent and responsive to the above objective.",""],[1,"202","11","Institutional Coordination and Social Protection Harmonization Mechanism","Further promoting and developing a mechanism for institutional coordination including harmonization of the existing intervention schemes, preparing studies and functional analysis of target areas of protection, instruments and implementation arrangements aimed at increasing efficiency in resource use and fill the gap in social protection for the poor and vulnerable that will result in a comprehensive social security system under the Law on Social Security System for the Cambodian People.",""],[1,"203","9","Comprehensive Social Safety Net System","The Royal Government remains committed to developing and implementing a comprehensive and sustainable social safety net system aimed at protecting the livelihoods of the poor and most vulnerable segments of the population.",""],[1,"203","9","Social Safety Net Policy Consensus-Building","CARD has taken some important steps to build consensus on the key concepts and broad direction for policy development on social safety nets for the poor and vulnerable segments of the population in collaboration with implementing line ministries.","implementing line ministries"],[1,"203","11","Scale-Up of National Social Protection Programs","Test, implement and scale-up programs proposed under the NSPS to start putting in place a comprehensive, effective and affordable social protection system.",""],[1,"203","11","Evaluation, Harmonization, and Scale-Up of Existing Social Protection Programs","Social protection programs for the poor and vulnerable currently being designed, implemented and/or piloted (cash transfers, public works, nutrition, Health Equity Fund, school feeding, and poverty-targeted scholarships) need to be evaluated, harmonized and scaled-up by:",""],[1,"204","4","Social Protection System Harmonization and Delivery Strengthening","Building an efficient and effective Social Protection (SP) system requires harmonizing across the existing and new programs and strengthening delivery systems.",""],[1,"204","12","Strengthen Social Protection and Safety Nets","To implement RGC's priority policies to strengthen social protection and safety nets, three strategies are put forth: (1) Increase the effectiveness of social services; (2) Promote the social security system; and (3) Strengthen institutional capacity and resource-raising.",""],[1,"206","24","Comprehensive Social Security System","Create a comprehensive social security system covering layer on the scope of people of all segments of society as the core of the social safety net.",""],[1,"207","1","Social Security Law Drafting and Legal Framework Preparation","study, prepare draft law on social security for general people submitting to stakeholders for discussion and approval and prepare supporting legal frameworks.",""],[1,"207","2","Social Officers Institutional Capacity and Professional Responsibility Strengthening","Continue efforts to build institutional capacity and strengthen professional responsibility of the social officers for them to take up the said tasks.",""],[1,"207","3","National Institute of Social Affairs Establishment","Set up the National Institute of Social Affairs to train human resources for state institutions and NGOS.",""],[1,"207","4","Cross-Sector Reform Program","Continue to implement the reform program on all sectors in accordance with the Government's policy to increase effectiveness.",""],[1,"207","5","NGO Partnership for Support to Vulnerable Groups","Continue to strengthen the partnership with NGOs to help the victims, poor and vulnerable groups.",""]],"33":[[1,"182","22","Health Insurance Expansion","Expand health insurance and pension division: Health Insurance:",""],[1,"182","23","Health Insurance Legal and IT Management System","Prepare legal standards for health insurance and prepare an IT-based system for management of registration for pay-ins and pay-outs.",""],[1,"182","24","Health Service Fee Payment Methods","Establish health service fee payment methods.",""],[1,"182","25","Health Insurance Information Dissemination Campaign","Disseminate information on health insurance through workshops, meetings, advertising spots and leaflets.",""],[1,"182","26","Pension Scheme Feasibility Study","Conduct a study into the possibilities of having a pension scheme.",""],[1,"182","27","Legal Standard Document Preparation and Human Resource Training","Prepare legal standard documents and training of human resources.",""],[1,"182","28","Pension Implementation Information Technology System","Prepare an information technology system for implementation of pensions and conduct widespread public dissemination.",""],[1,"183","1","Social Security Expansion for Labor Risk Insurance, Health Insurance, and Pensions","Develop social security to recipients of labor risk insurance, health insurance, and pensions:",""],[1,"183","3","Labor Risk Insurance Policy","Develop a labor risk insurance policy, and take measures to prevent occupational injuries among workers/employees.",""],[1,"183","3","Occupational Injury Prevention Measures","Develop a labor risk insurance policy, and take measures to prevent occupational injuries among workers/employees.",""],[1,"183","4","Pre-Rehabilitation Support for Workers with Occupational Injuries","Provide a pre-rehabilitation service to workers/employees who suffer from occupational hazards resulting in permanent loss of physical fitness, so that they receive some restoration of their physique, intelligence and profession.",""],[1,"183","14","Social Safety Net System Strengthening","Further developing and strengthening social safety net systems to be centralized, integrated, consistent and efficient.",""],[1,"184","16","Long-Term Savings Mobilization for Social Safety Net","Encourage mobilizing long-term saving to create a social safety net.",""],[1,"184","18","Pension System Legal and Regulatory Framework","Formulate a legal framework to regulate and monitor the pension system.",""],[1,"202","12","Strengthening of Civil Servants and Veterans Pension Funds","Further implementing the national policy on pension for veterans and former civil servants more efficiently through strengthening the national social security fund for civil servants and national fund for veterans.",""],[1,"203","8","Occupational Risk Insurance Expansion","Further expanding occupational risk insurance and making arrangements to implement health insurance scheme for workers, employees and their dependents, and pension fund for workers and employees.",""],[1,"203","8","Worker Health Insurance Scheme","Further expanding occupational risk insurance and making arrangements to implement health insurance scheme for workers, employees and their dependents, and pension fund for workers and employees.",""],[1,"203","8","Worker Pension Fund Arrangement","Further expanding occupational risk insurance and making arrangements to implement health insurance scheme for workers, employees and their dependents, and pension fund for workers and employees.",""],[1,"204","11","Expansion of Contributory Social Security to the Informal Sector","Strengthening and expanding the coverage of the existing contributory social security programs and developing a strategic framework for expansion to the informal sector.",""],[1,"206","14","Social Security Benefits for Former Civil Servants","Continue to provide them social security benefits in accordance with budget provisions.",""],[1,"206","15","State Contribution to Civil Servant Pension Scheme","Continue to implement the principle of state contribution of 6% of salary instead of civil servants paying for it.",""],[1,"206","16","Civil Servants Social Security Benefits","Continue to implement the social security for civil servants 6 benefits, include: retirement, invalidity, maternity, work injury, death and their dependents.",""],[1,"206","17","National Veterans Policy Implementation","Continue implementing the national policy on veterans.",""],[1,"206","18","Veterans Support Funding","Continue to provide resources to support programs for the veterans to the extent that the national budget permits.",""],[1,"206","19","Veterans Social Security Payment Information System","Develop an information system to ensure that payment of social security fund that the veterans get what is due to them.",""],[1,"206","20","National Veterans Fund Contribution Sub-Decree","Prepare sub-decree on determine contribution required for supporting the National Veterans Fund.",""]],"34":[[1,"205","1","Street Folk Support and Social Integration Services","Continue to strengthen problem-solving for street folk, provide services to street folk based on the principle of respect for human rights, and give a chance for them to get a livelihood and integration into the society.",""],[1,"205","2","Anti-Human Trafficking Victim Rehabilitation and Reintegration Programme","Fight against human trafficking and assist victims through rehabilitation, vocational training and integration of the victims back to the community",""],[1,"205","3","HIV/AIDS Assistance Programme","Continue to provide assistance to people affected by HIV/AIDS",""]],"35":[[1,"70","19","National Social Security Fund Work Risk Insurance Expansion","Between 2008 and 2012, NSSF registered 4,583 enterprises and 868,134 employees, and provided work risk insurance to more than 37,000 employees.",""],[1,"70","19","Work Risk Insurance Geographic Coverage Expansion","By about the first quarter of 2013, the work risk insurance would expand its coverage to 24 cities of all the 24 provinces in the country.",""]],"36":[[1,"81","4","Gender-Based Violence Cross-Cutting Interventions","With Development Partners' support, the Ministry of Women Affairs (MOWA) is striving to promote cross cutting interventions on Gender-based Violence","Ministry of Women Affairs (MOWA)"],[1,"85","16","Safe Village-Commune Policy","The implementation of Safe Village-Commune Policy has contributed to promoting social morality, and women and family-values.",""],[1,"86","2","Training of Judicial Police Agents for Women Victims of Gender-Based Violence","In 2013, 141 staff members of MOWA at both national and sub- national levels have become qualified as Judicial Police Agents on the protection and assistance for women victims of gender-based violence, and have begun to perform their roles according to the law.","MOWA"],[1,"86","3","National Action Plan to Prevent Trafficking in Persons","In order to prevent trafficking in persons, MOWA has developed the National Action Plan for implementation in 2012-2014","MOWA"],[1,"86","3","Cambodia-Thailand Bilateral Cooperation to Eliminate Trafficking in Women and Children","amended the Memorandum of Understanding between Cambodia and Thailand on Bilateral Cooperation to Eliminate Trafficking in Women and Children and Rescue of the Trafficked Victims","MOWA"],[1,"86","3","Cambodia-Vietnam Bilateral Cooperation on Trafficking Victim Rescue","MOWA has signed an amendment to the agreement between the Cambodia and Vietnam on Bilateral Cooperation to Eliminate Trafficking in Persons and Rescue Trafficked Victims","MOWA"],[1,"86","3","Action Plan for Trafficking in Persons Prevention","has drafted an Action Plan for implementation in 2013-2014","MOWA"]],"37":[[1,"74","2","National Social Protection Strategy Implementation","The implementation of National Social Protection Strategy (NSPS) requires a mix of programs that cover both chronic and transient poverty as well as help promote human capital development.",""],[1,"74","2","IDPoor Targeting Tool","This has been done through the targeting tool IDPoor, that identifies poor people by capturing idiosyncratic risks and covariate vulnerability like that caused by climate change or natural hazards.",""],[1,"74","2","Social Protection Programme Scale-Up","The NSPS has provided a framework to scale-up existing interventions such as the school meals program, poverty-targeted scholarship programs and the health equity fund, and to introduce new modalities of implementation through for example the Productive Assets and Livelihood Support program (a cash-based public works program).",""],[1,"74","5","Model Cash Transfer Program for Pregnant Women and Young Children","A model cash transfer program using government structures has been designed to provide benefits to pregnant women and young children taking into account early childhood development approach.",""],[1,"74","5","Pilot Cash Transfer Programs by Development Partners","Pilot programs are being implemented by development partners and the successful modality will be subject to review by CARD for national scale up.",""],[1,"100","6","Context-Specific Poverty and Vulnerability Alleviation Strategies","Develop poverty/vulnerability alleviation strategies contextualized to geographic and territorial specificities.",""],[1,"100","8","ID-Poor Program Expansion","Intensify ID-Poor programs.",""],[1,"100","9","Social Security Network Expansion","Expand social security network - Cash transfers, Food For Work, pensions, others.",""],[1,"104","5","Pension Fund Savings Mobilization and Social Safety Net","Encourage mobilizing and institutionalizing long-term savings for both, investments through the pension fund route, and a social safety net for the pension beneficiaries.",""]],"38":[[1,"72","16","Community and Religious Support for the Elderly","Encouraged communities, and Buddhist and other religious places, to assist the elderly.",""],[1,"202","14","National Policy for the Elderly People Implementation","Further promoting the National Policy for the Elderly People through the Cambodian National Committee for the Elderly People; further strengthening the association of senior citizens, promoting welfare programs for elderly people at the community level and improved care programs for seniors at the family level; and in particular, enhancing arrangements and processes in providing services to the aged including provision of training for their care providers.",""],[1,"206","4","National Elderly Policy Implementation","Continue to implement the national policy for the elderly.",""],[1,"206","5","Support for National and Sub-national Elderly Policy Implementation Mechanisms","Promote the activities of the National Committee and sub-national mechanisms for the implementation of policies for the elderly people.",""],[1,"206","6","Community Elderly Development Program","Implement two programs: (1) The elderly in the community development program, and (2) Care for the elderly in the family.",""],[1,"206","6","Family Elderly Care Program","Implement two programs: (1) The elderly in the community development program, and (2) Care for the elderly in the family.",""],[1,"206","7","Family-Based Elderly Care Promotion Program","Continue to promote elderly care program in the family to the media, promoting good family tradition of respect and gratitude to the elderly.",""],[1,"206","8","Community Support for Elderly Assistance","Continue to encourage the communities, Buddhist and other religious place, to assist the elderly.",""],[1,"206","9","Elderly Support Program","Continue to strengthen the activities for the elderly people: create a health care program, a rice bank, a death rescue fund, and a solidarity program for helping each other.",""],[1,"206","10","Humanitarian Support Program for Elderly People","Continue to encourage charities to create a humanitarian program to help the elderly and to help build houses for poor elderly people.",""],[1,"206","11","Humanitarian Assistance Continuation","Encourage the elite, charities and authorities at all levels to continue providing humanitarian assistance.",""],[1,"206","12","Cambodia Service Center for the Elderly","Prepare and implement the Cambodia Service Center for the elderly.",""],[1,"206","13","Elderly Health Service Provision by NGOs and Private Sector","Encourage NGOs/private sector to create health services for the elderly.",""]],"39":[[1,"202","13","National Disability Policy Implementation and Disability Fund Service Improvement","Further implementing the national policy on disability through the Disability Action Council; strengthening the implementation of the Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, and promoting the enhancement of rights and welfare of the disabled according to the United Nations Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, as well as improving the quality and efficiency of the disability fund's services.",""],[1,"205","15","Disability Rights Protection and Anti-Discrimination Implementation","Implement the law on protection and promotion the rights of persons with disability in accordance with the national policy, eliminate discrimination and provide them opportunities for participating all activities in the society.",""],[1,"205","16","Disability Fund Service Delivery","Continue implementing the disability fund to provide services to people with disabilities according to the law.",""],[1,"205","17","Support for Poor People with Disabilities","Support poor people with disabilities in conjunction with availability of funds.",""],[1,"205","18","Community-Based Disability Services and Economic Inclusion Programme","Continue implementing community-based services for persons with disabilities, provide rehabilitation services, constitute self-help groups, induct them into small- scale businesses, encourage formation of organizations of persons with disabilities like the Blind Association, Cambodian People with Disabilities Organization, and National Center for Persons with Disabilities.",""],[1,"205","19","Employment Quota for Persons with Disabilities","Provide employment opportunities to people with disabilities; up to 2%in government institutions, and 1% in private institutions.",""],[1,"206","1","Special Services Center for Children with Disabilities","Continue providing services to blind and deaf children and children with mental deficiency through creation of a center to provide special services.",""],[1,"206","2","Disability Inclusion in Media, Sport, and Accessibility Support","Encourage art and sport movement for persons with disabilities, have news bulletin in sign language, and develop sign language and brail.",""],[1,"206","3","National Disability Programme 2014-2018","Prepare and implementation of the national program on disability 2014-2018, including people with disabilities by mines.",""]],"40":[[1,"205","6","Child Welfare and Youth Rehabilitation Programme","Develop child welfare and youth rehabilitation:",""],[1,"205","7","Implementation of the Convention on the Rights of the Child","Continue to implement the International Convention on the Rights of the Child; in particular, the survival rights, development rights, protection rights, and participation rights, prepared report the 4th to 6th on the implementation of the convention on the rights of the child and report on the implementation of other relevant protocol to the UN on time and quality.",""],[1,"205","8","National Plan for Child Development 2015-2025","Develop NationalPlan for Child Development 2015-2025; laws and policy related to Child Rights, to promote implementation of the National Plan on the elimination of child labor; and continue to plan activities for social budget analysis focused on the children.",""],[1,"205","8","Child Rights Law and Policy Framework","laws and policy related to Child Rights, to promote implementation of the National Plan on the elimination of child labor; and continue to plan activities for social budget analysis focused on the children.",""],[1,"205","8","Social Budget Analysis for Children","continue to plan activities for social budget analysis focused on the children.",""],[1,"205","9","Strengthening the Cambodia National Council of Children","Continue to strengthen the Cambodia National Council of Children, both at the national and sub-national levels and increase cooperation with partner organizations to promote children's rights.",""],[1,"205","11","Child Welfare System and Alternative Care Strengthening","Continue to implement the child welfare system, promote alternative care policy for children, set minimum standards on alternative care, and strengthen the role of the sub-national institutions in children's affairs.",""],[1,"205","12","Residential Care Center Quality Strengthening and Adoption Cooperation Measures","Continue strengthening the quality of the residential care centers through inspection, seek legal standards and mechanism to find families for children, and implement the Hague Convention on cooperation related to inter-country adoption.",""]],"41":[[1,"51","8","Road Infrastructure Rehabilitation and Construction Projects","Completed thirty road infrastructure rehabilitation and construction projects (1,972.7 Km) and another 35 projects (2,365.27 Km) are under progress.",""],[1,"51","13","Truck Overloading Control Measures","The Permanent Coordination Committee (PCC), under the supervision of the Overloaded Truck Inspection Committee, has undertaken measures against overloading of trucks.",""],[1,"51","14","Road Safety Enhancement Measures","The National Road Safety Committee (NRSC) has formulated a new draft law on road traffic; a National Decade Action Plan for Road Safety 2011-2020; and an Action Plan for Road Safety 2011-2014 focusing on use of safety helmets and safety belt, and controlling drunken driving.",""],[1,"53","3","GMS Cross-Border Transport Agreement Implementation","To implement this agreement, RGC has entered into bi-lateral MOUs on Initial Implementation of the GMS Cross-Border Transport Agreement with Thailand and Vietnam.",""],[1,"156","8","National and Rural Road Paving Expansion","Stepping up the construction of national, provincial and rural roads, particularly by targeting the paving of 300 to 400 Km of additional roads per year with asphalt or concrete pavement.",""],[1,"156","9","Road Repair and Maintenance System Strengthening","Directing more attention to the repair and maintenance of the transport system, particularly roads through the strengthening of mechanisms and enhancement of road repair and maintenance system, including effective and strict enforcement of punitive measures against overloading.",""],[1,"157","6","Road Infrastructure Improvement Programme","Improve more 3,500 Km of road infrastructure in the next 5 years.",""],[1,"157","7","1-Digit National Roads Upgrading Programme","Improve 1-Digit National Roads - expand from DBST to AC pavement.",""],[1,"157","8","National Road Widening Programme","Widen 1-Digit NRs from 2 lanes to 4 lanes in and around major cities.",""],[1,"157","10","National Road Drainage Facilities for Flood Control","Install drainage facilities in 1-Digit National Roads, for flood control.",""],[1,"157","14","High-Speed Road Construction Programme","Encourage for constructing high speed roads (1st Priority is Phnom Penh to Preah Shihanouk).",""]],"42":[[1,"156","10","Traffic Safety Law Enforcement and Road Safety Improvement Measures","Further focusing on traffic safety through the improvement and stricter enforcement of the \"Law on Land Traffic\", including the strict enforcement of measures against traffic violation, strengthening vehicle safety inspection and the system for issuance of vehicle roadworthiness certificates, the mechanism for issuing driving licenses, installation of traffic signs, facilitation of traffic flow, professional ethics and competence of law enforcement officers, as well as promotion of public awareness and dissemination of information on traffic safety in accordance with the slogan: \"Today, Tomorrow: No Traffic Accident!\".",""],[1,"157","11","Capital Area Traffic Signal Expansion","Increase traffic signals in the Capital Area for smooth and safe traffic.",""],[1,"157","13","Road Safety ICT Camera Installation","Install ICTV cameras in 1-Digit NRs to check the over speed and over loaded vehicles to reduce traffic accidents and improve road safety.",""],[1,"158","29","Road Safety Action Plan Preparation","Continue the preparation of 10 years road safety action plan.",""],[1,"159","1","Road Traffic Law Enforcement for Road Safety Policy","Prepare for the defense of national road safety policy by further urging the legal enforcement of road traffic law.",""],[1,"159","2","Safety Helmet Inspection Center Construction Monitoring","Monitor the process of safety helmet inspection center construction.",""],[1,"159","3","Road Safety Management Seminar","Continue organizing the seminar on road safety management.",""],[1,"159","5","Truck Inspection Management Reform","Design methods and strategies to crack down on non-performing activities by reforming the management system of (overloaded) truck inspection.",""],[1,"159","24","Traffic Management Measures","Put in place additional measures for the management of traffic, to minimize traffic congestion.",""],[1,"159","25","Traffic Law Enforcement and Road Safety Improvement","Enforce the Traffic Law and improve road safety.",""]],"43":[[1,"156","11","Master Plan for Transport Infrastructure Development","Designing and implementing the Master Plan for Transport Infrastructure Development to connect all parts of the country and with the neighboring countries through developing multi-modal and cross border transport systems along with an efficient and competitive logistics system aimed at promoting investment, trade, tourism and rural development, with focus on the completion of railroad restoration and development, further development of airport and seaport infrastructure, assessment of the potential for investment in inland waterway transport as well as finding alternatives to monopolistic transport services and intensified implementation of various cross- border agreements and protocols signed by Cambodia.",""],[1,"156","12","Transport Infrastructure Legal and Regulatory Framework Reform","Preparing necessary policies and legal framework for the management and development of infrastructure, such as the Law on Roads and related regulations addressing road standards and quality, Law on Ports and the Law on Road Transport to facilitate the implementation of Master Plan for Transport Infrastructure Development.",""],[1,"157","1","Urban Infrastructure Development Master Plan","Preparing a Master Plan for Urban Infrastructure Development, in particular public transport in urban areas and connectivity of production centers on the outskirts of municipalities, main economic poles, industrial zones and special economic zones",""],[1,"157","2","Public-Private Partnership Promotion Policy for Transport Infrastructure","Further encouraging participation of the private sector in the development of transportation infrastructure by strengthening and improving the \"public-private partnership\" mechanism through the introduction of policy on the promotion of public- private partnership in Cambodia in order to attract and facilitate the implementation of infrastructure projects financed by the private sector.",""],[1,"157","3","Public Works and Transport Infrastructure Construction and Maintenance","Ministry of Public Work and Transportation (MPWT) is responsible for implementing the national policy concerning construction of all public works.","Ministry of Public Work and Transportation | State Secretariat of Civil Aviation | RGC"],[1,"159","6","Transport Mapping and Reporting for Trucking Sector","Draw maps and make transport reports for sending to Trucking Companies and truck owners.",""],[1,"159","8","Transport Policy and Planning Development","Make transport policy and planning in each transport sector.",""],[1,"159","9","National Expressway Master Plan and Priority Projects","Make a national expressway master plan and start initiating priority projects.",""],[1,"159","10","National Railway Master Plan and Priority Projects","Make a national railway master plan and start initiating priority projects.",""],[1,"159","11","National Port Master Plan and Private Port Investment Initiative","Make a national port master plan and invite private investment in ports.",""],[1,"159","12","Environmentally Sustainable Transport Plan","Promote environmentally sustainable transport plan.",""],[1,"159","13","National Transport Policy and Planning Integration","Integrate all transport policy and planning as a national transport policy and planning.",""],[1,"159","15","Logistics Supply and Multimodal Transport Master Plan","Prepare, in collaboration with concerned ministries/agencies, a master plan on logistics supply and multi-modal transport to enable trade facilitation.",""],[1,"159","16","Freight and Logistics Efficiency Improvement","Increase the efficiency of freight sending services, multi-modal transport, logistics, and of Kampuchea Shipping Agency & Brokers (KAMSAB).",""],[1,"159","17","Support to KAMSAB Freight and Logistics Services","Support the activities of KAMSAB to enable it to play its roles as freight sender, representative and service provider, on behalf of ship-owners or ship chartering entities or freight owners, and as logistics provider;",""],[1,"159","18","Freight Capacity Expansion of Preah Sihanouk Port and Phnom Penh Port","Increase freight capacity of Preah Sihanouk Port and Phnom Penh Port.",""],[1,"159","27","Transport Sector Planning and Data Management Strengthening","Strengthen and improve planning, statistics, data management, and information dissemination in the transport sector.",""],[1,"159","28","Transport Sector Human and Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen human and institutional capacity in the transport sector.",""],[1,"159","31","Public Works and Transport Legal Framework Development","Continue formulating laws, sub-decrees, Prakas and other legal documents related to public works and transports.",""],[1,"173","4","Transport Infrastructure Investment Programme","RGC during the Fifth Legislature will continue according priority to improve the physical infrastructure through increased public investment in transportation networks, including roads, railways, waterways (river, sea), and air routes;",""]],"44":[[1,"54","7","International Airport Terminal Expansion","Airport infrastructure: total size of boarding lounge for international terminal is 16,000 sqm (on-going expansion by 850 sqm).",""],[1,"54","8","Performance-Based Navigation Flight Procedure Implementation","Air Navigation System [Performance Based Navigation (PBN) Flight Procedure] has been implemented since July 2013.",""],[1,"54","12","PBN Flight Procedure Implementation","PBN Flight Procedure has been designed and will been implemented in 2014.",""],[1,"160","2","Strengthen International Cooperation in Civil Aviation","Strengthen international cooperation in civil aviation sector:",""],[1,"160","3","Regional Integration and Harmonization with ASEAN and Related Frameworks","Gradually integrate into and harmonize with ASEAN, GMS, CLMV Open Sky Policies, and other international cooperation frameworks.",""],[1,"160","4","SSCA Institutional Decentralization and Capacity Enhancement","Develop and enhance institutional capacities, particularly the management structure of the SSCA to transform the management system from a centralized one to one, which is decentralized.",""],[1,"160","5","Flight Security and Safety Strengthening","Strengthen flight security and safety:",""],[1,"160","6","Civil Aviation Law Amendment for Flight Safety and Climate Mitigation","Amend the Law on Civil Aviation, adopted and promulgated to meet the needs of strengthening flight security and safety, and minimize the impact of air transport services on climate change.",""],[1,"160","7","Civil Aviation Regulatory Update for Technical, Economic, and Environmental Norms","Update and formulate regulations for technical and economic norms, and for environmental sustainability, in the civil aviation sector.",""],[1,"160","8","Security and Safety Enhancement under Existing Laws and Regulations","Enhance security and safety based on the existing laws and regulations.",""],[1,"160","9","Cross-Border Security and Operational Data Exchange Agreements","Institute official agreements on security, safety, and operational data exchanges with neighboring countries.",""],[1,"160","10","Air Navigation and Aerodrome Services Strengthening","Strengthen air navigation and aerodrome services:",""],[1,"160","11","Airport Modernization and CNS/ATM Operationalization","Improve and modernize identified airports, including operationalizing the new system of Communication Navigation Surveillance/Air Traffic Management (CNS/ATM).",""],[1,"160","12","Private and Public Sector Airport Infrastructure Development","Promote participation of the private and public sectors in the development of airport infrastructure and aviation services, in particular, foster private investment in activities directly and indirectly related to the aviation sector.",""],[1,"160","13","Concessional Agreement Business Oversight and Coordination","Control and coordinate businesses under concessional agreements.",""],[1,"160","14","Female Employee Capacity-Building in Air Transportation","Further enhance the capacity and knowledge of female employees to improve the role and status of women in air transportation services.",""],[1,"160","15","Information Technology and Data Systems Development","Develop information technology, meteorological information system, statistical data system, and conduct studies and researches.",""],[1,"160","15","Meteorological Information System Development","Develop information technology, meteorological information system, statistical data system, and conduct studies and researches.",""],[1,"160","15","Statistical Data System Development","Develop information technology, meteorological information system, statistical data system, and conduct studies and researches.",""]],"45":[[1,"6","11","Trial Construction of Climate-Resilient Rural Roads","Studying and carrying out trial construction of rural roads 450 km with a bituminous surface which is 100% adaptive to climate change",""],[1,"6","12","VDC Capacity Building for Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation","Building the capacity of the VDCs in the option of adapting to and reduction of climate change and the use of appropriate and scientific knowledge acceptable at the locality",""],[1,"154","7","Rural Roads Maintenance and Repair Programme","Continue carrying out maintenance and repair of rural roads and other structures.",""],[1,"154","8","Rural Road Surface Upgrading Programme","Continue to improve the surface of rural roads from laterite to double bituminous surface or concrete.",""],[1,"154","9","Rural Roads Inventory Completion","Continue to prepare an inventory of rural roads and complete it for 24 capitals and provinces.",""],[1,"154","10","Climate Adaptation Study for Rural Roads and Civil Engineering Structures","Commence conducting a study of some rural roads and civil engineering structures to adapt them to climate change.",""],[1,"155","8","Trial Construction of Climate-Resilient Rural Roads","Studying and carrying out trial construction of rural roads 450 km with a bituminous surface which is 100% adaptive to climate change",""]],"46":[[1,"158","24","Officer Training Programme","Provide both local and overseas training to officers at all levels under cooperation with the Technical Consultant Canarail.",""],[1,"158","25","North Rail Line Rehabilitation","Complete rehabilitating the north line between Phnom Penh and Poipet to connect to Thailand.",""],[1,"158","26","Rail Freight Terminal Completion","Complete the rail freight terminals at Phnom Penh and Preah Sihanouk.",""],[1,"158","27","Efficient Railway Operations under Concessions Contract","Ensure efficient railway operations under the concessions contract.",""],[1,"158","28","Railway Construction Expansion","Encourage for extending railway construction.",""]],"47":[[1,"158","6","Navigation Channel Dredging from Phnom Penh to Kratie","Continue dredging the navigation channel from Phnom Penh to Kratie.",""],[1,"158","7","Mekong River Water Depth Survey","Conduct water depth survey in upper-stream and lower-stream Mekong River.",""],[1,"158","8","Private Sector River Port Development Initiative","Invite the private sector to develop river ports.",""],[1,"158","9","Mekong Hydrographic Survey Completion","Complete the hydrographic survey in the Mekong up to Kampong Cham.",""],[1,"158","10","River Navigation Channel Development and Navigation Aids Installation","Develop river navigation channels and install navigation aids.",""],[1,"158","11","Inland Waterway Transport Regulatory Framework Enforcement","Continue formulating and enforcing related laws, rules and regulations, such as the law on inland waterway transport; sub-decree on format and procedure for issuing garage business permit; sub-decree on management of inland waterway transport; and sub-decree on location and technical specification of navigation beacon, signal, flashlight, whistle and emergency siren.",""],[1,"158","12","River Navigation Sub-Decree Revision","Continue to revise sub-decree on river navigation.",""],[1,"158","13","Inland Waterway Transport Master Plan Preparation","Continue preparing master plan on inland waterway transport and encourage private participation in shipping activities.",""],[1,"158","14","Cambodian Maritime Code Formulation","Formulate the Cambodian Maritime Code.",""],[1,"158","15","Port Entry Permit Prakas for Foreign Vessels","Formulate Prakas on port entry permit given to foreign vessels to call ports in Cambodia.",""],[1,"158","16","National Oil-Spill Response and Cooperation System","Formulate sub-decree on establishing national system for response and cooperation in case of oil-spill at sea.",""],[1,"158","17","Crew Book Sub-Decree","Formulate sub-decree on crew book.",""],[1,"158","19","Maritime Transport Law Enforcement","Enforce laws, provisions and rules of agreement related to maritime transport.",""],[1,"158","20","Electric Marine Chart Completion","Complete the electric marine chart in Preah Sihanouk Port.",""],[1,"158","21","Preah Sihanouk Port Multi-Purpose Terminal Completion","Complete the multi-purpose terminal at Preah Sihanouk Port.",""],[1,"158","22","Preah Sihanouk Port SEZ Promotion and Rent Fulfillment","Enhance the promotion of Preah Sihanouk Port SEZ and fulfill all rents.",""],[1,"158","23","User-Friendly Vessel Services","Provide user-friendly services for vessels.",""]],"48":[[1,"157","12","Capital Area Bus Public Transportation System","Introduce bus public transportation system in the Capital Area.",""],[1,"159","20","Environmentally Friendly Urban Transportation","Strengthen environmentally friendly urban transportation.",""],[1,"159","21","Urban Public Transport Planning","Plan public transport in major urban centers.",""],[1,"159","22","Urban Transport Master Plan and Infrastructure Development","Prepare a new master plan and development of infrastructure for urban transport, including a project for commuter light train to contribute to reduction of CO2 emission.",""],[1,"159","23","Private-Sector Urban Public Transport Infrastructure and Services","Foster efficient, effective, and safe urban public transport infrastructure, and services managed and owned by the private sector.",""]],"49":[[1,"128","10","Physical Infrastructure Investment Expansion","Continue to enhance investments in physical infrastructure such as roads, bridges, dams, and irrigation to facilitate agricultural development.",""],[1,"128","10","Local Transport System Development","A lot of attention will be paid on building the local transportation system to facilitate logistics and investment in power, to ensure a reasonable availability of electricity at price of the electrical power for family, business and industry consumption.",""],[1,"133","3","Transport and Logistics Infrastructure Improvement","improve the transport infrastructure and logistics systems, including the provision of Information and Communication Technologies (ICT) to facilitate movement of goods and services, including in financial services;",""]],"50":[[1,"14","3","Competitiveness Improvement for Investment and Job Creation","Creating more jobs, especially for youth, through further improvement in Cambodia's competitiveness to attract and encourage both domestic and foreign investments.",""],[1,"14","9","Market Diversification Strategy for Exports and Investment","to sustain growth will require an entirely different set of strategies, including diversifying markets, both for exports and investments.",""],[1,"14","9","Institutional Preparedness for New Partnerships","New partnerships would also imply newer forms of institutional arrangements, for which there is need for internal preparedness.",""],[1,"242","1","Measures to Mitigate External Economic Slowdown Impacts","the RGC is taking systematic and sequenced measures to mitigate the adverse impacts of the continued slowdown in advanced economies and many other emerging economies on Cambodia's financial and economic system and to protect its hard-earned achievements.",""],[1,"242","2","Big-Push Investment and Capacity-Building Strategy","the appeal is to 'have a big-push to step up investments, activities, capacities and institutional structures, so as to gradually taper off external financing'.",""]],"51":[[1,"105","5","Special Economic Zones and Border Market Development","Continue with the policy of developing Special Economic Zones, Export Refinery Zones, Free Trade Zones, and market development along the country's borders.",""],[1,"130","4","Special Economic Zones and Border Trade Zone Development","Continue encouraging the development of Special Economic Zones, Export Refinery Zones, Free Trade Zones, market development, and business creating services along the borders with participation from the private sector.",""],[1,"132","12","Industrial Development Policy","Introducing the required policies, in particular the Industrial Development Policy, to move the country to a higher value chain in the regional and global economy, especially",""]],"52":[[1,"70","6","One Village One Product Movement","Continued implementing the \"One Village One Product\" movement in designated rural areas.",""],[1,"75","6","One Village One Product Awareness Workshops","Organizing workshops to raise awareness of the proven success of the concept of One Village One Product at National and Sub-National Levels.",""],[1,"75","7","OVOP Product Quality and Marketing Workshops","Organizing 7 workshops consecutively.",""],[1,"75","8","Mulberry and Silkworm Research and Development Centre","Facilitating the setting up a Research and Development Centre for mulberry planting and silkworm cultivation to promote silk production in Cambodia.",""],[1,"75","9","Kirivong OVOP Silk Production Promotion","Selecting Kirivong District of Takeo province to promote silk production as a part of OVOP movement with the development OVOP Market, OVOP Supporter's Association, and to encourage people there to plant mulberry, rear silkworm, and produce raw silk.",""],[1,"75","10","Rural Technical Training for Mulberry, Silkworm, Raw Silk, and Handicraft Production","Providing technical trainings on planting and processing such as planting mulberry, rearing silkworms and producing raw silk and handicraft improvement training to farmers at rural areas.",""],[1,"155","11","One Village, One Product Promotion Measures","To achieve RGC's priority policies related to promotion of One Village, One Product (OVOP), Council for Agriculture and Rural Development (CARD) will:","Council for Agriculture and Rural Development (CARD)"],[1,"155","12","One Village One Product Movement Strengthening","Continue strengthening the OVOP movement, including the capacity building to the relevant concerned agencies, community and institutions, developing the relevant documents to promote One Village One Product Movement.",""],[1,"155","13","One Village One Product Partnership Development","Develop the partnership with relevant institutions/organizations for promoting One Village One Product.",""],[1,"155","14","OVOP Product Quality, Packaging, and Marketing Support","Encourage the community people to produce OVOP products with high quality, decoration and marketing.",""],[1,"155","16","OVOP Pilot Projects","Develop OVOP pilot projects in eighteen provinces (6 pilot projects for 2014-2015 for 10 provinces).",""],[1,"155","17","OVOP Advocacy Campaign","Develop advocacy campaign by all kinds of media and IEC materials to promote OVOP movement at National, Sub-National and International levels.",""],[1,"156","1","Local Product Competition Award under the OVOP Movement","Develop the competition award for local product of OVOP movement in 18 target provinces.",""],[1,"156","2","OVOP Participation Promotion Initiative","Encourage the participation of youth, universities, associations, communities or relevant working groups in promoting OVOP activities.",""],[1,"156","3","OVOP Coordination, Implementation, Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","Develop the coordination mechanisms for planning, implementing, monitoring and evaluation of OVOP works.",""]],"53":[[1,"68","1","SME Registration and Fee Reduction Reform","In order to achieve these aspects, the Royal of Government has reduced minimum requirements for the registration of small and medium enterprises and the company registration fee.",""],[1,"68","1","SME Lending Expansion by Financial Institutions","Loans provided by financial institutions (microfinance institutions) to small and medium enterprises have increased considerably.",""],[1,"68","2","SME Commercial Registration Reform","The Ministry of Commerce (MOC) has taken steps to reform the commercial registration procedures for SMEs.","Ministry of Commerce (MOC)"],[1,"68","8","Factory and Handicraft Workshop Statistics and Internet System Strengthening","Promoted factory and handicraft workshops statistics in accordance with International Standard Industrial Classification and strengthened factory and handicraft workshops via internet system.",""],[1,"68","12","Factory and Handicraft Registration Procedures Regulation","Formulated Prakas on regulations and procedures (documentations) for the registration of factories and handicrafts.",""],[1,"68","13","Annual Production Reporting and Manufacturing Policy Development","Officially announced the required information to be filled in the annual production report and further plans to the handicraft-factory and enterprise owners so that the statistics of handicrafts, factories, and other enterprises can be managed and manufacturing policy can be developed.",""],[1,"69","2","SME and Manufacturing Financing Promotion Forums","the ministry cooperated with financial institutions such as the International Finance Corporation, the National Bank of Cambodia, and ADB to facilitate orientation and forums to respond and to promote financing to the SMEs and manufacturing sector.","the ministry"],[1,"69","4","Industrial and SME Support Policy Formulation","Formulating policies to support industries and SMEs:",""],[1,"69","5","SME Support through Development Partner Cooperation","Proposed a strategic development plan and encouraged SMEs through cooperation with development partners in the area of Mekong River Basin and ASEAN framework.",""],[1,"69","17","Industrial Property Rights Policy Strengthening","Formulating and implementing policies to strengthen works on industrial property rights:",""],[1,"69","24","Metrological Policy Strengthening","Formulating and implementing policies to strengthen works on metrological issues:",""],[1,"69","27","Metrology Training Dissemination Programme","Disseminated and provide trainings on metrology-related subjects for 15 provinces;",""],[1,"70","2","Industrial Intellectual Property Protection Mechanism","Strengthened mechanism of industrial right protection in order to promote industrial innovation.",""],[1,"99","20","Entrepreneurship and SME Promotion","Encourage entrepreneurship & SMEs.",""],[1,"105","10","Entrepreneurship Promotion Support Package","Promote entrepreneurship, especially among Cambodian nationals, for them to know how to operate businesses and industries.",""],[1,"105","11","SME Development Support Programme","Promote SME development by providing technologies, management services, funding, and support infrastructure.",""]],"54":[[1,"179","3","Development of Cambodian Standards for Products and Systems","Developing Cambodian Standards for products and systems based on the demand in the national, regions, and international markets.",""],[1,"179","4","Standards Law Enforcement and Inspection Strengthening","Formulating legal documents to enforce Law on Cambodia Standards, enhancing inspections and take up other tasks.",""],[1,"179","5","Trade Standardization Awareness Campaigns","Increasing promotional campaigns to raise awareness on standardization, compliance assessment, and technical barriers on trade.",""],[1,"179","6","Product and System Certification Issuance","Promoting the issuance of Product and System Certificate.",""],[1,"179","7","Product and System Certification Unit Establishment","Seeking concurrence from international institutions for Cambodia to issue Product and System Certification Unit and building the capacity of the National Recognition Assessment Unit of the Cambodia Standard Institute.",""],[1,"179","10","Metrology Development Improvement through National Center of Metrology","Improving the effectiveness of metrological development ... through National Center of Metrology:",""],[1,"179","11","Metrology Standards and Verification Strengthening","Supporting and promoting the activities of the metrological legalization and metrological science through strengthening the management of the metrological standards, verification of metrological devices, produced items and packed items, calibration, type approval, testing, analysis to protect the benefits of the suppliers and consumers and ensure the fairness in commercial activities.",""],[1,"179","12","Metrological Registration and Licensing Support","Promoting the activities of metrological registration, issuance of metrological trademark use license, issuance of license for producing and repairing metrological devices to contribute to market expansion and make the Cambodian products more credible.",""],[1,"179","13","Metrology Promotion and Awareness Support","Supporting and increasing the promotion of the metrology and its benefits to contribute to promoting the development of all sectors as well as poverty alleviation of Cambodian people.",""]],"55":[[1,"59","11","Private Sector Enabling Environment and Investment Promotion Measures","To implement RGC priority policies for the Fourth Legislature, the highest priority of all concerned RGC institutions was to support the creation of an enabling environment that fosters private sector development by taking measures to alleviate major bottlenecks for private sector development.",""],[1,"59","12","Investor One-Stop Service Mechanism","The Cambodian Investment Board of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CIB/CDC) has operated a \"One Stop Service\" for investors for many years in order to reduce the administrative burden of seeking RGC's approval for new investment projects.","Cambodian Investment Board of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CIB/CDC)"],[1,"60","1","Investor Aftercare Mechanism","and a new \"Investor Aftercare\" mechanism, as well as, an \"Investor Tracking System\" was developed and implemented.",""],[1,"60","1","Investor Tracking System","and a new \"Investor Aftercare\" mechanism, as well as, an \"Investor Tracking System\" was developed and implemented.",""],[1,"60","1","Investment Promotion and Private Sector Competitiveness Coordination","The CIB/CDC and the Ministry of Commerce will continue to actively promote new investments in the priority economic sectors to diversify and broaden the economic base, develop and widely disseminate information on investment opportunities in priority sectors, and strengthen coordination between concerned RGC institutions to promote a sense of joint responsibility for enhancing the competitiveness of the private sector.","The CIB/CDC | the Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"60","2","Special Economic Zones Implementation Strengthening","The Council for the Development of Cambodia continued strengthening the implementation of the Special Economic Zones (SEZ)",""],[1,"60","2","SEZ Location Suitability and Integration Planning","and ensuring that the locations of the SEZs were suitable for maximizing the integration of Cambodian economy into the region.",""],[1,"60","3","Government-Private Sector Coordination Mechanism Strengthening","The Royal Government continued exploring new ways to further strengthen this Government-Private Sector coordination mechanism and to build public-private partnerships.",""],[1,"62","6","Trade Sector Programme Implementation Strengthening","Strengthened the implementation of the Trade Sector Programme that is based on a sector-wide approach, focusing on trade facilitation and private sector development.",""],[1,"69","3","Government-Private Sector Forum Partnership Mechanism","Strengthened partnership with private sector and development partners through implementing programs and activities with the framework of the Government- Private Sector Forum.",""],[1,"97","14","Competitiveness Improvement for Investment Attraction","Creating more jobs, especially for the youth, through further improvement in Cambodia's competitiveness to attract and encourage both domestic and foreign investments.",""],[1,"99","19","Private Investment and Trade Promotion","Facilitate and promote private investment and trade.",""],[1,"104","21","Private Investment Promotion and Enabling Business Environment Reform","RGC is committed to ensuring an enabling business and investment environment for private investment as well as to making Cambodia an attractive destination for investments.",""],[1,"105","4","Economic Openness and Investment Integration Initiative","Continue to open the economy and integrate it into the region and the world, to open business and investment opportunities to entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"105","9","Foreign Investment Attraction and Investor Support Services","Focus on attracting foreign investments and enhancing support services to the existing investments.",""],[1,"107","1","Business Environment Improvement for Foreign Investment","business environment to attract foreign investment, encouraged transfer of technology, and widened the export markets.",""],[1,"115","4","Investment Attraction for Job Creation","Creating more jobs for people especially the youth through further improvement in Cambodia's competitiveness to attract and encourage both domestic and foreign investments.",""],[1,"128","12","Investment Environment and Trade Facilitation Reform Package","Increase the effectiveness of the implementation of reforms related to investment environment and trade facilitation, including fighting corruption, reducing unnecessary bureaucracy, implementing Legal and Judicial Reform and Public Administration Reform, and strengthening the rule of law.",""],[1,"130","3","Private Investment Regime Review","Review the private investment regime to provide suitable incentives for long-term development.",""],[1,"130","5","Investment Facilitation and One-Stop Service Mechanism","Create a conducive environment for receiving domestic and foreign investment, including facilitating registration and providing licenses and other permission letters [especially through the One-Stop Service Mechanism to accelerate operations related to business and investment and to reduce the informal expenses].",""],[1,"132","8","Investment Attraction and Export Diversification Package","RGC will continue focusing on attracting investments from both domestic and foreign sources, diversifying the production base, expanding export markets, promoting transport connectivity and logistics systems, improving the regulatory framework, strengthening institutional mechanisms including conflict resolution mechanisms, and enhancing capacity building to ensure favorable environment for Cambodia's development.",""],[1,"173","5","Private Sector Legal and Regulatory Framework Strengthening","the RGC will continue to strengthen the legal framework for the private sector (laws and regulations, administrative procedures) to improve productivity.",""],[1,"173","10","Investment Climate and Regulatory Reform","Further strengthening favorable investment and business climate through improvement in regulatory framework, rationalization of incentives for investment projects, and improvements in good governance and efficiency of public institutions including the strengthening of \"Single Window\" mechanism of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC).",""],[1,"174","2","Government-Private Sector Forum Strengthening and Upgrade","Strengthening the effectiveness of \"Government-Private Sector Forum\" to address the challenges faced by the private sector, while upgrading it to a platform for dialogue for recommending policy options and advice that will further promote the role of private sector as a stakeholder in development.",""],[1,"174","3","Investment Aftercare Services Strengthening","Strengthening \"investment aftercare services\" to address in a timely manner investor issues and concerns.",""],[1,"174","4","Monitoring and Evaluation System Strengthening for Investment Projects","Strengthening the monitoring and evaluation system in implementing investment projects to ensure compliance with stipulated principles and conditions.",""],[1,"174","7","Investor One-Stop Service and Investment Promotion","CIB/CDC has operated a \"one stop service\" for investors for many years for new investments.","Cambodian Investment Board (CIB) of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CIB/CDC) | Ministry of Commerce (MOC)"],[1,"175","17","Foreign Investment Attraction Initiative","Attract foreign investments.",""]],"57":[[1,"91","2","Customs Regulation Alignment","Customs regulations, consistent with the international practices, have now been put in place.",""],[1,"101","7","Customs Administration Modernization","Strengthen and improve the customs administration by encouraging the use of Automated System for Customs Data (ASYCUDA) and fully implementation the Trade Facilitation Policy and a Single Counter System.",""],[1,"128","9","Single Window Export Facilitation and Approval Streamlining","Facilitate exports (especially agri-exports) through a 'Single Window' payment, and streamline the approval process.",""],[1,"128","13","Export Market Diversification and Trade Integration","Continue promoting trade through diversifying export markets and accelerating the speed of integration in the free trade framework of ASEAN and the world.",""],[1,"129","6","Customs Administration Modernization and Trade Facilitation Policy Implementation","Improve customs administration by encouraging the ASYCUDA System and urge a full implementation of the Trade Facilitation Policy.",""],[1,"132","7","Trade Liberalization and Market Access Promotion","RGC will make further strides on the path of trade liberalization, aimed at free movement of goods and services within the country and between Cambodia and her trade partners.",""],[1,"132","7","Promotion of Cambodian Products in Regional and Global Markets","RGC will continue promoting access to Cambodian products in the regional and world markets, thereby creating more jobs, and fueling economic growth.",""],[1,"133","3","Export Market Expansion and Product Diversification Measures","Taking measures to increase Cambodia's export market through product diversification; negotiate to open up new markets with other countries within and outside the region;",""],[1,"133","3","Non-Tariff Barrier Compliance Support","comply with the non-tariff barriers such as standards, and sanitary and phyto-sanitary standards (SPS).",""]],"58":[[1,"98","17","Industrial Development Policy","the two central policies that the government intends following are, a Promotion of Paddy Production and Rice Export Policy and an Industrial Development Policy",""],[1,"99","12","Industrial Development and Rice Intensification Policy Implementation","Implement Industrial Development Policy (IDP) and Rice intensification policy",""],[1,"99","21","Implementation of IDP Promotions and Regulations","Implement all the promotions & regulations of IDP and Rice Export Policy.",""],[1,"99","21","Rubber Export Policy Rollout","Roll out the Rubber Export Policy.",""],[1,"106","3","Industrial Development Policy","The Industrial Development Policy (IDP) aims to promote industrial growth with an emphasis on diversifying the production base, creating more non-farm jobs, improving competitiveness, upgrading technologies, and linking the sector with the regional and international value chains.",""],[1,"106","5","Large-Scale Industrial Enterprise Development","RGC aims at setting up new large-scale industrial enterprises, targeting at least 5 big projects each year.",""],[1,"106","5","Manufacturing Export Expansion","The government also targets to increase the manufacturing export (other than garments) to exceed 10% of the total exports value.",""],[1,"106","7","Industrial Corridor and Special Economic Zone Development","In the first phase, the approach will be established (and strengthening) industrial corridors and SEZs",""],[1,"107","1","Long-Term Industrial Growth Linkage Strategy","In the third phase, the aim would be on maintaining a long-term industrial growth through improved linkages with foreign enterprises.",""],[1,"127","4","Export Base Diversification Initiative","diversifying the export base of the Cambodian economy to align with regional and global demand;",""],[1,"128","8","Economic Diversification and Export Competitiveness Policy","Continue to implement economic diversification policies based on competitiveness of the Cambodian economy and link the economy with regional production value chain with special attention on increasing rice production and milled rice for export, raising manufacturing and agro-industry products also for export, and furthering the Tourism Development Plan 2011-2020.",""],[1,"173","7","Investment Promotion in Modern High-Value Industrial Sectors","Promoting investments in modern and high value added industrial sectors aimed at upgrading the diversification of the manufacturing base.",""],[1,"173","9","Local Enterprise Modernization and Innovation Linkage Initiative","Further promoting the modernization of local enterprises and improved innovation capacity as well as strengthened links between local enterprises and domestic industries with foreign investment projects, aimed at promoting transfer of technology, knowledge and know-how, increasing productivity, and enhancing attractiveness and competitiveness of Cambodia.",""],[1,"173","12","Physical Infrastructure Investment and Special Economic Zone Development","Increasing investments in physical infrastructure including improvements in services and means to facilitate and support business processes and further strengthening and developing special economic zones.",""],[1,"174","5","Agro-processing and Assembly Industry Promotion Policy","RGC will promote a favorable climate for developing the agro-processing industry and assembling industry (both electronic and machinery assembly).",""],[1,"174","5","Special Economic Zones Legal Framework Enhancement","RGC will enhance the legal framework for creating the law for efficient operations of Special Economic Zones.",""],[1,"174","8","Special Economic Zones Implementation Strengthening","CDC will further strengthen the implementation of the Special Economic Zones (SEZ) and will ensure that the SEZ's locations are suitable for maximizing the integration of Cambodia's economy into the region.",""],[1,"177","10","Industrial Base Diversification and SME Development","RGC continue promoting further diversification of the industrial base through encouraging investments in new high value added and competitive industries, including assembly of electronics, spare parts manufacture, metrological industry, agro-processing and other manufacturing industries, while also promoting further development of SMEs and handicrafts and expanding industrial development into rural areas.",""],[1,"177","11","Industrial Development Policy Formulation","Formulating industrial development policy based on two key approaches: (1) expansion of industrial base supported by increased attractiveness of Cambodia to investors and investment promotion including modernization of SMEs; and (2) improved connectivity with regional production networks to integrate with and move up the global value chains.",""],[1,"177","13","SME Development Framework Update and Support Package","Updating the SMEs Development Framework to be consistent with the industrial development policy aimed at enhancing SME's capacity to link with large enterprises and form a cluster while promoting entrepreneurship, productivity, creativity, innovation and specialization through introduction and implementation of a comprehensive package of supporting measures including clustering, enhanced technology transfer, increased access to finance, strengthened technical standards, establishment of business development counseling centers, promotion of \"one village one product\" movement and improvement of regulatory framework as well as strengthened institutional coordination.",""],[1,"177","14","Industrial Cluster and Special Economic Zone Investment Promotion","Aligning private sector development and investment policies with SME and industrial development policy especially by encouraging investment in industrial clusters and industrial parks through promoting the adoption of Law on Special Economic Zones, in order to upgrade management, infrastructure and operations in the industrial sector to international standards.",""]],"59":[[1,"99","12","Infrastructure Investment Expansion","Invest more on Infrastructure (irrigation, transport, electricity, water, sanitation, public services, others).",""],[1,"99","20","Infrastructure Expansion and Connectivity Development","Expand electrification, telecommunication, roads, rural roads, railways, (sea & river), ports, irrigation.",""],[1,"102","1","Physical Infrastructure Improvement and Maintenance Programme","improvement and maintenance of physical infrastructure such as roads, railways, ports, irrigation, power, clean water supply, schools, hospitals, and so on.",""],[1,"102","9","Infrastructure Financing Diversification","Diversify financing sources to the maximum to respond to an increase in expenditures on physical infrastructure.",""]],"60":[[1,"32","3","Insurance Sector Regulatory Capacity Strengthening","Strengthened capacity of the insurance service providers through regulations to ensure sustainable development of insurance sector in accordance with the rules of the International Association of Insurance Supervisors (IAIS).",""],[1,"33","4","Information Technology System for Mortgage Operations","Professionalism has been encouraged in mortgage operations using information technology system for regulators, operators, and authorities.",""],[1,"33","5","Banking Infrastructure Strengthening and Payment System Modernization","The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has helped improve the banking infrastructure by strengthening the legal frameworks, setting up the National Payment System, and establishing the Credit Bureau.",""],[1,"33","8","Banking Information System and Payment System Modernization","A well-organized institutional infrastructure is required, e.g. that having an efficient information system for banking operations, harmonization of legal and regulatory frameworks, and a wider use of the Payment System.",""],[1,"178","19","National Settlement System Implementation","Continuing to implement the national settlement system and promoting financial product development.",""],[1,"178","19","Financial Product Development Promotion","Continuing to implement the national settlement system and promoting financial product development.",""],[1,"178","20","Financial Environment Improvement for Private Investment and Domestic Capital Market Development","Continuing to improve the financial environment for attracting private investment and establishing a domestic capital market.",""],[1,"183","5","Financial Sector Development Reform","The Royal Government of the Fifth Legislature aims to further develop the financial sector to be more broad-based, diversified, deepened, sound and effective, based on market principles to support sustainable economic growth and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"183","6","Financial Sector Development Strategy Implementation","RGC will further promote effective and successful implementation of the \"Financial Sector Development Strategy 2011-2020\", particularly focusing on:",""],[1,"183","7","Financial Sector Regulatory and Supervisory Capacity Strengthening","Further developing and coordinating implementation of policy and regulatory frameworks, particularly in strengthening regulation and supervision mechanisms, institutional and human resource capacity in line with Cambodia's economic development and in response to the need for Cambodia's financial system to integrate with the regional and global financial system.",""],[1,"183","8","Crisis Prevention and Resolution Mechanism","Continued development of a crisis prevention and resolution mechanism including an early-warning system through improved institutional coordination especially consideration of the need to establish a national financial stability board.",""],[1,"183","9","Financial Infrastructure Strengthening and Development","Further strengthening and developing effective financial infrastructure that includes a payment system, introduction of money market/interbank market, and promotion of use of international best practices in accounting and corporate governance.",""],[1,"183","10","Banking and Microfinance Regulatory and Supervision Reform","Further supporting growth in banking and microfinance sectors to promote financial inclusion, focusing on improved registration and licensing as well as supervision systems so as to render them simple, transparent, accountable and effective especially Microfinance Institutions, while further diversifying financial tools and financial products such as financial leasing and risk sharing schemes' operations.",""],[1,"183","12","Compulsory Insurance Expansion and New Product Development","Further strengthening and expanding the scope of compulsory insurance and developing new products especially in life and micro insurance through development and improvement in regulatory frameworks along with strengthened capacity of the insurance regulator.",""],[1,"183","13","Securities Market Development and IPO Promotion","Further developing the securities market, encouraging firms and companies to launch their Initial Public Offerings (IPOs) in the market while improving trading facilities, and considering the need to issue government securities.",""],[1,"183","15","Non-Bank Financial Subsector Development","Further developing and strengthening other components of the non-bank financial subsector such as trust funds and real estate markets as well as pawn shops.",""],[1,"183","16","Financial Center Feasibility Exploration","Further exploring the possibility to establish a financial center.",""],[1,"184","1","Monetary Policy for Price and Financial Stability","Implement monetary policy to maintain price stability and contribute to financial stability.",""],[1,"184","2","Riel Usage and De-dollarization Promotion","Promote utilizing Riels and reduce dollarization; promote utilizing Riel investment tools such as treasury cards and debt-cards.",""],[1,"184","3","Bank Supervision Strengthening","Facilitate financial regulators to strengthen monitoring of banks.",""],[1,"184","4","Risk-Based Monitoring Method","Put in place the Risk-Based Monitoring Method.",""],[1,"184","5","Crisis Prevention and Resolution Mechanism","Contribute to creating Crisis-Prevention and Resolution Mechanism.",""],[1,"184","6","Bilateral SWAPS Contract Implementation","Be ready to implement bilateral SWAPS contract and the Chiangmai Initiative on Multi- Lateral Debt Mechanism.",""],[1,"184","6","Chiang Mai Initiative Multilateral Debt Mechanism","Be ready to implement bilateral SWAPS contract and the Chiangmai Initiative on Multi- Lateral Debt Mechanism.",""],[1,"184","8","Inter-Bank and Money Market Development","Put in place an inter-bank market and money market development.",""],[1,"184","13","Insurance Sector Conflict-Resolution Mechanism","Create a conflict-resolution mechanism for the insurance sector.",""],[1,"184","14","Pre-Notification Risk Warning System","Put in place a pre-notifying system for risks, using information technology.",""],[1,"184","19","IT-Based Financial Transactions System","Develop a strong IT-based financial transactions system.",""],[1,"184","20","Development of Securities Markets","Develop a debt-security market, a state security market, a corporation license market, and other security markets.",""],[1,"184","21","Debt Security Management Framework and Credit-Rating Agency","Create a management framework and Credit-Rating Agency to support selling of debt security.",""],[1,"184","22","Commodity Futures Exchange Feasibility Study","Study the feasibility of establishing a Commodity Future Exchange.",""],[1,"184","23","Bankruptcy Legal Standards Reform","Formulate and put in place legal standards related to bankruptcy.",""],[1,"184","24","Supporting Financial and Security Infrastructure Systems","Build a supporting infrastructure, such as a security keeping system, security verifying and clearing system, and cash clearing system.",""],[1,"184","25","Financial Instruments Diversification and Investment Mechanisms for Securities Market Development","Continue promoting financial instruments diversification and investment mechanisms to develop the security market.",""],[1,"184","26","Master Investment Program for Non-Banking Institutions","Encourage non-banking institution operations to be brought under a master investment program for mobilizing investments.",""],[1,"184","27","Financial Development Center","Establish a Financial Development Center to attract financial flows.",""],[1,"184","28","Regulatory IT Information-Sharing System Strengthening","Continue strengthening the IT system for regulators to sharing information.",""],[1,"184","29","Regulator and Market Participant Training Programme","Continue to educate and train regulators and other participants on expertise in security market and other aspects of finance.",""]],"61":[[1,"103","16","Insurance Industry Development and Coverage Expansion","Accelerate the development of the insurance industry by spreading the coverage of insurance services including life insurance widely.",""],[1,"103","17","Insurance Sector Capital Mobilization for Financial Market Investment","Encourage the flow of capital from the insurance sector to the mainstream financial markets for investments.",""],[1,"104","4","Actuarial Science Training Institution","Establish an institution for the study of Actuary Science.",""]],"62":[[1,"100","12","Rural Affordable Loan and Market Access Expansion","Expand access to affordable loans, & markets for rural people.",""],[1,"103","13","Microfinance Sector Strengthening and SME Lending Support","Continue strengthening the micro finance sector to mobilize savings from the depositors and channel them into the mainstream, improve their financial effectiveness and sustainability and at the same time provide loans to small and tiny enterprises and other self-employed workers.",""],[1,"103","14","Microfinance Services Expansion Programme","Expand the coverage of microfinance services across the country and widely disseminate their benefits to the people.",""],[1,"103","15","Pro-Poor Lending Orientation for Providers","Keep orienting the providers towards their focus of lending to the poor at reasonable interest rates and without imposing debilitating conditions.",""],[1,"104","1","Small and Micro Insurance Scheme Expansion","Encourage small/micro insurance schemes to meet the demands of the people with modest incomes and for people living in areas not effectively served by the banking/financial sector.",""]],"63":[[1,"183","11","Microfinance Expansion for Rural Poor, Farmers, and SMEs","Exerting more effort to expand microfinance services with affordable prices and better terms and conditions, especially targeting the poor and agricultural communities to promote the rural economy, and further expand credit to SMEs.",""],[1,"184","9","Micro-Finance Sector Expansion","Scale up the Micro-Finance Sector and broaden the coverage of micro-financial services.",""],[1,"184","10","Microfinance System Strengthening","Continue to strengthen micro-finance system for it to be stronger, more effective, and more beneficial to the poor with reasonable, acceptable financial service fee.",""],[1,"184","11","Insurance Route Capital Inflow Promotion","Attract capital in-flow through the insurance route into the finance market.",""],[1,"184","12","Small-Scale Insurance for Low-Income People","Encourage small-scale insurance to meet the demands of low-income people.",""]],"64":[[1,"103","5","Monetary Policy for Price and Financial Stability","Implement the monetary policy to maintain price stability and contribute to financial stability.",""],[1,"103","6","Riel Promotion and Dollarization Reduction Policy","Promote utilizing the Riel and reducing dollarization.",""],[1,"103","7","Promotion of Riel-Denominated Investment Instruments","Promote utilizing Riel-denominated investment instruments such as treasury bills and debit cards.",""],[1,"103","9","Debt Swap Mechanism for Currency Stabilization and Debt Management","Implement debt swap-mechanisms for stabilizing the currency and debt management.",""],[1,"127","6","Prudent and Flexible Monetary Policy","Pursuing a prudent and flexible monetary policy including a more vigilant management of capital flows to help safeguard macro-economic stability and create a conducive environment for development; ensuring an increase in international reserves; continuing to implement a managed float exchange rate regime to maintain stability of the Riel and strengthen public and investor confidence of the local currency to promote its greater use and reduce the high level of dollarization; strengthening and ensuring stability of the financial system especially that of banking system to be accomplished through making it more efficient, integrated and competitive, strengthened supervision and management of liquidity, credit and market risks in compliance with international standards.",""]],"65":[[1,"103","8","Banking Sector Prudential Monitoring System","Facilitate financial regulators to strengthen monitoring of the banking sector by putting in place a system to prevent banking institutions from over-stretching and thereby defaulting.",""],[1,"103","11","Deposit Assurance Capacity Improvement","Improve the ability of the central bank and other banks to offer full assurance to deposits.",""],[1,"103","12","Inter-bank Lending System and Money Market Development","Put in place an inter-bank lending system and promote money market development.",""]],"66":[[1,"104","8","Debt and Securities Market Development","Develop a debt security market(including state security market), a corporate license market, and other security markets.",""],[1,"104","9","Debt Securities Management Framework and Credit Rating Agency","Create a Management Framework and Credit Rating Agency to oversee the sales of debt securities.",""],[1,"104","10","Commodity Futures Exchange Feasibility Study","Study the feasibility of establishing a Commodity Futures Exchange.",""],[1,"104","11","Corporate Governance Strengthening in Securities","Promote and strengthen implementation of good corporate governance in securities.",""],[1,"104","14","Diversification of Financial Tools and Investment Mechanisms","Continue promoting diversification of financial tools and investment mechanisms.",""],[1,"104","19","Investor, Reporter, and Market Observer Training Programme","Continue educating and train the investors, reporters and market observers.",""],[1,"104","20","Regulators and Market Participant Training Programme","Continue educating and train the regulators and other participants to have better expertise on security markets.",""]],"67":[[1,"214","2","Domestic Private Sector Financing Measures","RGC will also implement measures to encourage financing of the (domestic) private sector from the domestic financial sector.",""],[1,"214","2","Promotion of New Financial Instruments","there are a number of new financial instruments being promoted for channeling private savings into investments.",""]],"69":[[1,"30","4","Tax Administration Legal and Digital Modernization","The General Directorate of Taxation developed and implemented several legal letters, especially regulation on Tax on Property.","General Directorate of Taxation"],[1,"30","4","Expansion of the Automatic Declaration System","The General Directorate of Taxation also expanded its Automatic Declaration System in all provinces, and recruited and trained more than 300 new customs officers.","General Directorate of Taxation"],[1,"30","4","Customs Regulation Modernization","Customs regulations, which are consistent with the international practices were also developed and implemented.",""],[1,"30","4","Trade Facilitation and Customs-Private Sector Partnership Mechanism","Trade Facilitation and Customs-Private Sector Partnership Mechanism are now functional, and the Customs Database Automatic System has been put in place at 20 international checkpoints, covering nearly the entire customs operation.",""],[1,"30","4","Customs Risk and Business Credibility Management Systems","The Customs Risk Database Management System and Creditability of Businessmen Management System were developed and operated.",""],[1,"61","6","National Single Window for Trade Facilitation","Cambodia planned to establish a National Single Window by 2018, which should help improve on these two issues.",""]],"70":[[1,"105","14","Irrigation System Improvement","there is need to improve the irrigation systems",""],[1,"105","14","Modern Cultivation Inputs and Techniques Programme","apply superior techniques of cultivation including modern/scientific inputs",""],[1,"105","14","Low-Cost Agricultural Transport Support","promote low-cost transport",""],[1,"105","14","Paddy Collection and Storage Facilities","establish paddy collection and storage facilities",""],[1,"105","14","Paddy Processing Capacity Expansion","expand paddy processing capacity (at internationally comparable costs)",""],[1,"105","14","Agricultural Logistics and Quality Control Systems","set up logistics systems and quality control mechanisms",""],[1,"105","14","Phyto-Sanitary Standards Compliance","adhere to phyto sanitation standards",""],[1,"105","14","Agricultural Financing System Development","set up sound financing systems for the whole process",""],[1,"106","1","Agricultural Irrigation Infrastructure Investment","further investing in irrigation infrastructure and rationalizing its utilization;",""],[1,"106","1","Paddy Collection and Storage Improvement","improving paddy collection and storage facilities;",""],[1,"106","1","Agricultural Regulatory Framework Reform","improving the regulatory framework for seed production, import of agricultural inputs, contract farming, agricultural land-use, water-user associations, and human resource development in this sector.",""]],"71":[[1,"135","16","Agricultural Cooperative Establishment and Strengthening","Establishing and strengthening agricultural cooperative:",""],[1,"135","18","Agricultural Cooperative Development and Capacity Strengthening","Developing principles for agricultural cooperative development and promoting, establishing and strengthening the capacity of agricultural cooperatives.",""],[1,"135","21","Model Infrastructure for Cooperatives","Building a model infrastructure for cooperatives.",""],[1,"135","23","Agricultural Product Exhibition Promotion","Promoting agricultural product exhibitions at national, provincial and district levels.",""],[1,"136","3","Stakeholder Networking for Agricultural Machinery Value Chains","Promoting networks between researchers, traders, manufacturers, agricultural machinery sellers and farmers' cooperative.",""],[1,"136","5","National Agricultural Product Standards Development","Developing national standards for agricultural products.",""],[1,"136","6","Laboratory Services Strengthening for Quality and Product Safety","Strengthening laboratory services for quality and product safety.",""],[1,"136","7","Produce Quality Inspection and Monitoring Strengthening","Strengthening research and monitoring on produce quality through inspections.",""],[1,"136","10","Crop Protection and Phytosanitary Law Reform","Furthering the drafted law on crop protection and phyto-sanitary law and the on land management and utilization.",""],[1,"136","11","Crop Management and Farmers' Cooperative Legislation","Developing legislation on crop management, copyright of breeders and farmers' cooperatives.",""],[1,"138","9","Agricultural Product Processing Information Systems","Establish information systems on processing agricultural products.",""],[1,"138","10","Technical Support to Rural Areas","Provide technical support to rural areas.",""]],"72":[[1,"133","6","Agricultural Modernization and Commercialization Programme","RGC's vision is to modernize Cambodia's agriculture based on a new approach and with changed scope and pace, to transform this sector from primarily depending on expanded use of available resources (such as land and other natural resources) and traditional agricultural inputs, into one which primarily depends on the application of techniques, new technologies, mechanization and irrigation to improve the yield rate, and diversify activities into high value crops, livestock, and aquaculture in an environmentally sustainable manner.",""],[1,"133","10","Agricultural Productivity, Diversification and Commercialization Support","The Royal Government will focus on:",""],[1,"134","1","Agricultural Productivity Enhancement and Support Services Programme","Further improving the productivity of all crops by strengthening and expanding sustained extension services and market information; extending the outreach of the supporting services structure to local levels and linking them to the concerned networks and other stakeholders; promoting R&D for productivity improvement and adaptation to climate change; promoting production and use of quality seeds; further investing in irrigation and rationalizing water use; improving collection and storage facilities; and preparing and improving the regulatory framework for seed production, import of agricultural inputs, contract farming, agricultural land-use, water-user associations, as well as human resource development in this sector.",""],[1,"134","2","Agricultural Diversification and Innovation Promotion","Further promoting agricultural diversification through promotion of R&D; disseminating new crops having potential for production expansion and exports; strengthening the environment to attract private investment, especially in research, production and distribution of seeds, and agro-processing; intensifying cooperation with all stakeholders, aimed at transfer of \"knowledge and know-how\"; and promoting the use of agricultural machinery.",""],[1,"134","3","Agricultural Commercialization and Export Promotion Measures","Further promoting commercialization through implementing laws and policies and strengthening institutional arrangements to promote trade and export of agricultural products, including effective implementation of the law on agricultural cooperatives, enhanced processing capacity, further improvement in trade facilitation including \"one- stop services\", strengthened logistics system, enhanced quality of agricultural products according to international standards, improved capacity to provide affordable credit, and enhanced partnership between farmers and traders and between large- scale agro-industries and household farming.",""],[1,"134","4","Promotion of Paddy Production and Rice Export Policy Implementation","RGC will further promote the implementation of the \"Policy on the Promotion of Paddy Production and Rice Export\"",""],[1,"134","6","Holder-Based Agriculture Support Programme","Promote special programs to promote holder-based agriculture, which include access to adequate financial and non-financial services for these farmers, access to markets and a regulatory framework for crop-based collateral borrowing.",""],[1,"134","14","Good Quality Seed Introduction and Rice Variety Renewal Review","Enhancing introduction of good quality seeds and reviewing the renewal of 10 rice varieties that not matches to the real situation of Cambodia.",""],[1,"135","1","Integrated Crop Management Knowledge Strengthening","Enhancing and strengthening the knowledge of crop protection and yield improvement through integrated crop management system.",""],[1,"135","3","Good Agricultural Practice Promotion","Promoting Good Agricultural Practice (GAP) to ensure quality of the products and safety standards.",""],[1,"135","7","Agricultural Extension Strengthening","Strengthening agricultural extension work at the commune and village level.",""],[1,"135","8","Agricultural Extension Service Guide Development","Developing guides on agricultural extension service.",""],[1,"135","10","Commune-Level Agricultural Centers","Creating Agricultural Centers at the commune level.",""],[1,"135","14","Agricultural Extension Information Dissemination","Scaling-up agricultural technology information through publishing and distributing agricultural extension booklets through public media and other public forums.",""],[1,"135","15","Tele-Center Establishment and Operation","Creating and running Tele-Center at the district and commune levels.",""],[1,"135","36","Agricultural Machinery Selection and Supply-Chain Improvement","Selecting appropriate agricultural machinery for Cambodia and improving agricultural machinery supply-chain, and improving users' skills, especially for reducing costs.",""],[1,"135","37","Agricultural Machinery Service and Technology Use Capacity Building","Providing agricultural machinery service through enhanced knowledge on technology use among farmers, manufacturers and service providers.",""],[1,"136","13","Farmer Capacity Building in Modern Farming Practices","Promoting capacities of farmers in modern farming practices, farm diversification, 'farming systems' approaches, and aspects of finances and markets.",""],[1,"136","13","Farm Diversification Support","Promoting capacities of farmers in modern farming practices, farm diversification, 'farming systems' approaches, and aspects of finances and markets.",""],[1,"136","13","Farming Systems Approach Promotion","Promoting capacities of farmers in modern farming practices, farm diversification, 'farming systems' approaches, and aspects of finances and markets.",""],[1,"136","15","Rice Breeding for Stress-Resilient Varieties","Breeding to improve rice varieties for abiotic and biotic stresses, yield and quality, in rain-fed lowlands.",""],[1,"136","16","Breeding Early-Maturing Rice Varieties","Breeding to improve very early / early maturing rice varieties tolerant to BPH (Brown plant hoppers) and bacterial leaf blight disease (Santhomonasoryzaepvoryzae).",""],[1,"136","17","Crop Breeding for High-Yielding Varieties","Breeding to develop high-yielding variety legumes, maize, mango, and vegetables.",""],[1,"136","23","Cost-Effective Technology Packages for Cropping Systems","Develop cost-effective technology packages for viable cropping systems in lowlands (rain-fed and fully irrigated) and uplands.",""],[1,"137","6","Agricultural ICT, Awareness, Training, and Knowledge Transfer Initiative","Improving Information Communication Technology (ICT), public awareness, training course, and knowledge transfer, to improving farmers' livelihoods.",""],[1,"137","7","Researcher and Extension Worker Capacity-Building Training","Strengthening the capacity and skills of researchers and extension workers through in- country and overseas training courses.",""],[1,"172","12","Agricultural Productivity Enhancement and Competitiveness Improvement","Enforcement of Agricultural: Enhancement of Agricultural Productivity: Improves the agricultural competitiveness and leads the green growth through improving the agricultural productivity and securing the diversity.",""]],"73":[[1,"137","9","Sustainable Freshwater and Marine Fisheries Management Measures","At the same time RGC would continue implementing measures aimed at ensuring sustainability of both freshwater and marine fishery resources.",""],[1,"146","6","Fishing Community Resource Management Support","RGC will continue to attach high priority to encouraging fishing communities to participate in managing the natural resources by providing guidance and technical training.",""],[1,"146","6","Fishing Lot Demarcation","the Royal Government will ensure the proper demarcation of the fishing lots.",""],[1,"146","7","Efficient Fish Market Mechanism","RGC will establish an efficient fish market mechanism.",""],[1,"146","8","Enforcement Against Illegal Encroachment and Illegal Fishing","RGC will continue to take action against illegal encroachment of flooded forests, use of illegal fishing gears, and all anarchic activities preventing the conservation efforts.",""],[1,"146","9","Aquaculture Support Package for Fish Farmers","RGC will provide a package of assistance to the fish farmers, including technology, seed, credit and market.",""],[1,"146","9","Law Enforcement Improvement Through Existing Mechanism","Improvement in law enforcement through the existing mechanism will continue to be the priority.",""],[1,"146","10","Sustainable Fisheries Resource Management Programme","The Fisheries Administration (FIA) will focus its efforts to strengthen the management, conservation, and development of sustainable fishery resources.",""],[1,"146","10","Ten Year SPF Implementation","FiA will continue to implement the Ten Year SPF 2010-2019, following three development pillars, namely:",""],[1,"147","10","Prime Minister's Recommendations on Water-Based Fisheries","Continue to implement the Prime Minister's Recommendations \"where there is water there is fish\".",""],[1,"147","11","Research and Development Continuation","Continue research and development.",""],[1,"147","15","Fish Processing Loss Reduction Initiative","Reduce losses in fish processing and wastage especially in small-scale fish processing.",""],[1,"147","18","Flooded-Forest Boundary Demarcation and Protection Works","Demarking boundaries and installing poles to protect flooded-forests.",""]],"74":[[1,"99","21","Agricultural, Livestock, and Fish Extension Services Strengthening","Strengthen agricultural, livestock/fish extension services.",""],[1,"99","23","Industrial and Agricultural Database Strengthening","Strengthen industrial & agricultural database.",""],[1,"99","24","Industrial and Agricultural Research Linkage Programme","Promote Industrial and Agricultural Research linked to industry (& other stakeholders).",""],[1,"106","1","Agricultural Extension and Market Information Strengthening","Further strengthening, expanding and ensuring the sustainability of extension services and market information; extending the outreach of supporting services to the local/farm levels and linking the services to different stakeholders;",""],[1,"106","1","Agricultural Research and Development for Productivity and Climate Adaptation","promoting Research and Development for productivity improvement, and adaptation to changes in the climate;",""],[1,"106","1","Quality and High-Yield Seed Promotion","promoting production and use of quality/high yielding variety seeds;",""],[1,"135","2","Agricultural Research and Post-Harvest Technology Promotion","Promoting research and development, and promoting the use of pre and post-harvest technology to maintain quality and reduce losses.",""],[1,"135","4","Pest Control and Crop Disaster Protection Measures","Strengthening interventions to get rid of pests and secure the crop from natural disasters.",""],[1,"136","1","Agricultural Research and Development in Pre- and Post-Harvest Technologies","Promoting research and development in pre- and post-harvest technologies using machinery.",""],[1,"136","18","Seed Production System Enhancement","Enhancing seed production systems and utilizing seeds that CARDI has released.",""],[1,"136","19","Sustainable Land Management and Crop Nutrient Research","Conduct research to develop technologies and approaches towards sustainable land management and determine plant nutrient requirements for rice-based cropping systems (1. EWS+WS, 2. Recession + Pre-rising water, and 3. Fully irrigated with 3 crops), and bio-energy crops (cassava).",""],[1,"136","20","Irrigation Water Technology and Approach Research","Conduct research to develop technology and approaches towards sustainable and optimal use of irrigation waters.",""],[1,"136","21","Agricultural Tools Research and Development","Conduct research to develop agricultural tools for pre-harvest operations.",""],[1,"136","22","Pest Management Technology Research Programme","Conduct research to develop technologies about pest management, including rats, golden apple snails, insects and weeds with particular focus on preventive strategies.",""],[1,"136","24","Coastal Crop Production Technology Research","Conduct research to develop technologies for crop production in coastal zones under conditions of climate change.",""],[1,"136","25","Greenhouse Gas Emissions Reduction Research","Conduct research to develop approaches that help minimize Green House Gas Emissions and also assess the impact on climate change.",""],[1,"136","26","Crop Insurance Scheme Research","Conduct research to develop information on crop insurance schemes.",""],[1,"136","27","Integrated Watershed Management Technology Research","Conduct research to develop technologies for Integrated Watershed Management Systems to improve productivity and sustainability promote best practices in the utilization of soil and water.",""],[1,"137","1","Conservation Agriculture Effectiveness Research","Conduct research to assess the effectiveness of 'Conservation Agriculture' under Cambodian conditions.",""],[1,"137","2","Farm Mechanization Effectiveness Research","Conduct research to assess the effectiveness of farm mechanization.",""],[1,"137","3","Climate Variability Impact Research on Crop Quality","Conduct research to assess the impact of climate variability on the quality of grains, vegetables and fruits.",""],[1,"137","4","Farmer Climate Change Adaptation Capacity Building","Improving farmers' capacities in adapting to climate change in agriculture.",""],[1,"138","15","Climate-Resilient Agro-Industries Development","Mitigate impacts of climate change through development of agro-industries.",""]],"75":[[1,"137","9","Value Chain-Based Livestock and Aquaculture Policy Framework","RGC in the Fifth Legislature will promote broader livestock farming and aquaculture through introducing a policy framework based on the value chain principle, and also accounting for issues such as food safety standards and market regulation functions, especially sanitary and phyto-sanitary standards.",""],[1,"137","10","Strategic Planning Framework for Fisheries Implementation","Further implementing Strategic Planning Framework for Fisheries 2010-2019 with the aim of boosting fish production to serve domestic consumption and export markets by relying on 3 pillars: (1) freshwater and marine-based natural fisheries, (2) freshwater and marine aquaculture, and (3) facilitating processing and trade.",""],[1,"137","11","Livestock Farming Policy and Strategy Development and Implementation","Promoting the development and implementation of livestock farming policy and strategy.",""],[1,"137","12","Livestock and Aquaculture Research and Development Enhancement","Enhancing R&D in areas such as breeding, animal health and feed production, and farming systems both in livestock and aquaculture sectors.",""],[1,"137","14","Animal Feed Production Investment Support","Encouraging investments in medium and large-scale animal feed production to support livestock farming, along with improvements in the extension services system, animal breeding, credit and market access for farmers, incentives for private investment in processing of livestock and fisheries products, establishment of modern slaughterhouses as well as facilitation of trade in livestock, livestock products, and fish and fisheries products.",""],[1,"137","17","Livestock Human Resources Development","Develop human resources for livestock production.",""],[1,"138","1","Veterinary Services Improvement Programme","Decrease prevalence of morbidity and mortality of animals through better veterinary services.",""],[1,"138","2","Animal Feed Production and Breeding Stock Improvement","Improve the quality of animal food production and animal breeding stocks.",""],[1,"138","4","Animal Health and Livestock Production Research and Dissemination","Strengthen research and dissemination of animal health and livestock production.",""],[1,"138","6","Livestock Production and Veterinary Services Investment Promotion","Promote investments in livestock production and veterinary services, and foster markets for animals and animals-originated products.",""],[1,"138","19","Legal Accessibility Study for Rubber Cultivation Land","Study the legal accessibilities of the potentiality of available land suitable for rubber cultivation.",""],[1,"138","20","Smallholder Rubber Cultivation Support","Encourage smallholder cultivation of rubber.",""],[1,"138","21","Rubber Estate-Based Smallholder Development","Promote rubber estates to be the nucleus of small holders development.",""],[1,"138","22","Rubber Value Chain Enhancement","· Enhance rubber value chain.",""],[1,"138","23","Strengthening the General Directorate of Rubber","Improve the role of the General Directorate of Rubber.",""],[1,"146","12","Inland and Marine Aquaculture Development","Promotion and development of inland and marine aquacultures.",""],[1,"147","12","FiA Human Resource Development Expansion","Expand human resource development in the FiA at both central and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"147","13","Inland and Marine Aquaculture Development","Develop both, inland and marine aquaculture.",""],[1,"147","14","Community Fisheries and Rice-Field Fisheries Support","Support community fisheries and rice-field fisheries.",""]],"76":[[1,"137","13","Animal Health and Production Law Adoption and Sanitary Enforcement","Promoting the adoption of the law on animal health and production to provide the basis for the institutional arrangement and management of this sector, aimed at strengthening enforcement of sanitary standards for animal products, and strengthening and enforcing animal sanitary and phyto-sanitary measures to prevent and combat the outbreak of animal diseases, and to protect public health.",""]],"77":[[1,"64","24","Khmer Heritage Preservation and Promotion Programme","The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts (MOCFA) not only continued to preserve ancient temples and archaeological museums but also actively promoted Khmer arts including traditional Khmer dances, songs and other artistic endeavours.","Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts (MOCFA)"],[1,"64","24","Khmer Handicrafts Revival, Production, and Marketing Support","The ministry also promoted revival, production, and marketing of Khmer handicrafts.","Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts (MOCFA)"],[1,"64","26","Ancient Temple Preservation and Access Infrastructure Improvement","The preservation of ancient temples, as well as improvements to roads and bridges for easy access to the ancient temples.",""],[1,"64","28","Construction of Provincial Conservative Offices and Tribal Centre","The construction of conservative offices in provinces and a Tribal Centre in North East.",""],[1,"65","1","Cultural Exhibition Hall and Traditional Dance Performance Hall Construction","The construction of a cultural exhibition hall for exhibiting products and a hall for traditional Khmer dance performances.",""],[1,"69","6","Creative Industries Roadmap","Proposed a roadmap for creative industries for promoting the investment for prioritized local industries.",""],[1,"176","4","Cultural Heritage Preservation and Promotion Programme","The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts (MOCFA) will continue ensuring preservation and sustainable development of built and living heritage, including archaeological urban and underwater heritage, traditional performing arts, minority traditions and arts, museums as well as the fight against illicit trafficking of cultural artefacts and will actively promote creativity in the domain of arts, cultural industries and cultural entrepreneurship.","Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts (MOCFA)"],[1,"176","7","Traditional Knowledge and Creative Industries Support","Maintain traditional knowledge and forms of work as forms of sustainable development as part of the recognition of creative industries.",""],[1,"176","8","Safeguard Traditional Performing Arts and Promote Creative Industries","Safeguard of traditional performing arts and promote of creativity, contemporary works and innovation through the arts and creative industries.",""],[1,"176","10","Performing Arts and Creativity Promotion and Dissemination","Promotion and dissemination of performing arts and creativity in order to connect products and customers that the government will address in this regard.",""],[1,"176","12","Film Sector Human Resource Development","Develop human resource in film sector.",""],[1,"176","13","Foreign Film Production Attraction Initiative","Attract foreign film production companies to shoot in Cambodia.",""],[1,"176","14","One Stop Service for Film Production Facilitation","Increase facilitation for film production through One Stop Service.",""],[1,"176","17","Cultural Organizations and Enterprises Database","Establish a database on cultural organizations and enterprises.",""],[1,"176","19","Handicraft Human Resources Development and Private Sector Cooperation","Develop human resources in handicraft; cooperate with private sector.",""],[1,"176","20","Cultural Products Promotion Initiative","Strengthen promoting cultural products.",""],[1,"176","22","Heritage Area Registration and Conservation Programme","Register heritage areas including urban heritage, conserve them and present them to the public, especially major sites in remote areas such as Banteay Chhmar, Sambor Prei Kuk, and Preah Khan Kampong Svay.",""],[1,"177","1","Heritage Protection and Ancient Site Excavation Programme","Protect heritages, restore and excavate in ancient sites.",""],[1,"177","2","Heritage Officials Capacity Strengthening through Institutional Cooperation","Strengthen the capacity of the heritage officials through a reinforced cooperation with relevant national and international institutions in particular with the APSARA National Authority and Preah Vihea Authority.",""],[1,"177","3","Public Heritage Preservation Participation Initiative","Encourage public participation in the preservation of heritage.",""],[1,"177","6","Regulatory Enforcement and Reform","Increase the control of the existing legal regulations and formulate new regulations.",""],[1,"177","7","Officials' Capacity Development","Continue encouraging development of officials' capacities.",""],[1,"177","8","Art Education and Cultural Vocational Training Support","Support art education in cooperation with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sport and vocational training for artists, practitioners and other professionals in the field of culture.","Ministry of Education, Youth and Sport"],[1,"177","9","Monitoring Guidelines Development","Develop monitoring guidelines on evaluating the performance.",""]],"78":[[1,"166","11","Electricity Supply Capacity and Coverage Expansion","RGC will further strengthen the capacity and security of electricity supply and expand the supply coverage",""],[1,"166","12","Expansion of Clean and Low-Cost Electricity Generation and Transmission Networks","Further expanding the capacity of low-cost and hi-tech electricity production, especially from new and clean energy sources, along with continued development of all levels of the transmission network aimed at strengthening energy security and ensuring efficient, safe, high quality, reliable and affordable electricity supply and distribution to respond to development needs.",""],[1,"166","13","Private Sector Investment in Power Infrastructure","Further encouraging the private sector to invest in electricity generation, and transmission and distribution infrastructure by focusing on technical and economic efficiency and minimization of environmental and social impacts.",""],[1,"166","14","Electrification Strategy Implementation","Stepping up the implementation of the electrification strategy to realize the goal \"by 2020, all villages in the Kingdom of Cambodia will have access to electricity supplied by the national grid and other sources\".",""],[1,"166","15","Rural Electrification Fund Support","Further supporting the rural electrification fund aimed at achieving equitable electricity access for the population, through government budget, social fund from Electricity Du Cambodge (EDC) and seek support fund from other development partners.",""],[1,"167","1","Off-Peak Electricity Tariff Rationalization","Pursuing rationalization measures for electricity consumption by reducing power tariffs during off-peak hours to serve production and irrigation systems aimed at improving agricultural productivity and accelerating the development of industry and handicraft sectors.",""],[1,"167","9","Electricity Supply Expansion and Tariff Reduction","Increasing electricity supply capacity and reducing tariff to an appropriate level, while the strengthening institutional mechanisms and management capability.",""],[1,"173","4","Electricity Generation and Distribution Expansion","increase electricity generating capacity and expand the electricity distribution network in urban and rural areas;",""]],"79":[[1,"57","1","Energy Sector Development Plan Implementation","the Ministry of Industry Mine and Energy has continued the implementation of Energy Sector Development Plan, 2005-2024.","Ministry of Industry Mine and Energy"],[1,"57","1","Rural Electrification Master Plan for Renewable Energy","Meanwhile, Rural Electrification Master Plan focusing on the use of renewable energy is also being implemented.",""],[1,"57","9","115 kV Transmission Line from Thai Border","A 115KV-transmission line, from the Thai border to supply electricity to Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap, and Battambang Provinces.",""],[1,"57","10","230 kV Transmission Line from Cambodia-Vietnam Border to Phnom Penh","A 230KV-transmission line from Cambodia-Vietnam border to Phnom Penh.",""],[1,"57","12","230 kV Transmission Line Project","A 230KV-transmission line connecting Phnom Penh, Kompong Chhnang, Pursat and Battambang.",""],[1,"57","13","230 kV Transmission Line Project","A 230KV-transmission line connecting Takeo, Kampot and Preah Sihanouk.",""],[1,"57","14","230 kV Transmission Line between Phnom Penh and Kompong Cham","A 230KV-transmission line connecting Phnom Penh and Kompong Cham.",""],[1,"57","15","Rural Electrification Policy Implementation","To implement the Rural Electrification Policy, the RGC has transferred Rural Electrification Funds be led by Electricite Du Cambodge (EDC) to promote equity in access to electricity supply services and encourage private sector to participate in investing in rural power supply services with a sustainability, in particular, encourage the use of new technologies and renewable energy.",""],[1,"57","16","GMS Power Trade Plan Implementation","Cambodia has been participating in the implementation of GMS Power Trade Plan.",""]],"80":[[1,"167","2","Oil and Gas Exploration and Commercialization Initiative","Stepping up the exploration and commercialization of the oil and gas sector",""],[1,"168","1","Petroleum Sector Legal and Regulatory Framework Development","Developing laws, regulations and regulatory framework for the petroleum sector to ensure an efficient management of oil and gas.",""],[1,"168","2","Associated Gas Utilization Plan","Preparing plans for appropriate use of gas, which is otherwise flared, for productive purposes.",""],[1,"168","3","Downstream Oil and Gas Processing Enhancement","Enhancing appropriate downstream activities in commercial processing and use of the oil and gas resources.",""],[1,"168","4","Oil and Gas Sector Human Resource Development and Institutional Strengthening","Promoting human resource development and institutional strengthening to improve management efficiency in the oil and gas sector.",""],[1,"168","5","Petroleum Agreements Management and Monitoring","Managing and monitoring the implementation of petroleum agreements efficiently.",""],[1,"168","6","Oil and Gas Research and Development Promotion","Promoting research and development focused on oil and gas issues.",""],[1,"177","10","Extractive Industries Development","RGC will also focus on the development of extractive industries.",""]],"81":[[1,"167","5","Private Sector Energy Infrastructure Investment Promotion","RGC will encourage the private sector to invest in energy infrastructure: generation, transmission and distribution.",""],[1,"167","5","Environmental Safeguards for Energy Projects","RGC will make further efforts to mitigate the adverse effects on environment and society while implementing energy projects; yet safeguarding the economic efficiency.",""],[1,"167","5","Electricity Sector Capacity Building and Institutional Reform","Attention will also be paid to capacity building and institutional reform in the Electricity Authority of Cambodia (EAC), Electricity Du Cambodge (EDC) and other relevant agencies to improve supply and the management's efficiency.",""],[1,"167","6","Legal and Regulatory Framework for Sector Resource Management","RGC will also develop a legal and regulatory framework for the sector to ensure efficient management and use of resources.",""],[1,"167","11","Energy Sector Legal and Regulatory Framework Development","Developing a legal and regulatory framework for the energy sector to ensure efficient management and use of resources.",""],[1,"167","14","Energy Source Exploration for Electricity Generation","Promote the exploration of energy sources such as hydropower, natural gas, and coal for the electricity generation.",""],[1,"167","16","Energy Efficiency and Environmental Mitigation Measures","Encourage the efficient use of energy and mitigate the adverse effects on the environment resulting from energy supply and use.",""],[1,"167","17","Private Sector Energy Investment Promotion","Encourage the private sector to invest in energy, including in generation, transmission and distribution.",""],[1,"167","18","Renewable Energy Development and Energy Efficiency Promotion","Further foster development of all types of renewable energy such as biomass, biogas, bio-fuel etc., and enhance the efficiency of energy through the use of energy-saving stoves, to reduce the use of fuel, firewood, charcoal, etc.",""],[1,"167","19","Regional Energy Trade Cooperation","Promote regional energy trade through bi-and multi-lateral cooperation.",""]],"82":[[1,"154","6","Gender Program Continuation","Continue implementing the gender program.",""]],"83":[[1,"209","3","Law Enforcement Measures Against Human Trafficking and Sexual Exploitation","Further strengthening law enforcement in measures against human trafficking and sexual exploitation of women and children.",""],[1,"210","1","Multi-sectoral Primary Prevention Strategy on Violence Against Women","Primary prevention: to reduce violence against women through a multi-sectoral coordinated primary prevention strategy targeting key actors and settings for positive change.",""],[1,"210","2","Legal Protection and Multi-sectoral Services for Survivors of Violence Against Women","Legal protection and Multi-sectoral services: to increase the provision of easily accessible, appropriate, quality services, and coordinated response to the varied needs of all survivors' of violence against women without discrimination.",""],[1,"210","3","Gender-Sensitive Laws and Policies for Protection of Survivors of Violence Against Women","Laws and policies: to ensure that laws and policies in Cambodia are gender sensitive and designed to protect the rights of survivors of violence against women.",""],[1,"210","4","Capacity Building for Violence Against Women Response and Prevention","Capacity building: to increase the capacities and resources of key sectors at the national level on designing, implementing, reporting, monitoring, evaluating, and coordinating violence against women response and prevention interventions.",""],[1,"210","5","Domestic Violence, Rape, and Human Trafficking Law Enforcement and Monitoring","RGC will closely monitor the incidents of domestic violence, rapes and human trafficking and enforce laws implementation in order to bring perpetrators to justice.",""]],"84":[[1,"15","4","Environmental Conservation Efforts for Tonle Sap, Water Systems, and Forests","there is scope to step up efforts to save especially the Tonle Sap (and other water systems) and forests for sustainable development, sustainable livelihoods of people in rural areas, and sustainable agriculture.",""],[1,"41","8","National Sustainable Land Use Management Action Plan","Draft National action plan on sustainable land use management.",""],[1,"41","9","Soil Fertility Management and Conservation Guideline","Draft guideline on soil fertility management and conservation.",""],[1,"43","16","Fishery Resource Management and Conservation Support","Equipment and funds to support the management, research activities, extension, conservation and protection of fishery resources.",""],[1,"45","4","Management of Natural Protected Areas","MOE has appointed park rangers for patrolling, observing, monitoring, recording data, and preventing natural-resource-related crimes, for managing the 23 natural protected areas and RAMSAR sites.","MOE"],[1,"99","13","Protected Forest Areas Management","Manage/implement better: 23 protected forest areas, Natural resources/minerals, Water, Fisheries.",""],[1,"99","13","Natural Resources and Water Sector Management","Manage/implement better: 23 protected forest areas, Natural resources/minerals, Water, Fisheries.",""],[1,"116","1","Forestry and Fisheries Reform","other reform programs including public financial management reform, land reform, and forestry and fisheries reform",""]],"85":[[1,"147","25","Environmental Impact Assessment of Development Projects","Evaluate environmental impacts of any development projects proposed.",""],[1,"147","26","Environmental Pollution Monitoring and Inspection","Maintain a high quality environment: it should be chemical-free; by monitoring and inspecting polluting sources and monitoring water, soil and air.",""],[1,"147","28","Biosafety and Biotechnology Implementation Strengthening","Strengthen the implementation of bio-safety and biotechnology activities.",""],[1,"147","29","Environmental Education and Information Dissemination","Strengthen environmental education and dissemination of environmental information.",""],[1,"148","1","Environmental Pollution Management Law","Developing a Law on the Management of Environmental Pollution.",""],[1,"148","2","Environmental Impact Assessment Law Development","Developing a Law on Environmental Impact Assessment.",""],[1,"148","4","Biodiversity Law Development","Developing a Law on Biodiversity.",""],[1,"148","5","Chemicals Management Law Development","Developing a Law on Chemicals Management.",""],[1,"148","6","Minamata Convention Ratification Law Development","Developing a Law on Ratification on Minamata Convention on Mercury.",""],[1,"148","7","Sub-Decree on Establishment of Funds for Natural Protected Areas","Developing a Sub-decree on the Establishment of Funds for Natural Protected Areas.",""],[1,"148","8","Ministerial Order on Natural Protected Areas Management Structure Adjustment","Developing a Ministerial Order on adjusting the management structure of the natural protected areas.",""],[1,"148","9","Environmental Impact Assessment Sub-Decree Amendment","Amending the Sub-decree on the environmental impact assessment.",""],[1,"148","11","LMSSP Monitoring and Evaluation Unit","Establishing a M&E unit for LMSSP.",""],[1,"148","12","Sub-Decree on Management of Electric and Electronic Appliances in Waste Management","Developing a Sub-decree on the management of electric and electronic appliances within waste management.",""],[1,"148","13","Wastewater Management Circular","Issuing a circular on management of waste water, to municipal and provincial authorities.",""],[1,"148","14","Solid Waste Management Circular","Issuing circular on scientific collection, transportation, recycling and disposal of solid waste and rubbish.",""],[1,"148","15","Environmental Impact Assessment Requirement for Development Projects","MOE will in collaboration with concerned the ministries and agencies, ensure sustainable use of natural resources by conducting environmental impact assessments, prior to the implementation of development projects.","MOE | concerned the ministries and agencies"],[1,"148","16","Environmental Impact Assessment Guideline Development","Develop guidelines for environmental impact assessment in the sector of oil and gas, agriculture, tourism and infrastructure.",""],[1,"148","17","Environmental Impact Assessment Capacity Building","Strengthen technical capacity of technical staff at all levels on environmental impact assessment.",""],[1,"148","18","Environmental Management Plan Monitoring and Environmental Protection Agreement Implementation","Monitor implementation of environmental management plan presented in the environmental impact assessment report, and implement environmental protection agreements with project owners.",""],[1,"148","20","Public Water Quality Monitoring","Monitor the quality of public water in rivers, streams, lakes and public sewers.",""],[1,"148","21","Public Water Quality Monitoring Expansion","Look into possibilities to expand the monitoring of public water quality.",""],[1,"148","22","Industrial Wastewater Pollution Monitoring","Monitor pollution caused by waste water from factories and enterprises.",""],[1,"148","24","Air Pollution and Noise/Vibration Monitoring","Monitor air pollution and disturbance by noise and vibration.",""],[1,"148","25","Air Pollution Monitoring System","Look into possibilities of monitoring air pollution in the capital and provinces.",""],[1,"148","27","Laboratory Quality and Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the quality and capacity of laboratories.",""],[1,"148","28","Environmental Officials Capacity Building and Public Awareness Campaign","Strengthen the capacity of capital and provincial environment officials, and promoting public awareness on environmental pollution and public health.",""],[1,"150","8","Biosafety and Modern Biotechnology Strengthening","Strengthen bio-safety and modern biotechnology activities under the Cartagena Protocol on Bio-safety to contribute to environmental conservation, human health, and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"150","9","DNA Analysis Capacity for Living Modified Organisms","Strengthen the capacity to analyze DNA of living modified organisms.",""],[1,"150","12","Environmental Education Integration","Integrate environmental education at all levels in education.",""],[1,"150","13","Informal Environmental Education Enhancement","Enhance the informal environmental education by integrating knowledge and culture (traditional and contemporary), into the main environmental issues.",""],[1,"150","14","Environmental Education Human Resource Development","Strengthen human resource development for environmental education, for sustainable development.",""],[1,"150","15","Regional Environmental Information and Training Networks","Improve ways to exchange environmental information, skills and resources in the region and providing support for environmental education and training through formal and informal networks.",""]],"86":[[1,"39","11","National Coastal Zones Integration Strategy","The Ministry has prepared a national strategy for coastal zones integration for the four provinces, namely Kep, Kampot, Preah Sihanouk, and Koh Kong.","The Ministry"],[1,"40","5","National Committee for Managing and Developing Cambodia's Coastal Zones","Royal Decree on the Establishment of a National Committee for Managing and Developing Cambodia's Coastal Zones.",""]],"87":[[1,"130","11","Climate Change Adaptation and Resilience Strengthening","Intensifying efforts to reduce the impact of climate change by strengthening the adaptation capacity and resiliency to climate change, particularly by implementing the \"Cambodia Climate Change Strategic Plan 2014-2023\", \"National Policy on Green Development\" and the \"National Strategic Plan on Green Development 2013- 2030\".",""],[1,"130","12","Climate Change Mainstreaming Capacity Strengthening","Continuing to strengthen technical and institutional capacity to promote the mainstreaming of climate change responses into the policies, laws and plans at national and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"145","2","Carbon Trading Regulatory Framework Development","through the development of regulatory frameworks and mechanisms for carbon trading",""],[1,"145","2","Climate Change Adaptation Capacity Strengthening","strengthening the capability, preparation and implementation of climate change adaptation measures",""],[1,"145","2","Environmental Financing Mechanism Assessment","assessment of the scope of the use of environmental financing mechanisms including payment for environmental services and environmental fund",""],[1,"147","22","Cambodia Climate Change Strategic Plan Implementation","Implement the Cambodia Climate Change Strategic Plan 2014-2023.",""],[1,"147","23","Green Growth and Low-Carbon Development Strategy Adoption","Adopt Green Growth and low carbon development strategies, which are key to sustainable economic development.",""],[1,"147","27","Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Measures","Adapt to climate change and mitigation measures for reduction of greenhouse gas emissions.",""],[1,"147","31","Climate Change Legal Framework Development","Prepare the climate change legal framework which will include updating institutional arrangement, financing arrangements, and mainstreaming of climate change across sectors.",""],[1,"148","3","Green Growth Law Development","Developing a Law on Green Growth.",""],[1,"149","3","Strengthening the National Committee for Climate Change Management Secretariat","Strengthen the capacity of the secretariat of the National Committee for Climate Change Management, in coordinating inter-ministerial activities and also in managing national climate change funds.",""],[1,"149","4","Cambodia Climate Change Strategic Plan Implementation","RGC is committed to full implementation of Cambodia Climate Change Strategic Plan 2014-2023, which includes:",""],[1,"149","5","National Climate Change Monitoring and Evaluation System","Put in place and implement national monitoring and evaluation systems for climate change projects.",""],[1,"149","6","Knowledge Management System for Climate Change Data and Local Knowledge","Create a knowledge management system for collection, analysis, and dissemination of data/knowledge, including knowledge of local communities on climate change.",""],[1,"149","7","Greenhouse Gas Inventory System Improvement","Improve a greenhouse gas inventory system: data collection, storage, analysis and modeling.",""],[1,"149","8","National Greenhouse Gas Reduction Mechanisms Registration System","Establish a national registration system for greenhouse gases reduction mechanisms, and foster implementation of appropriate mitigation activities (AMA) and greenhouse gas-reduction activities under different mechanisms within various priority sectors that provide multiple benefits.",""],[1,"149","9","Climate Change Action Plan Implementation Support","Mobilize funds and technical assistance for implementing the main activities outlined in the action plan and strategic plan to address sectoral climate change issues of the relevant ministries/institutions, including research activities, to support policy development.",""],[1,"149","10","Climate Change Capacity and Public Awareness Programme","Coordinate and enhance capacity and public awareness on climate change at national and local levels.",""],[1,"149","11","National Adaptation Plan Development and Implementation Strategy","Coordinate developing a national adaptation plan and develop implementation strategies for addressing medium- and long-term adaptation needs.",""],[1,"149","12","Green Growth Economy Development Strategy","RGC is committed to develop an economy based on Green Growth principles, as stipulated in the national policy on Green Growth, and the National Strategic Plan on Green Growth for 2013-2030.",""],[1,"149","14","National Green Growth Action Plan","Developing national action plan on Green Growth.",""],[1,"149","15","Green Growth Awareness Education and Capacity Building","Promoting education, training and capacity building on awareness about Green Growth.",""],[1,"149","16","Green Investment Promotion","Promoting green investment that utilizes green technology.",""]],"88":[[1,"46","3","Climate Change Awareness and Knowledge Dissemination","Both national and sub- national levels have begun raising awareness and disseminating climate change related knowledge and policies.",""],[1,"46","3","Climate Change Education Integration","The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has started to integrate climate change issues into the formal and non-formal education systems.","Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports"],[1,"46","3","Climate Change Negotiation Leadership","The Ministry of Environment has played an active role in leading the climate change negotiation process under the climate change talks of the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC).","Ministry of Environment"],[1,"46","4","Public Awareness and Participation in Biosafety and Biotechnology","MOE has also helped raise public awareness and participation in the fields of bio-safety and modern biotechnology.","MOE"],[1,"47","1","Environmental Education and Eco-School Programme","the MOE has worked with the ASEAN on environmental education, development of guidelines and implementing an \"Eco-School\" programmes, and sending Cambodian youth to join environmental efforts with other youth from ASEAN for information and experience sharing.","MOE | ASEAN"],[1,"47","1","Youth Environmental Debate Programme","organizing quarterly environmental debate programmes for the youth",""],[1,"47","1","National Environmental Awareness and Clean-up Campaigns","organizing the National and World Environment Day, and organizing the National Environmental Clean-up Day.",""],[1,"83","2","National Strategy on Environment and Health Dissemination Campaign","The National Committee for Environment and Health and Inter-ministerial Technical Staff has taken up the task of disseminating the National Strategy on Environment and Health.",""]],"89":[[1,"56","1","Cambodia National Mekong Committee Coordination Mechanism","Cambodia National Mekong Committee (CNMC) is an inter-ministerial committee responsible to ensure effective coordination among 17 member line ministries in implementing all related programmes and activities at regional and national levels under the framework of the Mekong River Commission (MRC).",""],[1,"56","1","Mekong River Commission Strategic Planning and Basin Strategy Updates","In the past years, MRC Strategic Plan, Integrated Water Resources Management Principles (IWRM), and MRC IWRM-based Basin Development Strategy have been developed and updated for implementation.",""],[1,"56","1","MRC IWRM-Based Basin Development Strategy Implementation","CNMC with full cooperation of its member line agencies has been actively implementing the MRC IWRM-based Basin Development Strategy and related programmes: Basin Development Plan, Fisheries, Irrigated Agriculture, Sustainable Hydropower, Flood Management, Drought Management, Climate Change, Mekong Integrated Water Resource Management, Information and Knowledge Management, and Integrated Capacity Building, to serve regional and national interests.",""],[1,"164","15","Mekong River Commission Cooperation and Self-Financing Transition","RGC will continue to fully cooperate with other Mekong Member Countries under the MRC Framework to ensure the Sustainable of the Mekong River Basin.",""],[1,"164","15","Mekong River Commission Full Self-Financing Arrangement","Head of the Government of the Mekong Member Countries committed to full self- financing of the MRC by 2030 of which each Government of the Mekong Member Countries has to increase its financial contribution to operate MRC and prepare itself to gradually take over partly responsibility starting from 2012 to fully responsibility in 2030.",""],[1,"164","16","Mekong River Commission Strategic Planning and Programme Implementation","RGC will continue to cooperate with other Mekong Member Countries in updating the MRC Strategic Plan, IWRM-based Basin Development Strategy and effectively implementing the set programmes under the MRC Framework namely Basin Development Plan, Fisheries, Irrigated Agriculture, Sustainable Hydropower, Flood Management, Drought Management, Climate Change, Mekong Integrated Water Resources Management, Information and Knowledge Management and Integrated Capacity Building.",""],[1,"164","16","River Basin Management Decentralization Road Map","the Road Map for Decentralization of Core Function of River Basin Management has been developing and gradually implementing since 2012 and expects to have full implementation in 2030 by all the Mekong Member Countries",""]],"90":[[1,"165","1","Urban Water Supply Legal Framework Development","Develop a legal framework for urban water supply:",""],[1,"165","2","Comprehensive Water Supply Law","Develop a comprehensive water supply law.",""],[1,"165","3","Urban Water Supply Investment and Licensing Regulations","Develop investment and licensing regulations for urban water supply.",""],[1,"165","4","Urban Water Supply Economic Regulation Framework","Develop economic regulations for urban water supply.",""],[1,"165","5","Urban Water Supply Technical Regulations","Develop technical regulations for urban water supply.",""],[1,"165","6","Urban Water Supply Decentralization and De-concentration","Promote decentralization and de-concentration in the urban water supply sector:",""],[1,"165","7","Decentralization of Urban Water Supply Service Delivery","Promote the decentralization of the urban water supply service delivery mandate to the appropriate sub-national level, while ensuring economic and technical regulation of services remains at central level.",""],[1,"165","8","Provincial Waterworks Service Delivery Autonomy Reform","Transfer full autonomy for service delivery to all provincial waterworks:",""],[1,"165","9","Provincial Public Waterworks Capacity-Building and Transfer Reform","Build the capacity of provincial public waterworks to enable the gradual transfer of roles and functions to autonomous state-owned enterprises.",""],[1,"165","10","Public Waterworks Autonomy Reform","Following the example of PPWSA, target the autonomy of all public waterworks by 2018.",""],[1,"165","12","Sector Development Strategy and Long-Term Investment and Financing Plan","Prepare a Sector Development Strategy, including a long-term investment and financing plan.",""],[1,"165","13","Waterworks Five-Year Business Planning and Expansion Programme","All waterworks will develop a 5-year business plan by 2018, including an investment and expansion plan.",""],[1,"165","14","Development Partner Resource Mobilization for Service Rehabilitation and Expansion","Continue the good partnership and cooperation with the development partners under the umbrella sector development plan to mobilize resources for rehabilitation and expansion of services.",""],[1,"165","15","Private Sector Concessional Loan Access Support","Conduct studies and encourage private sector financing through cooperation with other related institutions of the RGC, development partners, NGOs and local banks to support access to concessional loans for the private sector.",""],[1,"165","16","Private Sector Investment Promotion Framework","Encourage and motivate investment by the private sector through the creation of a policy, legal framework, and investment climate conducive to attracting public private partnerships, including incentives for private investment.",""],[1,"165","21","Urban Water Supply Human Resource Development","Develop quality human resources, with appropriate quantity, to respond to the needs of urban water supply sector development.",""],[1,"165","22","Cambodia Waterworks Association Establishment","Establish the Cambodia Waterworks Association as a national association representing the urban water supply sector and promote its role for mutual exchanges and learning between all waterworks.",""],[1,"165","23","National Urban Water Supply Training Center","Utilize the PPWSA's staff and resources and establish a national training center for urban water supply, providing nationally approved training and qualifications by the industry for the industry.",""],[1,"165","24","Replication of PPWSA Waterworks Model","Replicate the experiences of PPWSA at all waterworks, targeting higher standards for quality, affordability, and sustainability of water supply for the customers.",""],[1,"165","25","Urban Water Supply Performance Benchmarking System","Encourage a competitive environment in the urban water supply sector by adopting standard service performance indicators and a transparent benchmarking system, reviewed and audited by the ministry on an annual basis.",""],[1,"166","1","Public Waterworks Cost-Recovery and Reinvestment Reform","Urge public waterworks to provide the quality and affordable water supply to ensure the full cost recovery and a reserve for improvement and re-investment; reducing gradually the reliance on the external supports in re-investment in the public waterworks.",""],[1,"166","3","Interagency Coordination for Water Supply Development","Minimize negative impacts of water supply development on other sectors through close collaboration among relevant agencies to ensure that projects are interrelated and consistent.",""]],"91":[[1,"160","18","Water Resource Management and Irrigation Systems Development","RGC in the Fifth Legislature will continue to enhance water resource management and develop irrigation systems; undertake repair and maintenance of irrigation infrastructure where required; promote integration between irrigation, and hydropower and transportation; and develop legal framework, institutions and human resources.",""],[1,"160","19","Irrigation System Expansion and Infrastructure Upgrading","Pursuing the expansion of irrigation systems through mobilizing public and other resources in order to rationally increase irrigation capacity, focusing on enhancing standards and quality of irrigation infrastructure, effectiveness of investment and",""],[1,"161","1","Water Storage Reservoirs and Irrigation System Development","construction of water storage reservoirs, and development of a fully extended irrigation system, with attention on needed preparations for adaptation to climate change.",""],[1,"161","2","Irrigation System Management Master Plan","Improving the effectiveness of irrigation system management, with emphasis on strengthening policy and legal frameworks and water use mechanisms, improved maintenance and financing through formulation and implementation of a master plan for water resources and irrigation system management, continuing to strengthen maintenance mechanisms, repair and rehabilitation of irrigation systems including formulation and implementation of legal arrangements related to the management of farmers and water users associations, river basins, and water quality; and human resource and institutional developments.",""],[1,"161","3","Institutional Coordination for Water Infrastructure Development","Stepping up institutional coordination aimed at harmonizing development of irrigation infrastructure, hydropower and transportation to increase effectiveness of investment and use of water resources.",""],[1,"161","4","Water Resources Management Law Enforcement","Enhancing the sustainability of the use of water resources through vigorous implementation of \"Law on Water Resources Management of the Kingdom of Cambodia\" and other related laws.",""],[1,"161","10","Irrigation System Management and Institutional Capacity Strengthening","RGC will efficiently manage the irrigation system by strengthening the institutional capacity in the concerned ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"161","10","Community Participation and Water User Group Strengthening","It will further increase people's participation in the management and use of irrigation systems for cultivation, facilitation of navigation, and promotion of aquaculture, and will strengthen the water user communities.",""],[1,"161","10","Private Sector Participation in Irrigation and Water Supply","RGC will encourage private sector participation in irrigation and water supply.",""],[1,"161","14","Water Laws and Regulations Enactment","Enactment of laws and regulations related to water.",""],[1,"162","4","Irrigation Scheme Rehabilitation and Construction","Rehabilitate and construct the existing irrigation schemes to meet the urgent needs of water for agriculture.",""],[1,"162","5","Irrigation Scheme and Drainage System Rehabilitation and Construction","Prioritize the rehabilitation and construction of irrigation schemes and drainage system in areas where the poverty is high or economic potential areas which need water for productivity.",""],[1,"162","6","Reservoir and Water Infrastructure Maintenance and Expansion","Encouraging maintenance and expansion of reservoirs, lacks, ponds, intake canals and drainage system to ensure the water supply for cultivation zone, aquaculture, daily living and animals.",""],[1,"162","7","Water Management Innovation Technology Dissemination in Rain-Fed Agriculture","Promote the dissemination of water management innovation technology in rain-fed agricultural areas which depend on rain water.",""],[1,"162","8","Farmer and Stakeholder Participation in Irrigation and Drainage Projects","Encourage farmers' participation, especially women, stakeholders, and private sector to participate in all stages of projects preparation, projects improvement and irrigation and drainage system development.",""],[1,"162","9","River Basin Development Planning Study","Promote the study and river basin development planning in short, medium and long term with the consideration of changing of water discharge, water current, and aquifers to ensure the sue of water resources at present in the future.",""],[1,"162","11","Integrated Water Resources Management and Development","Implementing integrated water resources management and development thoroughly considering a clear link between water resources and other sectors of environment, the changing of the human and environment needs from water resources and other needs to achieve the effective management.",""],[1,"162","12","River Basin Development and Management Plan Implementation","Increasing the awareness and encouraging the implementation of river basin development and management plan with the cooperation of concerned ministries, stakeholders and beneficiaries, especially women.","concerned ministries"],[1,"162","13","Farmer and Private Sector Participation in Irrigation and Drainage Management","Encouraging the participation of farmer water users community, beneficiaries, and private sector at all stages of irrigation and drainage schemes development and management.",""],[1,"162","14","Farmer Water Users Community Capacity Building for Irrigation Scheme Operation and Maintenance","Improving farmer water users community (FWUC) capacity on operation and maintenance of irrigation schemes with farmers' and development partner participatory.",""],[1,"162","15","Farmer Water User Committee Strengthening and Establishment","Strengthening and establishing (FWUC) to participate in water resources management, water distribution, and irrigation maintenance with effectiveness and sustainability.",""],[1,"162","16","Participatory Irrigation Scheme Management Investment Support","Encouraging investment from international donors and private sector to support the irrigation schemes management with farmers' and development partner participatory.",""],[1,"162","17","Irrigated Agriculture Income Generation and Water Sector Investment","Generating income through irrigated agriculture and continual investments on water sector for agricultural productivity.",""],[1,"163","4","Water Resources Management Sub-Decrees","Prepare sub-decrees to implement the Law on Water Resources Management endorsed in June 2007, namely:",""],[1,"163","22","Administrative Process Strengthening and On-the-Job Training for MOWRAM Officials","Strengthen the administrative processes and provide high level on-job training to MOWRAM officials.","MOWRAM"],[1,"163","23","Capacity Building for Sustainable Water Resource Management","Further strengthen officials' capacity at national and sub-national levels and the capacity of FWUC to be aware of the importance of water and advise them to participate in preparing plans for sustainable water resource management, maintenance, conservation, and utilization in order to preserve good ecosystem, by organizing training programs",""],[1,"164","2","Gender Networks in Provincial Departments","Create gender networks in all the provincial departments of MOWRAM.","MOWRAM"],[1,"164","3","Gender Mainstreaming in Water Issues","Bring out the gender component on water issues in all provinces.",""],[1,"164","5","Technical and Managerial Capacity Building for MOWRAM Staff","Build technical and managerial capacity of the MOWRAM staff.",""],[1,"164","9","Irrigation Infrastructure Rehabilitation and Expansion Programme","Prioritize rehabilitation, construction, maintenance, and management of irrigation infrastructure -- reservoirs, drainage systems, canals, flood-control systems, polders, and pumping stations -- to increase the cultivated area and agricultural production.",""],[1,"164","11","Participatory Irrigation System Management","Ensure participation of concerned institutions and the ownership of people in the management of irrigation systems.",""]],"92":[[1,"55","5","Farmer Water Users Communities Establishment","Establishing 109 Farmer Water Users Communities (FWUC) involving 13,899 famer households.",""],[1,"55","15","Water Resources Sector Capacity Building for MOWRAM Officials","Strengthening capacity of the MOWRAM officials through training courses (302 staff members) and workshops (181 participants) related to conservation and development of the water resources sector both in domestic and international.","MOWRAM"],[1,"55","20","Rural Irrigation Infrastructure Rehabilitation and Construction","Prioritizing locations that have high potential for generating incomes in rural communities for rehabilitation and construction of irrigation infrastructure.",""],[1,"55","21","Commune Irrigation Infrastructure Management","Engaging Commune Councils in managing commune irrigation infrastructure.",""],[1,"55","22","Farmer Engagement in Water Resources Management","Encouraging famer in water resources management, which contributes to increase in agricultural production.",""],[1,"55","23","Farmer Participation in Irrigation System Management","Increasing participation of farmers and farming communities in solving matters related to the use and maintenance of irrigation system.",""],[1,"55","24","Irrigation System Maintenance Costing","Carrying out costing the maintenance of irrigation systems.",""],[1,"154","24","Small-Scale Irrigation Repair and Construction","Continue to carry out repair and construction of small-scale irrigation systems to supply water for small- and medium-scale agricultural enterprises.",""]],"93":[[1,"55","2","Flood Control Project Repair","Repairing eight flood control projects, which are able to protect 5,097 ha of cultivated land.",""],[1,"55","3","Sea-Water-Protecting Dam Repair Programme","Repairing 10 sea-water-protecting dam projects, which are able to protect 1,750 ha of cultivated land.",""],[1,"55","4","Pumping Station Installation and Repair Programme","Installing one pumping station and repairing 49 pumping station and 140 pumping machines.",""],[1,"161","5","Flood Management and Prevention Infrastructure Development","Improving flood management and prevention by developing water release infrastructure, flood prevention dams, water storage reservoirs and water diversion channels to reduce impact from floods.",""],[1,"161","7","Hydrological and Meteorological Monitoring and Forecasting Expansion","Further strengthening and expansion of monitoring, forecasting and institutional mechanism for dissemination of timely and more accurate hydrological and meteorological information in particular, to ensure safety of cultivation and to prepare for adverse effect of disasters.",""],[1,"162","19","Flood Studies Promotion","Promote studies on floods.",""],[1,"162","20","Flood Control and Drainage Infrastructure Construction","Construct flood-control and drainage structures for minimizing natural disasters caused by floods.",""],[1,"162","21","Flood Mitigation and Community Education Initiative","Undertake actions to mitigate floods areas having high economic potential, through imparting education to communities via mass media.",""],[1,"162","22","Support for People in Water-Related Disaster Areas","Respond to the needs of people residing in areas affected by drought, flood and other calamities caused by water.",""],[1,"162","23","Flood Mitigation Participation and Support Measures","Encourage people and institutions to participate in flood mitigation: identifying flood- safe grounds; providing materials and machineries, education; and disseminating new technologies.",""],[1,"163","1","Flood Disaster Mitigation Participation","Participate in national and international programs aimed at mitigating the impact of flood disasters.",""],[1,"163","2","Emergency Paddy Crop Water Pumping Support","Be prepared to pump water for rescuing the paddy crop in areas facing water shortage, especially those near water sources but not covered by irrigation systems.",""],[1,"163","10","River and Lake Water Level Maintenance for Navigation and Ecosystem Sustainability","Maintain water discharge and minimum water level in rivers and lakes to ensure navigation and sustainability of the ecosystem.",""],[1,"163","12","Reservoir and Natural Lake Flood Control Strengthening","Strengthen reservoirs and natural lakes having the capacity to store water to help control floods.",""],[1,"163","15","Meteorological and Hydrological Systems Strengthening","Strengthen meteorological and hydrological systems.",""],[1,"163","16","Emergency Forecasting and Public Warning System","Forecast and announce emergencies to people living in areas affected by droughts, floods and other fragilities.",""],[1,"163","17","Meteorological and Hydrological Monitoring Station Network","Set up meteorological and hydrological stations, rain gauge stations, and water staff gauges at important locations and rivers.",""],[1,"163","18","Hydrological Observation Systems Installation","Install hydrological observation systems measure water levels, water discharge rates, and other hydrological data.",""],[1,"163","19","Meteorological Observation and Weather Forecasting Systems","Install meteorological observation systems to receive accurate weather data and weather forecasting.",""],[1,"163","20","Public Weather Forecast Information and Education Service","Provide to public, weather forecast information, advice and education to enhance their understanding on how to minimize the impact of natural events: storm, lightening, storm, flood etc.",""],[1,"163","21","Geographical Mapping for Water Resources Management","Develop geographical map for irrigation systems, flood control systems, polders, river basins, inundated land areas, and water resources management.",""],[1,"164","13","Flood Mitigation and Flood Prevention Capacity Building","Maximize the mitigation of flood effects and build capacities to prevent floods.",""]],"94":[[1,"153","7","Rural Safe Drinking Water and Sanitation Improvement","Improvement of accessibility to safe-drinking water (from multiple sources) and sanitation in rural communities residing in water-scarce areas, as well as water for irrigation.",""],[1,"153","7","Community-Led Local Sanitation Innovation","innovations in sanitation at localized environments need encouragement, preferably with participation from communities (CLTS).",""],[1,"154","15","Health and Sanitation Education and Rural Latrine Construction","Continue to educate (people) about health care and sanitation and construct latrines for citizens in the rural community.",""],[1,"154","16","Rural Clean Water Supply and Infrastructure Maintenance","Continue providing clean water to rural areas through repair, maintenance and construction of wells, ponds, giant jars.",""],[1,"154","17","National Rural Water Supply and Sanitation M&E System","Establish a national M&E System on rural water supply and sanitation.",""],[1,"154","18","Safe Water Supply and Sanitation Budget Strategy","Prepare a budget strategy for safe water supply and sanitation focusing on the poor and vulnerable households.",""],[1,"154","19","Sub-national Roles for Rural Water and Sanitation Delivery","Define roles for sub-national agencies, in particular communes/sangkats and districts, in delivery of safe rural water supply and sanitation services, in line with the guidelines and capacity building programs.",""],[1,"154","20","National Behavior Change Program","Design a national program on change of behavior.",""],[1,"154","22","Water and Sanitation Financing Strategy for Poor and Vulnerable Households","Develop a financing strategy for water and sanitation focusing mainly on poor and vulnerable households.",""],[1,"154","23","Sub-national Water and Sanitation Service Delivery Guidelines and Capacity Building","Define the roles of sub-national government (communes and districts) in the delivery of water and sanitation related services by providing them with guidelines on the implementation and capacity building programs.",""],[1,"154","25","Health and Sanitation Education and Rural Latrine Construction","Continue to educate [people] about health care and sanitation as well as construct latrines in rural communities.",""]],"95":[[1,"161","6","Expansion of Clean Water Supply Coverage","Further expanding the coverage of clean water supply to the rural and urban areas through the rigorous implementation of \"The National Strategy for Rural Water Supply and Sanitation 2011-2025\", including formulation of a clear action plan and encouraging participation from the private sector.",""],[1,"161","9","Clean Water Supply Expansion","RGC will strive to provide clean water supply to the people for better livelihoods in accordance with the Cambodia Millennium Development Goals (CMDGs)",""],[1,"164","12","Year-Round Clean Water Supply Assurance","Ensure that sufficient clean water is available to meet the water requirements in all sectors for the whole year.",""],[1,"165","17","Water Connection Subsidy Program for Poor and Vulnerable Households","Implement the \"Water for All\" program focusing on targeted subsidies for connecting the poorest and most vulnerable households.",""],[1,"165","19","Water Production and Distribution Facility Rehabilitation","Rehabilitate existing water production and distribution facilities with resources from the RGC, waterworks' own funds, and external financial support from development partners.",""],[1,"166","2","Water Quality Control Systems Development","Develop efficient water quality control systems and quality of water supplies that will conform to the National Drinking-Water Quality Standards and Guidelines.",""],[1,"166","4","Urban Water Supply Disaster Risk Management Collaboration","Collaborate with the National Committee for Disaster Management and prepare for the increasing risks attributed to climate change and participate in disaster risk management activities to minimize impacts on the urban water supply sector.",""],[1,"166","5","Water Source Protection and Regulatory Enforcement","Improve water source protection and enforcement of regulations:",""],[1,"166","6","Source Water Quality Protection Collaboration","Collaborate with relevant agencies to protect water quality at source to ensure appropriate volumes of raw water and reduce the cost of water treatment.",""],[1,"166","7","Water Supply Development and Wastewater Treatment Improvement","Water supply development will protect public health and the environment, gradually reducing the quantities of wastes from water treatment facilities discharging into the natural watercourses without effective treatment.",""],[1,"166","8","Environmental Impact Assessment Requirement for Development Projects","Development projects will have clear environmental impact assessments to ensure that projects have environmental impacts within legal limits.",""],[1,"166","9","Standards-Based Affordable Water Service Delivery","Development will comply with national technical standards and use appropriate technologies to ensure affordable water tariffs and sustainable levels of service.",""],[1,"173","4","Clean Water Supply Network Expansion","to widen the clean water supply network;",""]],"96":[[1,"55","7","Hydrological Station Installation and Repair","Installing five hydrological stations along the Mekong, Tonle Sap and Basac rivers and repairing one hydrological station.",""],[1,"55","9","River Water Level Monitoring Infrastructure","Installing 31 water levels measuring boards and repairing three at check points along major rivers.",""],[1,"55","10","River Water-Discharge Measurement Installation","Installing two water-discharge measuring instruments along major rivers.",""],[1,"55","12","Climate Observation Station Installation and Upgrade","Installing 3 new climate-observation stations and upgrading five climate-observation stations in provinces.",""],[1,"55","13","Rainfall Measurement Station Installation and Repair","Installing18 stations and repairing 26 stations for measuring rain precipitation.",""],[1,"55","14","Installation of Automatic Instruments in Climate Observation Stations","Installing other automatic instruments in eight climate-observation stations.",""]],"97":[[1,"39","15","Urban Master Planning and Town Land Use Planning","Master plans and town land use plans are being established for Kep Town and Preah Sihanouk town.",""],[1,"39","17","District Master Planning and Land Use Planning","Master plans and land use plans are being established for Taveng district, Andong Meas district, and Oyadao district in Rattanak Kiri Province.",""],[1,"40","6","National Committee for Land Management and Urban Planning","Royal Decree on the Establishment of a National Committee for Land Management and Urban Planning.",""],[1,"40","7","Committee for Land Management and Urban Planning Establishment","Sub-Decree on the Establishment of a Committee for Land Management and Urban Planning at the Municipal, Provincial, District, and Khan Levels.",""],[1,"40","9","Draft Land Management and Urban Planning Law","A Draft Law on Land Management and Urban Planning is also being prepared.",""],[1,"207","8","Urban Development and Economic Corridor Linkage Programme","Monitoring movement of people within the country in consonance with the implementation of strengthened land management and urban planning policies, and focus on: (1) Development of Phnom Penh, and other key economic poles, satellite cities and urban areas of the country while making efforts to create jobs in these communities; and (2) Linking satellite cities and urban areas with important economic poles and centers to form economic corridors.",""],[1,"207","13","Urban and Agglomeration Management Improvement","RGC will strengthen urban and agglomeration management to make cities clean with full sanitary facilities, fresh air, green spaces, and gymnasium complexes.",""]],"98":[[1,"18","12","Armed Forces Reform","and (iv) reform of the armed forces.",""],[1,"25","7","Armed Forces Organizational and Capability Reform","RCAF has reform the organizational structure and has strengthened the technical and fighting capacity.",""],[1,"25","7","Policy Development for Category 2 and Retired Armed Forces Personnel","It has also developed policies for the Armed Forces of Category 2, and those retired.",""],[1,"25","9","RCAF Capacity Building and Modernization","RCAF has been conducting training in combat and diplomatic skills, learning new technologies, knowledge and skills in defence, upgrading weaponry, and participating in peace missions under the umbrella of the United Nations.",""],[1,"25","11","Military Commercial Activities and Income Generation Department","The RCAF has been authorized to undertake commercial activities since 2012.",""],[1,"26","1","Female Military Advancement and Gender Awareness Initiative","The RCAF has been encouraging female military officers to move up the organizational ladder",""],[1,"26","3","RCAF Capacity Strengthening in Defence, Industry, and Skills","RCAF still needs strengthening defence activities, defence industry, business development, science, technical and vocational knowledge, and skills.",""],[1,"26","5","Military Community Development Partnerships","Military Community Development: Strategic development partnerships for long-term investment cooperation require putting in place.",""],[1,"26","7","Democratic Governance Consolidation","RGC is committed to make every endeavour to ensure that these hard earned gains continue to enhance and get fully integrated into the Cambodian society and psyche.",""],[1,"72","24","Cambodia Veterans' Association Support","The RGC continued implementing Cambodia Veterans' Association in order to",""],[1,"102","1","National Sovereignty and Territorial Protection","protection of national sovereignty and territory.",""],[1,"116","1","Armed Forces Reform","the Royal Government has firmly implemented key reform programs, including: (4) reform of armed forces",""],[1,"122","12","Armed Forces Reform and Capacity Strengthening","The Royal Government has implemented reform programs and strengthened the capacity of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCRF).",""],[1,"122","12","Continued Armed Forces Reform","In the Fifth Legislature, the Royal Government will continue reforming the armed forces to ensure the effective defense of sovereignty, territorial integrity, security and social order of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Based on the available resources and the evolving international and domestic security situation, the reform will focus on:",""],[1,"122","13","Professional Competence Enhancement for RCAF and National Police","Enhancing professional competence of RCAF and National Police through further implementation of the 'Three Strategies and Ten Operation and Development Actions' program, including by updating and promoting the implementation of Cambodia's National Police Strategic Plan aimed at improving the effective functioning of police, particularly through adoption and enforcement of necessary laws and regulations.",""],[1,"122","14","Armed Forces Modernization and Training Enhancement","Developing human resources and enhancing the capability of the armed forces through technological modernization, improving the quality of training of soldiers, inducting youth into the military to build a young armed force, and strengthening cooperation with other countries.",""],[1,"122","16","Armed Forces Welfare and Logistics Support","Supplying technical equipment and promoting welfare of the armed forces, especially through more effective management of supplies, logistics and finances for units stationed on the frontiers and island territories.",""],[1,"123","2","Inter-Branch Armed Forces Cooperation and Civil Support Programme","Enhancing cooperation between the different branches of the armed forces and between armed forces and line ministries and institutions; further strengthening the tradition of good relations between the armed forces and the public (especially during natural disasters and humanitarian operations); and involving military personnel in farming, building civilian physical infrastructure, and protecting environment and natural resource.",""],[1,"123","4","RCAF Human Resources Development Programme","Developing human resources in RCAF for business, agriculture, handicraft, small and medium industry, mining and information technology, so that the community becomes self-sufficient.",""],[1,"123","5","Gender Equality Promotion in RCAF","Promoting gender equality in RCAF by encouraging leadership and participation in decision- making processes and equal access to benefits for women.",""],[1,"123","7","Green Investment Projects for Military Community Energy Generation","Developing green investment projects particularly in energy generation to support other development activities in the military community.",""]],"99":[[1,"63","12","Tourism Service Quality Improvement Initiative","During the Fourth Legislature, the Ministry of Tourism (MOT) focused on improving the quality of tourism services in order to attract visitors, make them extension their stay, and attract new investments in the tourism sector.","Ministry of Tourism (MOT)"],[1,"63","13","Open Sky Policy Implementation and Tourism Promotion Campaign","Continued to implementing the Open Sky Policy and advertising Cambodia - Kingdom of Wonder and promoting the contest for \"clean city\", \"clean resort\", and \"good service\".",""],[1,"63","16","Tourism Law Dissemination and Enforcement","Continued disseminating the Law on Tourism to concerned institutions in particular private sector in order to effectively enforce this Law and improve the quality of tourism goods and services.",""],[1,"63","17","Domestic Tourist Travel Facilitation","Facilitated travel and transportation, and reduce unnecessary barriers that restrict tourist travel within the country.",""],[1,"64","9","National Eco-Tourism Strategic Policy","National Eco-Tourism Strategic Policy (on-going).",""],[1,"64","16","Tourism Promotional Board Establishment","A Tourism Promotional Board-meant to encourage the private sector and public to promote the tourism industry-is yet to be established.",""],[1,"99","22","Tourism Policy Implementation","Continue implementing Tourism Policy.",""],[1,"102","1","Tourism Development Programme","Tourism Development;",""],[1,"173","4","Tourism Infrastructure Development","and to expand the infrastructure system for tourism.",""],[1,"175","22","Tourism Service Quality and Investment Promotion","Ministry of Tourism (MOT) will focus on improving the quality of tourism services, extension of stay, and new investments.","Ministry of Tourism (MOT)"],[1,"175","23","Tourism Infrastructure Improvement","Improving infrastructure related to tourism in the country.",""],[1,"175","24","National Tourism Institute Establishment","Establishing National Tourism Institute for research, study and analysis on the tourism sector.",""],[1,"175","25","Tourism Standards Improvement Initiative","Improving tourism standards to improve product quality.",""],[1,"175","26","Regional Tourism Development Plan","Drawing up the regional tourism development plan.",""],[1,"175","28","National Tourism Center Establishment","Establishing and putting in place, the National Tourism Center.",""],[1,"175","29","Tourism Marketing Strategic Plan","Preparing and implementing the Tourism Marketing Strategic Plan.",""],[1,"175","30","Marketing and Promotion Board","Creating Marketing and Promotion Board in private and public partnership.",""],[1,"175","31","Tourism Security and Safety Systems Strengthening","Strengthening tourism security and safety systems at tourist destinations.",""]],"100":[[1,"180","10","Overseas Worker Recruitment Administration and Protection Measures","Further strengthening the administration of the recruitment of labor to work abroad, as well as enhancing protection of rights, health and safety of Cambodian overseas workers.",""],[1,"181","9","Management Procedures for Cambodian Workers Overseas","Improve procedures for the management of Cambodian workers overseas, both legally and illegally.",""],[1,"181","10","Establish Labor Attachés in Cambodian Embassies","Prepare principles to request RGC to establish labor attachés in Cambodian embassies in countries which have over 3,000 Cambodian laborers.",""],[1,"181","11","Protection Measures for Informal Overseas Cambodian Workers","Take measures to protect Cambodian laborers working overseas informally, particularly in Thailand, to ensure them basic rights.",""]],"101":[[1,"173","5","Trade Market Access Expansion through Regional Integration Obligations","RGC will make further efforts to expand access to international markets through implementing of its obligations under the framework of WTO, ASEAN, and sub-regional and regional economic integration initiatives.",""],[1,"173","11","Trade Facilitation Streamlining and Cross-Border Transport Reform","Further improving trade facilitation through streamlined administrative structures and procedures, and cross border transport processes, reduced costs of doing business and strengthened inter-agency coordination.",""],[1,"175","2","Trade Sector Program Implementation Strengthening","Strengthen the implementation of the Trade Sector Program, focusing on trade facilitation and the private sector development.",""],[1,"175","10","Trade Rules Transparency and WTO-ASEAN Compliance Reform","Enforce reforms as required under the WTO and ASEAN, as certain market access through trade negotiations, and have transparent trade rules and laws.",""],[1,"175","12","Technical Standards and SPS Requirements Strengthening","Strengthen Technical Standards and SPS Requirements.",""],[1,"175","14","Intellectual Property Rights Compliance Improvement","Increase adherence to Intellectual Property Rights.",""]],"102":[[1,"175","3","Export Promotion and Diversification Initiative","Continue promoting exports of agricultural products and garments, and also attempt to diversify.",""],[1,"175","5","National and International Trade Fair Promotion","Organize more national and international trade fairs.",""],[1,"175","11","Trade Logistics Improvement and Trade Cost Reduction","Increase Cambodia's competitiveness through reduced import/export costs and increase in competitiveness through improved trade logistics.",""],[1,"175","13","Export Investment Environment Improvement","Create investment environment for exports.",""],[1,"175","15","Garment Export Market Diversification Initiative","Continue to grow and diversify markets for garments through targeting new markets, increasing domestic inputs, and expanding in higher value products.",""],[1,"175","16","Footwear Export Market Diversification","Continue to grow and diversify footwear exports through developing new markets.",""],[1,"175","18","Light Engineering Industrial Cluster Development","Develop industrial clusters for light engineering.",""],[1,"175","19","Processed Food Sector Diversification and Market Expansion","Continue to grow and diversify in the processed food sector seeking new markets, moving to higher value products, and expanding domestic inputs.",""],[1,"175","20","Cassava Export Diversification Initiative","Increase cassava exports to China and Korea, and lessen dependency on exports of unprocessed tubers to Thailand and Vietnam.",""],[1,"175","21","Rubber Production and Export Expansion","Increase rubber production and export.",""]],"103":[[1,"175","6","Market Surveillance Strengthening","Strengthen effectiveness of market surveillance to protect the health and well-being of consumers.",""],[1,"175","7","Effective Law Enforcement Promotion","Promote effective law enforcement.",""]],"104":[[1,"203","6","Social Land Concessions and Land Grants for Vulnerable Groups","Further implementing measures to distribute land through social land concessions and land grants to the poor, handicapped soldiers, and families of deceased soldiers and former combatants who are either landless or with limited land, in accordance with RGC's land reform policy.",""],[1,"206","21","Social Land Concessions and Veteran Housing Support","Continue to provide lands under social land concessions and building houses for armed forces veterans and their families.",""],[1,"206","23","Veteran Development Site Sustainability and Housing Construction","Continue sustainability of Veteran Development Site donated by Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Keti Prit Buntit, and continue to build houses for veterans and their families through veteran association.",""]],"105":[[1,"18","12","Land Reform","other reform programs including public financial management reform, land reform, and forestry and fisheries reform, is to strengthen the capacity, efficiency and quality of public services",""],[1,"38","9","Land Reform Programme","The RGC's land reform programme is focused on measures to strengthen land management, land distribution and land use, to ensure the security of land ownership, to eradicate illegal land holding, and to prevent concentration of unused land in few hands.",""],[1,"38","9","Social Land Concessions for Farmers","Land reform is also crucial for the increase and allocation of agricultural land within the framework of granting social land concessions to farmers in order to enhance agricultural productivity and diversification, and rural poverty reduction.",""],[1,"38","12","Foreign Ownership Rights for Co-owned Private Buildings Law","Law on granting rights of ownership for Private Entities/Properties of Co-owned Buildings to Foreigners.",""],[1,"39","8","Land Management Student Training Programme","Moreover, 269 undergraduate students in land management and 296 associate degree students are being trained at the Faculty of Land Management and Land Administration.",""],[1,"39","21","Preparation of Legal Instruments for Program Implementation","Preparation of legal instruments to ensure the high efficient and effective implementation of the Program:",""],[1,"41","13","Land Titling and Tenure Security Programme","People in all places need land titles to ensure their land tenure security, to reduce land disputes and to improve their living standards, as well as to develop the national economy.",""],[1,"44","11","Community Development Volunteer Support for Land Measurement","Voluntary activities for community development: The FA also sent 198 personnel to join the national and provincial working groups and voluntary youth groups to facilitate land measurement activities.",""]],"106":[[1,"49","3","Rural Credit Provision to Households and Small Businesses","Decentralization of public services and provision of rural credit to households and small businesses are two of examples of the RGC's efforts in this sector.",""],[1,"50","25","Rural Credit Provision through NGO and Microfinance Cooperation","Cooperating with NGOs, microfinance enterprises in offering rural credit.",""],[1,"73","1","Family Livelihood and Community Development Support","improve family living condition, participation in local development, credit fund and death relief fund, house construction, and veteran community development.",""],[1,"74","7","Productive Assets and Livelihood Support Program","A new implementation modality of a cash for work program has been tested, the Productive Assets and Livelihood Support Program, which has increased national ownership and developed sub-national capacities to manage labour-intensive programs.",""],[1,"154","26","Border Region Village Development Programme","Continue to develop the villages at the border regions to the west and north (Cambodia-Thailand borders) and the triangle area of Cambodia, Vietnam and Laos.",""],[1,"154","27","Family Food Security Program","Continue to implement the Family Food Security Program in villages.",""],[1,"154","28","Ethnic Minority Development and Conservation Center","Construct an ethnic minority development and conservation center in Mondul Kiri.",""],[1,"154","29","Rural Credit Service Strengthening","Continue to strengthen credit service to the rural poor people.",""],[1,"154","30","Small-Scale Business and Enterprise Development","Develop small-scale businesses and enterprises.",""],[1,"214","1","Private Sector Investment for Economic Diversification","First, these investments would have to be made in the private sector to sustain and foster growth and diversification of the economic base, in particular of the rural economies.",""],[1,"214","1","Public Sector Support for Rural and Remote Area Development","Second, they require to be made in the public sector to provide coordinated support to expand and diversify the economic base, in particular of the rural economies, the hinterland and remote areas to alleviate poverty, continue mitigating the adverse effects of the global downturn (especially on the poor), support expansion and efficient delivery of the social sector services (to achieve CMDG targets), and strengthen the capacity of RGC institutions to deliver their programs and services efficiently.",""],[1,"214","5","Targeted Rural Economy Development and Diversification Support","Resources required to provide targeted support for the development and diversification of the rural economy to alleviate poverty in rural and remote areas and the hinterland.",""],[1,"214","8","Targeted Rural Economy Development and Diversification Support","resources required to provide targeted support for the development and diversification of rural economies to alleviate poverty in rural and remote areas (including disaster management) at 7,560.22 billion Riels or USD 1.84 billion",""],[1,"214","8","Expansion of Social Sector Services","resources to expand social sectors services to achieve CMDGs targets at 3,781.73 billion Riels or USD 922.3 million",""],[1,"215","4","Targeted Support for Rural Economic Development and Diversification","Targeted support for the development and diversification of rural economies to alleviate poverty in rural and remote areas",""]],"107":[[1,"172","3","National Science and Technology Development Strategy","During the Fifth Legislature RGC will continue develop all sectors in the purpose of achieving the vision of Cambodia's National Master Plan of Science and Technology which is Making the Leap to an Innovative S&T Nation.",""],[1,"172","5","Institutionalization of National Science and Technology","Institutionalization of National S&T: Establishes the legal system and the S&T national agenda and presents the organization to lead the S&T.",""],[1,"172","6","Science and Technology Human Resource Development","Cultivation of S&T Human Resource: Secures quantitative extension and qualitative enhancement of S&T man power through securing the technicians and fostering the researchers.",""],[1,"172","7","Systemization of Science and Technology Financial Support","Systemization of S&T Financial Support: Enhances the recognition and investment intention of government for securing the continuous investment in S&T.",""],[1,"172","8","Government-Driven Research and Development Promotion","Government-driven R&D: Introduces the technologies necessary for national development and promotes the R&D for securing the technologies.",""],[1,"172","9","International Science and Technology Cooperation Promotion","Promotes international technology cooperation based on technology transfer and S&T manpower development.",""],[1,"172","10","Systematic S&T Information Collection and Utilization","Promotion of S&T Information: A systematic collection and utilization of S&T information in order to support the reasonable S&T policy decision making and R&D activities of enterprises.",""],[1,"172","11","Public Awareness and Participation in Science and Technology","Enhancement of public awareness of S&T: Provides various PR activities and opportunities to participate in order to make the public understand the importance of S&T and enhance their interests in S&T.",""],[1,"177","12","Science, Technology and Metrology Industry Policy Development","Preparing science, technology and metrological industry policy with the objective to increase research and development capability of Cambodia in responding to the projected needs of national development in the next higher phase, in particular ensuring consistency with the industrial development policy and agricultural development policy as they evolve.",""]],"108":[[1,"30","4","Budget Expenditure Management Improvement","Budget expenditure management too has improved, enhancing accuracy in forecasting expenditure requirements and linking these with national priorities.",""],[1,"212","3","Bottom-Up Public Investment Planning and Resource Allocation Process","the MOP has been asking each line ministry/agency to provide information on their Public Investment Requirements for regularly for this information to be incorporated into the three-year Public Investment Program (PIP) Cycle.","MOP | line ministry/agency"],[1,"212","3","Strengthening of Planning and Resource Allocation Capacity","RGC will further strengthen and refine the planning and resource allocation processes and the capacities of the governmental institutions, to ensure that the data required for development planning and public investment resources allocation purposes are more readily available in the times to come.","RGC | governmental institutions"],[1,"214","8","Public Sector Investment Programme for Prioritized Policies","RGC has set a target of 46,225.38 billion Riels (USD 11.27 billion) for public sector investments to implement RGC's prioritized policies for the Fifth Legislature.",""],[1,"215","7","Public Sector Capital Expenditure Financing for Investment Projects","Within the framework of the Medium-Term Expenditure Framework (MTEF), RGC has allocated 8,004.6 billion Riels (USD 1.95 billion) for public sector capital expenditures, which could be leveraged to attract financing from the traditional and non-traditional development partners and the private sector, to implement the investment projects during the Fifth Legislature.",""],[1,"217","5","Identification of High-Priority Public Investment Requirements","Identify high priority public investment requirements, which include those stated in the five-year National Strategic Development Plans (NSDP) and the three- year rolling Public Investment Programme (PIP).",""],[1,"217","8","National Strategic Development Plan Preparation Methodology Refinement","RGC will further refine the methodology in preparing future National Strategic Development Plans",""],[1,"217","8","Public Investment Resource Envelope Development","the preparation of a public investment resource envelope that will serve as an operational and financing tool to implement policy priorities identified in the NSDP",""],[1,"217","8","Three-Year Rolling Public Investment Programme Strengthening","The process of preparing the three-year rolling PIP will be strengthened",""],[1,"217","10","Sequenced Priority Ranking for PIP Projects","RGC institutions will assign a sequenced priority ranking to projects for which they are seeking resources to implement through the planning period of PIP, taking into account the overall macroeconomic environment and an awareness of the scope, to mobilize external resources based on recent trends.",""],[1,"217","11","Public Investment Program Funding Screening","RGC will ensure that only those programs and projects that are part of the PIPs are included in a consideration for funding during the formulation of the Budget Strategic Framework.",""],[1,"218","2","Public Investment Planning and Budget Linkage Refinement","These methodological refinements will on the one hand ensure a closer linkage between the RGC's policy priorities, actions, programs and projects and the public investment resources required to implement the planned activities.",""]],"109":[[1,"140","4","Land Management and Urbanization Law Preparation","Promoting the preparation of Law on Land Management and Urbanization and Law on Agricultural Land.",""],[1,"141","14","Land Sector Public-Private Partnership Policy","Prepare a Policy on Public and Private Partnership (PPP) on the land sector.",""],[1,"141","16","Land Management and Urban Planning Law Reform","Make and approve the Law on Land Management and Urban Planning, and related legal policy documents for implementing this Law.",""],[1,"141","17","Land Management and Urban Planning Committee Implementation","Adopt and use effectively, according to the hierarchy as set by the Policy on Land Management of the Kingdom of Cambodia, the Royal Decree and Sub-decree on the Establishment of a Committee for Land Management and Urban Planning at all levels for land management plan in municipalities and provinces, especially for Phnom Penh City and provinces that lie along the coastal areas; master plans and land use plans for municipalities and urban areas of provinces lying next to the borders of Cambodia, Vietnam and Laos.",""],[1,"142","1","Coastal Zones Management and Development Implementation","Enhance the effective implementation of Cambodia's coastal zones management and development through the Circular on Coastal Zones Management and Development, and to push for adoption and implementation of integrated strategy for developing Cambodia's costal zones and Preah Sihanouk Master Plan",""],[1,"142","2","National Housing Policy Implementation for Poor Households","Continue to adopt the National Housing Policy in order to resolve housing problems for poor people so they can live in safety, welfare, and in dignity.",""],[1,"142","3","Technical Support for Local Master Plans and Land Use Plans","Continue to provide technical support to the councils of all municipalities, districts, khans, communes, and sangkats in the preparation of master plans and land use plans.",""],[1,"142","4","Land Management and Urban Planning Statistics Strengthening","Strengthen the effectiveness of work on collection, compilation, and production, as well as the dissemination of data and statistics for land management and urban planning.",""],[1,"142","10","Construction Sector Investment Coordination and Private Sector Partnership","Coordinate and facilitate the investments in the construction sector by paying attention to the strengthening of partnership with the private sector to boost the country's economy and create employment opportunities for citizens.",""],[1,"142","11","Construction Law and Standards Adoption","Prepare and adopt the Construction Law, construction standards, sub-decrees, and legal policy documents relating to the construction work for effective implementation.",""],[1,"142","11","Technical Staff Capacity Strengthening for Construction Administration","Strengthen mechanism and capacity of technical staff in order to effectively improve the administrative services, and continue to implement the de-concentration policy in the construction sector.",""],[1,"142","12","Public Dissemination of Construction Permit Procedures","Continue to widely disseminate to the general public the legal policy documents relating to construction work and the procedures on requesting a permit for building constructions.",""],[1,"143","1","Construction Sector Capacity Building and Competitiveness Programme","Enhance the capacity of physical persons and legal persons who make professions in the construction sector, and to better uphold the local construction industry to be able to compete, study/implement the construction project, and build mega constructions by ourselves, as well as to provide reliable services with quality and effectiveness both in the country and in the regions.",""],[1,"143","2","Construction Sector Data and Statistics Strengthening","Strengthen the effectiveness of work on collection, compilation, and production, as well as the dissemination of data and statistics for the construction sector.",""],[1,"145","7","Land Use Policy and Spatial Planning","Develop land use planning that allows for holistic planning across sectors, jurisdictions and local government borders (Land Use Policy and Spatial Planning).",""]],"110":[[1,"104","13","Security and Cash Clearing Infrastructure Development","Build a supporting infrastructure for a 'Security Keeping System', 'Security Verifying System', 'Security Clearing System', and 'Cash Clearing System'.",""],[1,"104","15","Regulation of Non-Banking Institutions under the Law of Trust","Bring the non-banking institutions' operations to fall under the Law of Trust.",""]],"111":[[1,"86","5","Women’s Leadership Promotion in Government Institutions","RGC has been increasing the number of women in leadership positions through incentives and by appointing women as leaders in ministries and institutions.",""],[1,"87","1","Sectoral Gender Mainstreaming Action Plans","MOWA has provided technical expertise to the line ministries to formulate their sectoral Gender Mainstreaming Action Plans (GMAP).","MOWA | the line ministries"]],"112":[[1,"120","5","Civil Service Human Resources Policy Implementation","Strengthening the management and development of human resources within the Civil Service through the implementation of the Policy on Human Resources to enhance performance within the Civil Service and uphold values of service, motivation, loyalty and professionalism.",""],[1,"121","8","Human Resource Management and Development Legal and Regulatory Reform","Review and amend the legal and regulatory base for HR management and development.",""],[1,"121","9","Work Organization and Role Clarification Reform","Enhance the organization of work through clarifying roles and responsibilities between units and the use of position descriptions.",""],[1,"121","10","Human Resource Planning and Rolling Staffing Plans","Further develop HR planning including medium and long term rolling plans addressing recruitment, deployment, training and succession needs.",""],[1,"121","11","Human Resource Management Process Streamlining","Streamline HR management processes making them more transparent and merit.",""],[1,"121","12","Performance Management System Development and Deployment","Develop and deploy a Performance Management System linked to promotion, deployment, compensation and training and development processes.",""],[1,"121","13","Ethics and Discipline Standards Implementation Strengthening","Strengthen the implementation of standards of ethics and discipline.",""],[1,"121","14","Competency Profile Development and Deployment","Develop and deploy competency profiles for selected positions.",""],[1,"121","20","Ministerial Human Resources Capacity Development","Further develop the capacity of ministerial HR units and staff.",""]],"114":[[1,"116","1","Anti-Corruption Reform Program","the Royal Government has firmly implemented key reform programs, including: (1) the fight against corruption",""],[1,"116","3","Anti-Corruption Law Formulation and Adoption","The government is strongly committed to formulate and adopt the anti-corruption law consistent with other fundamental laws to ensure coherence and consistency among different laws and their effective implementation, as soon as possible, in close consultation with all concerned parties.",""],[1,"116","4","Anti-Corruption Measures Strengthening","the Royal Government will further strengthen and enhance the effectiveness of three key measures",""],[1,"116","5","Anti-Corruption Law Dissemination and Awareness Campaign","RGC will further promote the dissemination of the Anti-corruption Law in all forms to both public and private sectors to raise awareness of the consequences of corruption and to discourage corrupt practices.",""],[1,"116","6","Civil Service Integrity and Ethics Framework","RGC will further encourage civil servants at all levels to conduct themselves with dignity, observe moral integrity and professional ethics, and effectively implement the principle of avoiding incompatibility of functions and conflict of interests stipulated by law and related regulations by preparing and implementing internal rules in addition to existing laws and regulations, including preparation of strategic plan, strategy, internal rules, code of professional ethics, and regulations to create an agency with moral integrity to serve as a role models for efficient and successful public services.",""],[1,"116","6","Public Oversight and Revenue Management Strengthening Measures","In addition, RGC will take specific measures to strengthen oversight institutions and promote better management of public revenue and expenditure, and expand the scope of the list of public service fees.",""],[1,"116","7","Anti-Corruption Enforcement and Investigation Capacity Strengthening","RGC will continue taking firm and strict measures against those who are found to be involved in corruption, without exception.",""],[1,"117","1","Anti-Corruption Regulations Education and Dissemination","Strengthen and speed-up the work of education, dissemination of corruption-related regulations.",""],[1,"117","2","Public Participation in Anti-Corruption Efforts","Encourage public participation in the fight against corruption.",""],[1,"117","4","Anti-Corruption Strategy Implementation","Anti-Corruption Unit will implement the following interwoven strategies during the Fifth Legislature.",""],[1,"117","5","Corruption Awareness and Public Participation Campaign","Continue raising awareness about all aspects of corruption, including its causes, impacts and consequences to encourage public participation in preventing and fighting corruption.",""],[1,"117","8","Implementation of Public-Private Interest Principles","Strengthen effective implementation of the principles in order to avoid conflict between the public and private interests.",""],[1,"117","9","Anti-Corruption Institutional Capacity Strengthening and Law Enforcement","Continue building and strengthening the institutional capacity, including inspection tasks for management and enforce the effective implementation of the Anti- Corruption Law.",""],[1,"117","11","Freedom to Report Corruption in the Media","Continue to further promote and protect the freedom to seek, obtain and disseminate information on corrupt cases in the media.",""],[1,"117","12","Corruption Awareness Seminars","Continue organizing national and international seminars on corruption for greater exposure and awareness.",""],[1,"117","13","International Anti-Corruption Cooperation and Partnership","Continue international cooperation and partnerships to prevent and combat corruption.",""],[1,"117","15","Private Sector Integrity and Fair Competition Framework","Continue developing and pursuing implementation of policies, legal and regulatory framework and procedures to protect the integrity of the private sector, to prevent collusion and ensure fair competition between private companies/enterprises by ensuring proper behavior, honorable conduct and dignity in all business transactions.",""],[1,"117","16","Public-Private Contract Safeguards","Safeguard the balance between the rights and interests in the contracts made between the public and private sector.",""],[1,"117","18","Anti-Corruption Legal Enforcement","Continue to take strict and severe legal actions against corrupt people to reduce corruption and to build confidence among people.",""],[1,"117","19","Anti-Corruption Priority Programs","The Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection (MONASRI) will continue focusing on fighting corruption through its five key priority programs, in particular its inspection program.","Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection (MONASRI)"],[1,"118","2","Strengthening the Field of Inspection Program","Strengthening the Field of Inspection: This program is aimed at fighting corruption, abuse of power, and misconduct.",""]],"115":[[1,"15","1","E-Governance Modernization Programme","the next phase in good governance will require significant efforts to bring-in e- governance to make governance effective.",""],[1,"23","5","Payroll System Automation through ICT","The payroll system has been automated through ICT.",""],[1,"23","9","Human Resources Management Information System","A Human Resources Management Information System is operational and personnel management mechanisms have been streamlined and steadily strengthened.",""],[1,"58","1","IT Systems and E-Government Development","of IT system and e-Government, and building and enhancing the efficiency of the backbone infrastructure of the information and communication technology sector.",""]],"116":[[1,"65","3","Employment Placement Services for Job-Seekers","The Ministry of Labour and Vocational Training (MOLVT) has been providing employment placement services to assist job-seekers in finding employment in private sector businesses in the country and overseas.","Ministry of Labour and Vocational Training (MOLVT)"],[1,"180","1","National Employment Policy","Developing and implementing a national employment policy to closely align the employment sector to the needs of socio-economic development, in particular by focusing on youth employment, labor force preparedness to respond to the implementation of the Royal Government's development policies, as well as being well prepared in managing and benefiting from Cambodia's participation in ASEAN Economic Community.",""],[1,"180","2","Employment Forum Strengthening","Strengthening the Employment Forum coordinated by the Royal Government and in which job providers, job seekers and education and training service providers participate, aimed at improving exchange of labor market information, counseling and responsiveness to changing market conditions.",""],[1,"180","3","Expansion of Employment Services and Job Centers","Expanding employment services to job seekers and a broader dissemination of information on job opportunities in the country and abroad to the public including counseling and support provided to worker recruitment through expansion of job centers under the National Employment Agency of the National Training Board across the country.",""],[1,"180","4","Labor Market Information System Strengthening","Further developing a sound labor market information system especially through strengthening data collection, analysis and dissemination of labor statistics and information on education and technical and vocational training programs, and providing information to the public on wages and the supply and demand of skills.",""],[1,"181","6","National Employment Policy Implementation","Begin implementing the national employment policy, focusing on job creation for the youth and also prevent a free influx of skilled laborers by 2015 (ASEAN integration).",""],[1,"181","20","Expansion of Front-Line Service Infrastructure","Expand infrastructure for front-line services ensuring that there is at least one in every province.",""],[1,"181","21","ICT-Enabled Public Service Delivery","Enhance use of ICT in providing services such as registration, employment seeking and staff recruitment, to help reduce time and costs.",""],[1,"181","22","Human Resources Development within NEA","Develop human resources within the framework of NEA.",""],[1,"181","23","Labor Market Information Dissemination","Disseminate [information about the] labor service and labor market information through publication, media and field dissemination.",""],[1,"181","24","Labor Market Information Dissemination and Compilation","Participate in labor fairs and workshops, disseminating and compiling labor market information from the existing data.",""],[1,"181","25","Labor Forum Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthen labor forum mechanisms with the participation of labor providers, job seekers and education and training providers.",""]],"117":[[1,"179","16","Labor Market Policy, Regulatory, and Institutional Reform","RGC will further deepen policy reforms and regulatory and institutional frameworks to ensure that all the components of labor market are consistent with each other and are responsive.",""],[1,"180","7","Labor Law and Social Security Scheme Implementation Strengthening","Further improving labor conditions through strengthening the implementation of the labor law and the law on social security schemes for persons defined by provisions of the labor law",""],[1,"180","7","Better Factory Program Support","further supporting the Better Factory Program and improvement of labor market environment",""],[1,"180","8","Trade Union and Labor Law Reform","through adoption of the law on trade unions, updating the labor law",""],[1,"180","8","Labor Dispute Prevention and Resolution Mechanism","institutional strengthening and coordination for implementation of labor dispute prevention and resolution mechanism as well as the mechanism to prevent and address labor protests",""],[1,"180","8","Labor Inspectorate Capacity Strengthening","strengthening capacity and role of labor inspectorate in dispute mediation and resolution",""],[1,"180","8","Labor Courts Establishment","and establishment of labor courts",""],[1,"180","9","Minimum Wage Review and Worker Protection Mechanism","Establishing mechanism to conduct regular and needed studies to provide recommendations for review and setting of minimum wage by region and sector in line with national economic conditions, as well as mechanism to protect the interest of workers and employees in case of factory bankruptcy.",""],[1,"181","1","Labor Law Implementation and Occupational Health and Safety Legal Compilation","Implement provisions in the law on labor and organize compilation of laws and documents on occupational health and safety.",""],[1,"181","2","Labor Law Amendment for Worker Rights and Safe Working Conditions","Amend provisions in the labor law to implement rights and freedoms in relation with health, work safety and good work conditions.",""],[1,"181","3","Workplace Inspection and Child Labor Enforcement","Conduct inspections in enterprises and establishments with the aim of ensuring minimum work standards and ban/withdrawal of child labor.",""],[1,"181","4","Child Labor Legal Information Dissemination","Disseminate legal information to all on child labor.",""],[1,"181","8","Rural Private Enterprise Labor Conditions Compliance","Encourage owners of private enterprises/establishments in rural areas to better abide by work conditions.",""],[1,"181","13","Labor Rights Awareness and Enforcement Strengthening","Disseminate awareness about the basic labor rights to all stakeholders and ensure better enforcement the labor laws.",""],[1,"181","14","Collective Negotiation and Bargaining Promotion","Promote collective negotiation at the enterprise/establishment levels to promote collective bargaining.",""],[1,"181","15","Labor Dispute Resolution Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthen labor dispute resolution mechanisms to promote the rights of workers, employers and trade unions, reduce strikes, and increase compliance to procedures.",""],[1,"181","16","Arbitration Council Dispute Resolution Mechanism","Promote dispute resolution via the mechanism of Arbitration Council (AC) in cases of collective disputes.",""],[1,"181","17","Trade Unions Law Review and Enforcement","Continue [to submit] requests for review and decision on the draft law on trade unions for approval by the national assembly, and then their enforcement.",""],[1,"181","18","Minimum Remuneration Adjustment Mechanism","Maintain data on the conditions of livelihood of workers/employees and modify the minimum remunerations appropriately.",""],[1,"183","2","Workplace Compliance Enforcement through Inspections and Administrative Measures","Enforce via on-site inspections of various enterprises-establishments, occupational injury surveys and administrative measures taken against enterprises and establishments failing to comply with the law.",""]],"118":[[1,"99","10","Public Finance Management Reform","Raise budget revenues (~18% of GDP by 2018), strengthen tax administration, Promote priority sector spending, Enforce results-based budgeting [& Public Finance Management Reform (PFMR)]; Strengthen monetary and fiscal policy (incl. all their instruments).",""],[1,"99","11","Commerce and Finance Regulatory Reform","Establish/implement laws and rules regarding commerce and finance, Improve economic (deficit ≤3%), trade (deficit ≤3%), inflation control (≤ 5%)], Push for implementation.",""],[1,"99","16","Monetary Policy and De-dollarization Measures","Implement monetary policy to make in more effective (esp. de-dollarization), Promote financialization in the economy (promote institutional financial transactions, create more finance institutions/instruments).",""],[1,"99","16","Fiscal Instruments and Macro-Financial Management Capacity Building","Invoke fiscal instruments to achieve the different policy options stated in 'Policy Section' and build capacities in the government on macro financial management.",""],[1,"100","22","Public Debt and Budget Deficit Management","On debt, the plan proposes to continue not to exceed a critical minimum so that managing the public debt does not pose a problem.",""],[1,"102","10","Public Debt Management Continuation","Continue implementing the main principles related to public debt management to maintain sustainability of public debt, promote long-term economic growth, and reduce poverty.",""],[1,"102","11","Debt Risk Management Policy Framework","Formulate and implement the policy framework on debt risk management and continue building capacities in the concerned ministries and other implementing agencies on public debt management.",""],[1,"102","11","Public Debt Management Capacity Building","continue building capacities in the concerned ministries and other implementing agencies on public debt management.",""],[1,"127","4","Coordinated Fiscal Policy and Crisis Resolution Mechanism","Ensuring macroeconomic stability and resiliency of the national economy by further implementing a flexible, coordinated and cross-cutting fiscal policy to be consistent with monetary policy; ... and strengthening institutional coordination of crisis prevention and resolution mechanism.",""],[1,"127","4","Fiscal Space Expansion and Debt Management","increasing \"fiscal space\" and keeping public debt at a manageable level;",""],[1,"128","3","Macroeconomic Stability and Poverty Reduction Policy Framework","RGC will frame policies to ensure macroeconomic stability, low inflation and a stable exchange rate exchange and enable Cambodia to move out of its Least Developed Country Status to become a Lower-middle Income Country by 2018, and a Higher- middle Income Country by 2030.",""],[1,"128","5","Macro-Economic Policy Implementation","Continue to implement macro-economic policy: public financial management policy, along with cautious monetary policy.",""]],"119":[[1,"186","5","Youth Development and Sports Participation Promotion","Further promoting the implementation of National Policy on Youth Development and the National Policy on Physical Education and Sports through inspiring young people to participate in social movements and sports activities",""],[1,"186","6","National Stadium and Sports Facilities Development and Athlete Training Programme","Further developing National Stadium and related sports facilities as well as training of athletes and sportsmen in the fields in which Cambodia has potential to prepare for the hosting of the SEA Game in 2023.",""],[1,"189","2","School Physical Education and Sports Promotion","Promote physical education and sport activities in schools including activities of sports associations, sports clubs and physical infrastructure.",""]],"120":[[1,"220","1","National Monitoring and Evaluation Policy Framework","The Royal Government of Cambodia has rolled out an M&E Policy Framework for the NSDP 2014-2018 cycle, which would provide to the planners and executing agencies an assessment of progress made on a sub-program, program, sector, or the whole economy.",""],[1,"221","10","Bottleneck Analysis Exercises","Ministry of Planning proposes to undertake some of these exercises as it is stated later in this chapter.","Ministry of Planning | MOP"],[1,"221","11","Results Framework Development at National, Sectoral, and Program Levels","During this plan cycle, RGC proposes that the different implementing ministries and agencies develop a RF at least at three levels: national, sectoral and program.",""],[1,"222","5","Macro-Level Development Planning Monitoring and Evaluation","Ministry of Planning (MOP) is assigned the task of monitoring and evaluating the outcome and impact indicators at the macro level, to assess progress made in development planning and consequently in human wellbeing.","Ministry of Planning (MOP)"],[1,"224","12","Applied Research Studies for M&E Linkage Analysis","MOP will conduct a series of applied research studies to establish linkages between inputs, outputs and outcomes at the macro level.","MOP"],[1,"225","10","Province-Level Data Profile Generation Using Administrative Datasets","it should be possible in this plan cycle to generate select data profiles at the province level using administrative datasets.",""],[1,"225","10","Expansion of National Institute of Statistics Data-Generating Processes","Additionally, National Institute of Statistics (NIS) at MOP has expanded the scope of its data-generating processes","National Institute of Statistics (NIS) at MOP"],[1,"226","4","Commune Database Official Statistics Integration","these data can be used only selectively, until the time when the CDB is brought within the domain of 'Official Statistics' and are subject to detailed scrutiny by the user community in the government and/or appropriate statistical authorities that the government appoints.",""],[1,"226","9","Standardization of Definitions and Data Generation Processes","An exercise to standardize of the definitions and data generating processes is undertaken so that different data generating ministries and agencies use the same definitions and data generating processes.",""],[1,"227","1","Standardized Statistical Definitions and Data Sources Agreement","Option 2 thus appears most suitable here, i.e. the government agrees on standard definitions and data sources for the variables and indicators listed in the Core List and the Additional List.",""],[1,"227","10","Online Administrative Databases Development","During this plan period, MRD and MOSVY plan to develop on-line databases and maintain them in electronic form.","MRD | MOSVY"],[1,"227","13","One-off Studies for Agricultural and Market Analysis","One-off studies (farm management studies, market studies, KAP Studies) to establish",""],[1,"228","5","Special Studies on Priority Development Areas","In this plan cycle, RGC aims to consider conducting special studies pertaining to priority areas in development analysis.",""],[1,"228","6","Annual Inter-Ministerial Review Meetings on Studies","MOP proposes convening at least one meeting annually with the concerned line departments to review the needs, modalities and findings (if any) these studies.","MOP | other ministries and agencies | concerned line departments"],[1,"228","13","National Monitoring and Evaluation System for NSDP Implementation","Establishing a National M&E System to monitor and evaluate the progress of implementation of NSDP.",""],[1,"228","14","Monitoring and Evaluation System for the Three-Year Rolling Public Investment Plan","Establishing an M&E System to monitor and evaluate the implementation of all projects carried out by line ministries and agencies in the Three-year rolling Public Investment Plan.",""],[1,"229","1","National Monitoring and Evaluation System","Develop an National M&E System to monitor and evaluate the progress of implementation of NSDP and the implementation of all projects carried out by line ministries and agencies in the Three-Year Rolling Public Investment Plan to strengthen the effectiveness of public investment expenditure, including national budget and cooperate financing.",""],[1,"229","2","National M&E System Technical Guideline and Manual Development","Develop technical guideline and manual of the National M&E System to monitor and evaluate the progress of implementation of NSDP and the implementation of all projects carried out by line ministries and agencies in the Three-Year Rolling Public Investment Plan.",""],[1,"229","3","SMART Indicator Formulation Training for Planning and Statistics Officials","Organize trainings to train officials-in-charge of planning and statistics of concerned line ministries and agencies on how to formulate SMART indicators.",""],[1,"229","4","National M&E System Training for Line Ministries and Agencies","Organize training on how to use the National M&E System to monitor and evaluate the progress of implementation of NSDP and the implementation of all projects carried out by line ministries and agencies in the Three-Year Rolling Public Investment Plan to the focal point officials in all concerned ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"229","5","NSDP Indicator Data Training Programme","Organize trainings on data collection, data analysis and data interpretation for measuring indicators set in NSDP to all focal point officials in all concerned ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"229","6","Technical Assistance for Sector M&E and Results Framework Development","Provide technical assistance to all concerned ministries and agencies for formulating indicators, collecting data, analyzing data and interpreting data, for formulating RF for their sector and setting up the M&E system as requested.",""],[1,"229","8","Dedicated Monitoring and Evaluation Function","Establish a dedicated M&E function to contribute to enhancing the effectiveness of its activities.",""],[1,"229","9","Statistics and M&E Capacity Building","Build capacity on statistics and M&E to the staff in the ministries and at the sub- national levels.",""],[1,"229","10","Ministry and Agency M&E Coordination Strengthening","Improve coordination within each ministry and agency to strengthen the M&E function.",""],[1,"242","4","National Monitoring and Evaluation Working Group","MOP has established a National Working Group on Monitoring and Evaluation (NWGM&E), chaired by MOP.","MOP"]],"121":[[1,"25","10","Demining Operations","RCAF's Engineering Unit, in collaboration with Cambodian Mine Action and Victim Assistance Authority (CMAA) and other mine- action agencies, undertakes demining operations.","Ministry of National Defence (MND)"],[1,"42","10","Mine Action Resource Mobilization and Domestic Financing","This situation requires intensified resource mobilization and increased national contribution to ensure sustainability and efficiency.",""],[1,"141","1","National Mine Clearance and UXO Removal Programme","Stepping up the implementation of the \"National Mine Action Strategy 2010-2019\", especially the clearance of the remaining mines and UXOs of the war to expand arable land, secure safety of infrastructure development and further reduce mine and UXOs explosion accidents.",""],[1,"143","3","National Mine Action Strategy 2010-2019","In close collaboration with concerned institutions, the Cambodian Mine Action and Victim Assistance Authority (CMAA) have formulated National Mine Action Strategy 2010-2019 in order to support the landmines and ERW clearance activities.",""],[1,"143","5","Mine Clearance Planning and Prioritization Improvement","CMAA will continue to improve the current planning and prioritization process, which has now been integrated with the Commune Investment Program.",""],[1,"143","5","Cross-Sector Mine Action Coordination","CMAA will ensure close consultation between mine action and other relevant sectors at all levels to forge a cross-sector synergy and cooperation.",""],[1,"143","5","Land Release Methodology Refinement","Furthermore, the CMAA will continue to refine the application of land release methodologies to release contaminated lands in a cost effective manner.",""]],"122":[[1,"124","4","Prison Renovation and New Prison Construction Programme","MOI will continue improving the conditions of prisons in accordance with that of international standards by renovating dilapidated prisons and equipping them with materials and equipment in proportion to the increased number of prisoners and to start construction of new prisons in the provinces of Kratie, Kampong Cham, Battambang, Pursat, Mondul Kiri, Stung Treng, Kampong Thom, Prey Veng, and Rattanak Kiri, and the construction of fourth re- education center in Pursat.","MOI"],[1,"124","4","Prison Re-education and Rehabilitation Programme","MOI will emphasize on the re-education and rehabilitation of culprits/prisoners in accordance with the policy framework on prison reform and the procedures on the management of prisons, as well as on the education for the inmates on spiritual values, virtue and equity.","MOI"],[1,"124","4","Prison Guards Statute and Prison Human Rights Cooperation","MOI will prepare a Royal Decree on the Statute of Prison Guards and continue to cooperate with the provincial/municipal authorities and NGOs to strengthen law enforcement and respect of human rights in prisons.","MOI"],[1,"124","5","Prison Guard and Officer Refresher Training Programme","Besides, the Police Academy will organize vocational training courses for prison guards and refresher courses for prison officers.",""]],"125":[[1,"34","6","Public Sector Management Capacity Building","Building capacities for improved public sector management.",""]],"126":[[1,"15","3","De-dollarization Policy","De-dollarization, thus, is to assume primacy.",""]],"127":[[1,"18","12","Anti-Corruption Reform","These are: (i) fighting corruption;",""],[1,"18","12","Public Financial Management Reform","other reform programs including public financial management reform, land reform, and forestry and fisheries reform, is to strengthen the capacity, efficiency and quality of public services",""],[1,"19","1","Ministry Focal Point Coordination with ACU","A focal point in each ministry/institution has been established for coordinating their work with ACU.",""],[1,"19","1","Public Service Fee and Duration Schedule","RGC has also set out a public service fee schedule and duration schedule for service provision, which government ministries and institutions are to follow for eliminating loss due to informal payments and other malfunctions within government institutions.",""],[1,"23","6","Performance and Accountability Enhancement Scheme","Innovative schemes to enhance performance and accountability such SOA is being deployed.",""],[1,"23","7","Performance Management and Accountability System","The Performance Management and Accountability System is being implemented to better mobilize human resources and identify capacity development needs.",""]],"128":[[1,"34","10","Crop Production Enhancement Activities","The Ministry of Agriculture, Forests and Fish (MAFF) leads, manages, and carries out activities to enhance crop production","Ministry of Agriculture, Forests and Fish (MAFF)"],[1,"36","11","Pest Research Programme","Continued researching on pests, and found 11 additional rice pests.",""],[1,"37","15","Contract Farming Mechanism","RGC has encouraged the \"Contract Farming Mechanism \"as it is key to ensure markets for farmers.",""],[1,"37","15","Agricultural Products Quality and Safety Law and Related Regulations","MAFF prepared a sub-decree on \"Contract Farming\" in 2011 and has prepared the draft law on \"Agricultural Products Quality and Safety\", and other legal regulations, such as guideline on \"Contract Farming\" and Prakas on \"Agricultural Enterprises and Agro-Industry Statistics Management\".","MAFF"]],"129":[[1,"43","3","Aquaculture Development Policy","Developing aquaculture development is an important additional policy of the Royal Government in order to help ensure food security.",""],[1,"43","3","Rice-Field Fisheries and Community Fish Refuge Ponds","Aquaculture has been implemented through pursuing diverse approaches including enhancing rice-field fisheries and establishing Community Fish Refuge Ponds which can help increase farm aquatic production by up to 15% per annum.",""]],"130":[[1,"46","1","Source and Dumpsite Waste Management Strengthening","MOE has undertaken measures to strengthen waste management at source and at final dumpsites to control environmental pollution.","MOE"],[1,"46","1","Urban Waste Recycling Promotion","MOE has also encouraged urban waste recycling and has tried to coordinate large-scale investments in waste management.","MOE"],[1,"46","1","Sub-national Sewage Management System Strengthening","Additionally, the ministry strengthened the sewage management systems at the sub-national levels, by setting up wastewater treatment plants in the provinces of Battambang, Preah Sihanouk, Siem Reap, the coastal provinces, and provinces surrounding the Tonle Sap Lake.","the ministry"],[1,"46","2","Industrial Pollution Surveillance and Source Control","MOE has improved its surveillance on major pollution sources, e.g. factories and large enterprises, by encouraging installation of liquid waste treatment plants at source, air purification devices before emission, and noise reduction equipment.","MOE"],[1,"46","2","Environmental Quality Monitoring and Pollution Compliance Enforcement","To achieve all this has required the participation of owners of the polluting sources and strict law enforcement, including warnings, fines, and compliance of courts judgments.","MOE"],[1,"46","4","Bio-safety Legal Framework and Laboratory Capacity Strengthening","MOE has made significant progress in bio- safety and biotechnology, including developing a legal framework for reducing risks from modified organisms, and strengthening the capacities of laboratories engaged in biotechnology.","MOE"]],"131":[[1,"23","11","Reform Communication and Outreach Tools","Communication tools have been deployed to inform about the reform (bulletin, website, periodic workshops and seminars).",""],[1,"59","2","Sub-national Community Radio and Local Media Service","They are operated locally in 16 municipalities/provinces, to live-relay major events and also air their own programmes for their community and region on topics ranging from societal education, human rights, and health, especially of women and children.",""],[1,"59","2","Provincial Radio Government Communication and Public Feedback Platform","Provincial radio stations serve as a bridge, linking the government and people by giving messages about government policies for them to take part in national development.",""]],"132":[[1,"61","2","Active Participation in Rules of Origin Negotiations","Cambodia needs to be active in negotiations involving ROOs, including the forthcoming RECP negotiations between the ASEAN and its Dialogue Partners.",""],[1,"61","13","Agricultural and Industrial Value Addition Expansion","Cambodia needs to explore possibilities for adding more value within the country.",""],[1,"61","13","Rice Processing Value Addition","In agriculture, this entails undertaking processing of farm-gate output, as is already underway in rice.",""],[1,"61","13","Manufacturing Value Chain Upgrading","In the case of garments, shoes, and bicycles, attention needs to be paid to produce more in the value-chain and retain a larger component of the value added within the country.",""],[1,"61","14","SME-Export Firm Linkage Promotion","Supply linkages between local SMEs and export firms are important and should be fostered.",""],[1,"61","14","Foreign Direct Investment Promotion for Domestic Input Production","FDI in the production of domestic inputs also needs to be encouraged.",""],[1,"62","3","Facility Upgrading for SPS-Sensitive Producers","In SPS-sensitive sectors (rice, cassava, corn, soy beans, hospitality sector, processed food, fisheries), producers should enhance the quality of their facilities to meet international standards.",""],[1,"62","3","SPS Surveillance and Food Safety Enforcement System","the government should put in place, surveillance and enforcement systems required by the importing countries to control plant pests and animal diseases, monitor use of pesticides, and control food safety.",""],[1,"62","4","Exporter Financial Backstopping through Specialized Financial Institutions","Financial backstopping of exporters through specialized financial institutions has received attention, including in the context of the 2010 Rice Sector Policy, but needs furthering in the coming years.",""],[1,"62","7","Export Promotion for Agriculture Products and Garments","Continued to promote exports of agriculture products, garments and other products as part of its poverty reduction strategy.",""],[1,"69","10","Standards Adoption Promotion for Entrepreneurs","Broadcasted the importance of national and international standards and encourage Cambodian entrepreneurs to adopt them in order to ensure the quality of their products and services.",""]],"133":[[1,"82","8","Tobacco Control Awareness and Smoke-Free Areas Initiative","The main activities include, organizing World No-tobacco days; strengthening the functions of the lnter-ministerial Committee for Education and Reduction of Tobacco Use, and one of Secretariat on Framework Convention on Tobacco Control; educating people on the impact of smoking; and announcing smoke-free areas in",""]],"134":[[1,"90","3","Revenue Gap Reduction and Expenditure Rationalization","The government is now committed to reduce the revenue-expenditure gap, and for doing this it is striving to find newer sources of revenue along with rationalizing expenditures.",""],[1,"91","2","Automatic Tax Declaration System Expansion","General Directorate of Taxation has expanded its automatic tax declaration system in all provinces and has tried to build administrative capacities among the personnel engaged in taxation, auditing, and debt clearance.",""],[1,"91","2","Non-Tax Revenue Collection System Improvement","The government has improved the non-tax revenues collection system as well.",""],[1,"91","2","Payment Slip-Based Non-Tax Revenue Collection","As of now, Payment Slips are being used for collecting non-tax revenues and fees for the economic land concession.",""],[1,"100","21","Revenue Collection and Expenditure Allocation Reform","The national budget revenue collection target has been fixed at increasing revenues and average by 0.5 point of the GDP per year; e.g., it was 13.2% in 2011, which should become at least 14.9 in 2013 and at least 15.4 in 2014.",""],[1,"101","2","Medium-Term Revenue Mobilization Strategy","Aims to review its current Revenue Collection Policy to prepare and carry out a Medium-Term Revenue Mobilization Strategy 2013-2018",""],[1,"101","3","Fiscal System Reform and Revenue Enhancement","Continue formulating and improving the fiscal system to make it a catalyst for accelerating economic growth.",""],[1,"101","5","Tax Law Reform and Tax Administration Expansion","Continue formulating and improving laws (and legal letters) on taxes, continue extending taxation on property in the entire country, reducing the annual corporate tax and expand the auto-declare regime, formulating laws on personal incomes, closely following international tax conventions, revising special levies, and examining tax regulations on petroleum and other mineral products.",""],[1,"101","6","Tax Administration Strengthening and Customs Capacity Building","Strengthen the tax administration machinery through building capacities of customs officers and others engaged in tax collection, simplifying processes for the taxpayers in depositing their due, strengthening tax auditing, tightening the tax collection machinery to increase the effectiveness of tax collection, and enhancing governance on customs and other tax officials.",""],[1,"101","8","Tax Administration Integrity and Anti-Smuggling Enforcement","Continue promoting good governance and inculcate honesty among the tax officers and tighten the implementation process to stopping smuggling.",""],[1,"101","9","Non-Tax Revenue Collection and State Property Management Law Implementation","Complete formulating and then putting into effect, the Law on Non-Tax Revenue Collection and Law on State Property Management to increase the effectiveness in revenue collection and state property management, as is stated in the PFMR.",""],[1,"101","11","Non-tax Revenue and Contract Enforcement Strengthening","Continue formulating and increasing the effectiveness of enforcement of laws (and legal letters) related to non-tax revenue mobilization and enforcement of contracts (or agreement on state property management), especially Economic Land Concession Contracts, public property-leasing, petroleum and mine concessions, and other concessions.",""],[1,"101","13","Revenue Collection Auditing Strengthening","Strengthen auditing on all types of revenue collection, including tax and non-tax revenues.",""],[1,"101","14","Revenue Source Research Studies","Undertake research studies on finding new revenue sources at both, the national and sub-national levels, with the ultimate aim of increasing national revenues.",""],[1,"127","8","Medium-Term Revenue Mobilization Strategy","Further enhancing the budget credibility by strengthening revenue collection and management, particularly adoption and implementation of a medium-term revenue mobilization strategy along with improvement in budget execution and cash management.",""]],"135":[[1,"91","2","Non-Tax Revenue and State Property Management Laws","the government is formulating a Law on Non-Tax Revenue Management and a Law on State Property Management.",""],[1,"101","12","State Property Inventory Registration Improvement","Improve the registration of state properties inventory through exhibiting the quantities and prices of the state property in the inventory list of the ministry-agency and sub- national administration.",""]],"136":[[1,"94","2","COBRA Document Tracking System","The COBRA System is operational for tracking documents.",""]],"137":[[1,"94","11","Insurance Law Reform","Draft Law on Insurance has been formulated to strengthen this sector.",""],[1,"104","2","Insurance Sector Arbitration Mechanisms","Create arbitration mechanisms for the insurance sector to solve conflicts (if any) for ensuring justice to the aggrieved and instilling people's confidence in insurance.",""],[1,"104","6","Pension System Legal and Regulatory Framework","Establish a legal framework to monitor and regulate the pension system.",""]],"138":[[1,"94","21","Information Technology System Promotion for Regulators, Operators, and Authorities","Use of information technology system for regulators, operators, and authorities is being promoted.",""],[1,"104","7","Financial Sector Information Technology System Development","Develop a strong information technology system to serve the financial sector, including pension funds.",""],[1,"104","18","Regulatory IT System Strengthening","Continue to strengthen the IT system for the regulators to promote release of information and conduct market surveys.",""]],"139":[[1,"99","9","Human Capital Development and Basic Services Expansion","Human capital formation at different levels, More schools beyond the primary levels, Skilling institutions, Labor market flexibility to ensure returns to skills - ensuring demand for skills and more job creation/labor market information, Gender parity at all levels, Widely spread health centers, Better nutrition and (almost) universal water and sanitation (WATSAN), Social safety net in place.",""],[1,"99","14","Human Development Budget Increase and Human Capital Policy","Raise budgets for Human Development sectors (Education>3% of GDP, Health>2% of GDP), have a clear policy for human capital formation in terms of creating competitive skills in science and technology.",""]],"140":[[1,"98","17","Paddy Production Promotion and Rice Export Policy","the two central policies that the government intends following are, a Promotion of Paddy Production and Rice Export Policy",""],[1,"102","1","Rice Production and Milled Rice Export Promotion","promoting Rice Production and Milled Rice Export;",""],[1,"105","13","Policy on the Promotion of Paddy Production and Rice Export","RGC will begin implementation of the \"Policy on the Promotion of Paddy Production and Rice Export\" fully during this plan cycle.",""],[1,"106","2","Paddy Commercialization and Agricultural Trade Support Measures","Further promoting commercialization of the paddy crop through, implementation of laws and policies and strengthening the institutional arrangements to promote trade and export of agricultural products; effective implementation of law on agricultural communities; enhanced processing capacity, further improvement in trade facilitation', including 'one-stop services'; strengthened logistics systems; enhanced quality of agricultural products in accordance with international standards; improved capacity to provide affordable credit; and enhanced partnership between farmers, traders, and paddy processing industries.",""]],"141":[[1,"99","12","Agriculture and Livestock-Fisheries Sector Strengthening","Strengthen Chamcar & livestock/fish sectors",""],[1,"105","12","Agricultural Productivity Improvement","A strategic objective of the RGC is to improve agricultural productivity in which exporting milled rice assumes centrality.",""]],"142":[[1,"99","12","Commercial Law and Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthen commercial laws and implementation",""],[1,"104","12","Bankruptcy and Financial Trust Legal Standards Reform","Formulate and put in place, legal standards related to bankruptcy and financial trust in the security market.",""]],"143":[[1,"99","12","Pro-Growth Policy and Growth Center Development","Pro-growth policies/ growth centers, Urbanization policies.",""]],"144":[[1,"99","26","Civil Service Census for Zero-Based Budgeting","Carryout another civil service census from the point of view of 0-based budgeting.",""]],"145":[[1,"100","11","Extension of Social Agricultural Land Concessions","6. Extend social (agricultural) land concessions.",""],[1,"101","4","Agricultural Land Tax Exemption Policy","Aims at not imposing taxes on agricultural land, so that this incentive helps farmers to invest more on land and other agricultural inputs for increasing crop and non-crop production and productivity, and also raise their standards of living.",""]],"146":[[1,"100","21","Public Financial Management Transparency and Accountability Measures","There would be greater focus on ensuring effectiveness, transparency, and accountability, in managing revenue collection and allocating expenditure.",""],[1,"100","23","Public Financial Management Reform Program, Phase II","It has also speeded up the implementation of Phase II,",""],[1,"101","1","Financial Accountability Reform Program Phases III and IV","'Increasing Financial Accountability' and now aims to carryout Phase III, 'Increasing the Linkage of Budget with Policies' and Phase IV 'Increasing Deliverable Accountability', of this reform program.",""],[1,"102","3","Public Expenditure Management Transparency and Accountability Reform","Promote effectiveness, transparency and accountability in expenditure allocation, from the stages of preparation to implementation, monitoring and auditing of the outcomes, in budget the implementation.",""],[1,"102","8","Strengthen Internal and External Audit on Expenditure","Strengthen internal and external audit on expenditure.",""],[1,"127","9","Financial Accountability and Budget Management Reform","Enhancing financial accountability by developing and introducing a new budget nomenclature, a new chart of accounts and budget entities as well as the Financial Management Information System (FMIS).",""]],"147":[[1,"100","21","Public Expenditure Prioritization for Social and Physical Infrastructure Sectors","On expenditures, RGC will continue attaching high importance to the socio-economic sectors, physical infrastructure, and improvement of the capacity and livelihoods of civil servants and armed forces; i.e., all that is prioritized in RS III.",""]],"148":[[1,"101","10","Casino Management Law Enactment","Attempt enacting the Law on Casino Management.",""]],"149":[[1,"102","4","Macro-Economic Framework and Program Budget Planning Reform","Strengthen the formulation of a macro-economic framework and public finance and budget strategic plan to increase the quality of annual budget preparation and lead to implement the program budget.",""],[1,"102","5","Program Budget Implementation for Medium-Term Revenue Mobilization Strategy","Strengthen and expend for program budget implementation of Medium-Term Revenue Mobilization Strategy 2013-2018.",""],[1,"102","6","Budget Implementation Procedure Simplification","Improve the procedure of budget implementation by reducing unnecessary bureaucratic procedures.",""],[1,"128","1","Program Budgeting Expansion and Budget Reform Strategy","Enhancing links between the budget and policies and accountability for performance by strengthening and expanding program budgeting coverage and improving the implementation of the budget strategic plan with the introduction of a concept paper on strategic directions of budget reform.",""]],"150":[[1,"102","7","Public Procurement Law Enforcement","Ensure strict enforcement of the Law on Public Procurement and other related legal letters.",""]],"151":[[1,"102","13","National Savings Mobilization and Formalization Initiative","During the plan cycle 2014-2018, it is (ambitiously) aimed to raise the savings rate to about 30% by the end of 2018.",""],[1,"103","2","Financial Architecture Development","The government aims to build a strong financial architecture based on market principles, serving to mobilize and allocating resources to contribute to maintaining macro- economic stability and enabling sustainable economic growth.",""],[1,"103","3","Financial Development Strategy Implementation","RGC has encouraged in the past and will continue encouraging, implementation of the Financial Development Strategy 2011-2020 to support economic diversification, innovation and competition of Cambodia economy.",""],[1,"104","17","Financial Development Center","Establish a Financial Development Center to attract financial flows.",""],[1,"127","5","Proactive Macroeconomic Policy for Growth","Pursuing proactive macroeconomic policy to support growth by enhancing private sector development; promoting labor market development; encouraging investment in key sectors aimed at achieving economic diversification and high and equitable growth; and further implementing needed structural reforms, including implementing \"Financial Sector Development Strategy 2011-2020\", to improve economic efficiency and competitiveness for attracting investments and promoting exports.",""],[1,"128","7","Market-Based Financial System Development","Continue to develop a strong, market-based financial system, which mobilizes and allocates resources to contribute to economic growth.",""]],"152":[[1,"103","10","Chiang Mai Initiative Multilateralization Promotion","Actively promote the Chiang Mai Initiative 'Multi-Lateralization Mechanism' for preventing any financial/debt crisis.",""],[1,"128","6","Monetary Inflow Strengthening and Crisis Management Mechanism","Strengthen and expand monetary inflow and invoke crisis management mechanism, to contain turmoil and disaster.",""]],"153":[[1,"105","2","Private Sector Incentive Scheme for Industrialization","Provide suitable incentives to the private sector for meeting the long-term development goals of industrialization.",""],[1,"105","3","Private Sector Infrastructure Concession Review","Continue to encourage and urge the private sector's participation in building infrastructure, for which the Law on Concession and other related legal letters will be reviewed.",""],[1,"105","6","Business Support Infrastructure Investment","Continue investing in necessary infrastructure that supports business creation and investment enhancement.",""],[1,"105","7","One-Stop Service Mechanism for Business and Investment Facilitation","Create a congenial business environment for receiving domestic and foreign investments including facilitating registration, and providing licenses and other permission letters.",""],[1,"105","8","Government-Private Sector Forum Partnership Mechanism","Continue partnerships through the Government-Private Sector Forum to resolve all the pending problems that the private sector faces.",""],[1,"106","4","Investment Attraction and SME Strengthening Institutional Arrangements","first, make institutional arrangements through strategic support to attract investments and to strengthen small and medium enterprises;",""],[1,"106","4","Modern Institutions for Productivity Enhancement","second, set up modern institutions to help raise productivity;",""],[1,"106","4","Product and Process Specialization Incentive and Regulatory Framework","third, promote (product and process) specialization through incentives and regulations, based on long-term policies.",""]],"154":[[1,"107","1","Domestic Linkages to Global Value Chains Initiative","In the second phase, the focus will be on establishing domestic linkages to global value chains and boosting exports through creating a competitive environment.",""]],"155":[[1,"120","4","Public Service Standards Implementation and Monitoring Mechanism","Strengthening the quality and delivery of public services through the implementation of the Policy on Public Service and the Guide on Public Services Standards to improve their responsiveness, reliability, effectiveness and efficiency.",""],[1,"120","10","Public Service Delivery Policy Dissemination","Continue to disseminate the Policy on Public Service Delivery.",""],[1,"120","11","Public Services Compendium Implementation, Dissemination, and Monitoring","Update, disseminate and monitor the implementation of the Compendium on Public Services.",""],[1,"120","12","Public Services Quality Standards Implementation","Disseminate and facilitate the implementation of the Guide on Public Services Quality Standards by ministry.",""],[1,"121","1","Service Commitments Codes and Charters","Facilitate the development and implementation of service commitments codes/charters.",""],[1,"121","2","Targeted Training for Ministerial Service Providers","Develop and implement targeted training for ministerial service providers.",""],[1,"121","3","Service Delivery Streamlining Reform","Support the streamlining of service delivery procedures and processes.",""],[1,"121","6","Quality Accreditation and Best Practices Reward Mechanism","Conduct research and establish mechanisms for quality accreditation and rewarding best practices.",""],[1,"121","7","Deployment of Special Operating Agencies","Promote the further deployment of Special Operating Agencies by ministries.",""]],"156":[[1,"121","16","Demand-Driven Training Mechanisms","Develop and implement mechanisms to ensure that training is demand driven.",""],[1,"121","17","Curriculum Development for Priority Technical and Personal Skills","Develop and implement curriculum to address priority technical, personal and inter- personal skills.",""],[1,"121","18","Mandatory Short-Term Training for New Recruits and Managers","Promote the Provision of mandatory short-term training for new recruits and for managers.",""],[1,"121","19","Institutional Capacity for Ongoing Training Development","Develop institutional capacity for ongoing training including the establishment of a national institute, of a distance learning capability and of partnerships with Cambodian and foreign training providers.",""]],"157":[[1,"102","1","Civil Servant and Armed Forces Salary Increase","to continue implementing an increase in salary for civil servants and armed forces based on the economic growth and the extent to which the national budget can support it.",""],[1,"120","6","Pay and Allowances Reform","Further reforming pay and allowances.",""],[1,"121","21","Salary Payment Through Banking System","Further implement the payment of salary through the banking system.",""],[1,"121","22","Gradual Public Salary Increase Policy","Gradually increase salary based on budget affordability while maintaining macro- economic stability.",""],[1,"121","23","Salary Composition and Allowance Review","Review and improve salary composition and other allowances.",""],[1,"121","26","Salary System Review and Adjustment","Review and make adjustment of salary system to ensure the consistency and equity within and among institutions and between civil servants and security and armed forces;",""],[1,"121","27","Salary System Review and Development","Review and develop salary system to support the performance.",""],[1,"121","28","Contractual and Floating Staff Management and Remuneration Reform","Strengthen the management and remuneration of contractual and floating staffs.",""]],"158":[[1,"123","1","Support for Veterans, Disabled Soldiers, and Military Families","Continuing support to veterans, disabled soldiers, families of deceased soldiers and families of military personnel through giving out social land concessions and development projects to the military communities and families of armed forces stationed in border areas.",""]],"159":[[1,"123","3","International Relations and Cooperation for Armed Forces Development","Strengthening and expanding international relations and cooperation to develop armed forces in all dimensions including continued participation in the UN peacekeeping missions.",""],[1,"124","6","International Cooperation for Democratic Governance and Security Support","MOI continues to enhance international cooperation with the countries within the region and the countries outside the region and with international organizations, especially to enhance the bilateral and multilateral cooperation aiming at the mobilization of the support from international communities for promoting of democracy process, decentralization and de-concentration policy, enhancement of political stability, capacity development for law enforcement officers and preventing cross-border crimes.","MOI"]],"160":[[1,"123","6","Strategic Agricultural and Processing Investment Partnerships","Developing strategic partners in agriculture and processing investment using resources of the military community to maximize resource utilization and create jobs and businesses for the community.",""]],"161":[[1,"123","13","Rule of Law and Democratic Governance Strengthening","Continued strengthening of the rule of law, democracy, culture of peace, morality in the society and respect for human rights and dignity, and no tolerance to forces of political instability.",""],[1,"123","14","Border Dispute Settlement and Border Development Strategy Implementation","Continued settlement of both land and maritime boundary disputes with based on aforementioned principles, along with continued preparation and strengthened implementation of border development strategies.",""],[1,"123","15","Crime Prevention and Suppression Measures","Prevention and suppression of all criminal activities, including terrorism and its financing, money laundering, illegal drug and human trafficking, and transnational crimes, and continued implementation of the \"Safe Village/Commune\" policy.",""],[1,"123","16","Traffic Safety and Public Order Strengthening","Continued strengthening of traffic safety and public order and eliminating illegal checkpoints.",""],[1,"123","17","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Priority Policy Implementation","To implement RGC's priority policies, MOI will focus on strengthening the institutional capacities at the national and sub-national levels, to deal with emerging","MOI"],[1,"124","5","National Police Force Strengthening Programme","MOI continues to strengthen the National Police Force to turn it a professionally skilled force equipped with modern technology and courteous officials capable to fulfilling their duties.","MOI"],[1,"124","5","Community Policing Strengthening Initiative","MOI will also strengthen the police force at administrative posts under the slogan \"police and community\".","MOI"]],"162":[[1,"124","5","Police Academy Recruitment and Training Programme","It would admit students to the Police Academy of Cambodia train them in the police profession, and then recruit them to the national police force in accordance with the Ministry's annual needs.","MOI"]],"163":[[1,"125","1","Private Sector Engagement in Drug Control","Encourage the involvement of the private sectors in fighting against drugs.",""],[1,"125","3","Strengthening Law Enforcement Against Illicit Drugs","Strengthening the effectiveness of law enforcement agencies: intensify the effectiveness implementation of legislation affairs.",""],[1,"125","3","Expand Border Liaison Offices","Strengthening and expanding the Border Liaison Offices (BLO's).",""],[1,"125","3","Strengthen NACD Laboratory Capacity","Strengthening the capacity of the NACD laboratory officials.",""],[1,"125","3","Computer-Based Training for Law Enforcement Officers","Continue using the mechanism of Computer-Based Training (CBT) to strengthen law enforcement officers.",""],[1,"125","3","Strengthen Law Enforcement Support for Harm Reduction","Strengthening the law enforcement affairs to support Harm Reduction programme.",""],[1,"125","4","Precursor Chemicals Control Plan","Formulation on Drafting legislations and establish the planning on the control of precursor chemicals for preventing of the diversion of legal trade of precursors chemicals into drugs producing and provided law enforcement agencies with a particular skill.",""],[1,"125","4","Natural Oils Production and Trafficking Control Measures","Set up controlling plan and the measure of the control of production trafficking of natural oils which consist of Saffrole-rich oil extracted from Saffron trees and others.",""],[1,"125","5","Green Border Villages and Communes Drug-Free Mechanism","Intensify the mechanism of green villages and communes drug-free along the borders.",""],[1,"125","5","Border Liaison Office Strengthening","Strengthening the mechanism of Border Liaison Office (BLOs).",""],[1,"125","6","International Drug Control Cooperation and Convention Implementation","Strengthening and expansion of the implementation of all binding obligation stipulated in the agreements and international drugs control conventions and Promote international cooperation with other countries in order to seek the support and assistances in all drugs control activities.",""]],"164":[[1,"126","1","Family and Religious Values Promotion Initiative","Ministry of Cults and Religions (MCR) will continue to actively promote the role of family and adherence to the traditional religious values of the Kingdom.","Ministry of Cults and Religions (MCR)"],[1,"126","1","Buddhism and Society Programme","MCR has established a programme called \"Buddhism and Society\" by inviting religious scholar of talent, intelligence and aptitude to come and give sermon every Buddhist-saint day (4 times a month) with the purpose of mainstreaming Buddhism for educational purpose amongst pupils, students and ordinary people in order to raise the awareness of morality value for living in the society avoiding the use of drug, domestic violence, pornography, sexual trafficking, and teenager violence.","Ministry of Cults and Religions (MCR)"],[1,"126","1","Interfaith Morality Education Promotion","MCR also encouraged other religions to provide morality education through their own religious services vigorously contributing their shares to the development of the nation.","Ministry of Cults and Religions (MCR)"],[1,"126","3","Youth and Children Cultural Education Programme","Increase education particularly the education amongst youth and children so that they understand very clearly the superb value of Cambodian culture, tradition, and customs which are the identity symbols of Cambodian nation and so they participate to preserve, promote, develop this national culture and to reduce the negative impact from the foreign cultures.",""],[1,"126","4","Buddhist Education and Religious Text Publication Support","the renewal of strengthening and expanding all levels of Buddhist schools, publication of religious texts, annotated texts, rules, and Dhamma discipline practice.",""],[1,"126","5","Interfaith Harmony and Anti-Discrimination Support","Supports other religions' activities in the society, strengthens the harmonization amongst all religious holders of all religion, fight against any discrimination or split amongst the people arising from their different religious views",""],[1,"126","6","Provincial Buddhist University Establishment Programme","Establish Buddhist universities in each province as it can afford in accordance with actual situation in order to strengthen the quality of Buddhist education from the Dhamma discipline level to primary level and to higher education level as well as post higher education level through providing training to Buddhist pupils and Buddhist students in Buddhist educational institutions which are available now and will be available in the future.",""],[1,"126","7","Library Strengthening and Expansion Initiative","Strengthens and enlarges libraries in departments, pagodas, and in Buddhist schools by providing books, religious texts, annotated religious texts, rules and other relevant documents in order to promote reading and research highly effectively.",""],[1,"126","8","Khmer Ah Char Association Management and Training Courses","Prepare the courses for training the roles, tasks and code of conduct for Khmer Ah Char, by preparing a management in form of Ah Char Khmer association in the nation- wide level from the central cities to local areas such as province level or district level and held a congress to round up the work of Ah Char Khmer association and set up the next target and also going on opening the courses for training the roles, tasks and practicing rules for nuns and renewing to maintain the customs, religions and other religious celebrations.",""]],"165":[[1,"111","8","Public Finance Management Reform Programme","As part of the RGC's Public Finance Management Reform Programme (PFMRP), the Ministry of Economy and Finance (MEF) has established 2 processes that provide important inputs in the preparation of Annual National Budget.","Ministry of Economy and Finance (MEF)"],[1,"112","1","Public Finance Management Reform Programme","As part of the implementation of the Public Finance Management Reform Programme, RGC is now in the process of strengthening linkages between the processes that: (i) identify high priority public investment requirements, which include the five-year National Strategic Development Plans (NSDP) and the Three-year Rolling Public Investment Programme PIP; (ii) the mobilisation of external resources from traditional and non-traditional development partners; and (iii) the preparation of the Budget Strategic Framework.",""],[1,"112","2","Public Investment Programme Formulation Strengthening","RGC attaches high priority to further strengthen the PIP formulation process.",""],[1,"112","2","PIP-Based Budget Funding Screening","the MEF will ensure that only those programmes and projects that are part of the PIP are included in a consideration for funding during the formulation of the Budget Strategic Framework.","MEF"],[1,"112","2","PIP Project Resource Mobilisation and Reporting","the CRDB/CDC will ensure that in its resource mobilisation activities it will actively promote the funding of projects included in PIP, and prepare regular reports on PIP projects that are supported by external development partners (EDPs) as well as projects supported by EDPs that are not part of the PIP.","CRDB/CDC"],[1,"112","3","Indicative Recurrent Expenditure Allocation Projection","the MOP has prepared a preliminary/indicative projection of recurrent expenditure allocation for RGC institutions for the NSDP 2014-2018 period","MOP"],[1,"115","1","Public Finance Reform Coordination","Public Finance Reform.",""],[1,"127","2","Public Financial Management Reform Program - Stage 2","The continued implementation of Public Financial Management Reform Program-Stage 2 has helped further strengthen budget credibility and improve financial accountability.",""],[1,"127","7","Public Financial Management Reform Program","Continuing to implement the Public Financial Management Reform Program aimed at improving the efficiency and effectiveness of Cambodia's public financial management system according to international standards, through:",""]],"166":[[1,"130","6","Government-Private Sector Forum Mechanism","Continue implementing the Government-Private Sector Forum Mechanism to resolve the outstanding problems in the private sector.",""],[1,"130","7","Entrepreneurship Promotion and SME Support Programme","Promote entrepreneurship (including SMEs), especially among Cambodian nationals: how to run business, investment options, incentives, consultancy, capital, and techniques.",""],[1,"132","1","Government-Private Sector Forum Strengthening","Continuing to promote and enhance the effectiveness of the Government-Private Sector Forum in order to strengthen the role of this mechanism in providing alternative policy options and recommendations that contribute to enhanced participation of private sector in development, as well as to strengthen its role in addressing business related bottlenecks and concerns it faces in Cambodia.",""]],"167":[[1,"129","1","Medium-Term Revenue Mobilization Strategy","Review the Revenue Collection Policy and prepare and carry out Medium-Term Revenue Mobilization Strategy 2013-2018.",""],[1,"129","2","Fiscal System Reform and Improvement","Continue formulating and improving the fiscal system to catalyze economic growth, increase effectiveness, reduce smuggling, and ensure social equity.",""],[1,"129","3","Agricultural Land Tax Exemption","Continue not to tax agricultural land, so as to help farmers improve their daily livelihoods.",""],[1,"129","4","Tax System Reform and Compliance Expansion","Continue to improve laws and legal letters on taxes, continue to spread on taxing property, reduce the annual corporate tax rate and expand the auto-declare regime, improve taxing individuals, follow up on international tax conventions, and revise special levies.",""],[1,"129","5","Tax Administration Strengthening Programme","Strengthen and improve tax administration by building the capacity of customs officers, increase the service delivery to tax payers, strengthen tax auditing, tighten tax collection measures, and improve the surveillance on customs officers.",""],[1,"129","7","Non-Tax Revenue Collection and State Property Management Law Implementation","Complete formulating and putting into effect, the Law on Non-Tax Revenue Collection and Law on State Property Management, to increase revenues and state property management, as per the PFMR.",""],[1,"129","8","Casino Management Law Enactment","Encourage an enactment of the Law on Casino Management.",""],[1,"129","9","Strengthening Enforcement of Non-Tax Revenue and State Property Contracts","Continue increasing the effectiveness of enforcement of laws and legal letters related to non-tax revenue mobilization and enforcement of contracts or agreement on state property management, especially Economic Land Concession Contracts, public property leasing, petroleum and mine concession provision and other concessions.",""],[1,"129","10","Research on New Revenue Sources","Encourage research studies on new revenue sources at both national and sub-national levels, to increase national revenues.",""],[1,"129","11","State Property Registration Strengthening","Strengthen the registration of state property by explicating the quantity and prices of the state property.",""],[1,"129","12","Revenue Collection Auditing Strengthening","Strengthen auditing on all types of revenue collection.",""],[1,"129","17","Macro-Economic Framework and Public Finance Planning Strengthening","Strengthen formulation of macro-economic framework, public finance and budget strategic plan.",""],[1,"129","18","Medium-Term Revenue Mobilization Strategy Program Budget Implementation","Strengthen and expend for program budget implementation of Medium-Term Revenue Mobilization Strategy 2013-2010.",""],[1,"130","1","Concessional Loan and Public Debt Management","Continue to implement the four main principles related to concessional loan, public debt management, for sustaining public debt, promoting long-term economic growth and effective and efficient use of loan.",""],[1,"130","2","Debt Risk Management Policy Framework","Formulate and implement the policy framework on debt-risk management and build capacities in the concerned ministries and agencies (having public debt) to maintain its sustainability.",""]],"168":[[1,"129","13","Priority Public Expenditure and Infrastructure Maintenance Programme","Continue prioritizing expenditures on education, health, social security, agriculture, land and rural development, and expanding the improvement and maintenance of physical infrastructure such as roads, railways, ports, irrigation, power, clean water supply, schools, and hospitals.",""],[1,"129","14","Civil Service and Armed Forces Salary Adjustment Policy","Continue to implement the policy on increasing the salary of civil servants and armed forces based on economic growth and growth in national budget.",""],[1,"129","16","Public Expenditure Management Transparency and Accountability Reform","Continue to promote effectiveness, transparency and accountability in expenditure allocation and management, beginning from the stages of preparation, to implementation, monitoring and auditing of outcomes.",""],[1,"129","19","Public Procurement Law Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthen strict enforcement of Law on Public Procurement and other related legal letters.",""],[1,"129","20","Strengthen Internal and External Audit on Expenditure","Strengthen internal and external audit on expenditure.",""],[1,"129","21","Financing Diversification for Public Infrastructure Investment","Expand the financing diversification to its maximum, to respond to the increase in the demand for financing public investments in physical infrastructure.",""]],"169":[[1,"129","15","Policy Promotion for Rice Production, Rice Export, Agro-Industry, Tourism, and Sovereignty Protection","Expend for promoting the policies on Promoting Rice Production and Milled Rice Export; Agro-Industry Development; Tourism Development Plan (2011-2020); and on protection of the sovereignity of the country.",""]],"170":[[1,"132","9","Inter-Ministerial Coordination Strengthening","the RGC will continue to further strengthen inter-ministerial coordination",""],[1,"132","9","Legal and Regulatory Alignment for International and Regional Membership Obligations","adopt laws and regulations required to meet the obligations of membership in international and regional organizations (especially the ASEAN)",""],[1,"132","9","Institutional Capacity Building for Law Enforcement","strengthen the capacity of the concerned governmental institutions to effectively enforce the adopted laws and regulations",""],[1,"133","4","ASEAN Agreements Implementation and Community Accession","Effectively implementing all ASEAN-related agreements and join the ASEAN Community by 2015 as an equal partner.",""],[1,"133","5","ASEAN Economic Community Adjustment Frameworks","Establishing necessary frameworks to manage changes resulting from its participation in ASEAN Economic Community expected to be in place by 2015, and ensuring that Cambodia's best interests are served especially in managing the labor market and movement of workers.",""]],"171":[[1,"128","14","Land Reform Implementation","Continue to implement Land Reform, particularly the continued implementation of \"Existing Policy with New Activity\" in the land sector to promote effective land use and ensure sustainable socio-economic development.",""],[1,"134","7","Agricultural Land Conservation and Improvement Program","7. Promote programs for agriculture land conservation and agriculture land improvement through:",""],[1,"134","8","Agricultural Land Protection Law and Regulations","Establishment of agricultural land law and other regulations under law to protect agricultural land from transfer to other uses.",""],[1,"134","10","Agriculture Sector Strategy Update and Implementation Support","Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries and Forestry (MAFF) will continue updating the Agriculture Sector Strategy and seek support to implement the strategy.","Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries and Forestry (MAFF)"],[1,"134","15","Soil Fertility Management for Land Restoration","Enhancing soil fertility management to combat land degradation and desertification.",""],[1,"135","25","Agricultural Land Policy Formulation","Agricultural land policy formulation.",""],[1,"135","26","Agricultural Land Law Preparation and Consultation","Agricultural land law preparation and consultation (on-going).",""],[1,"135","27","National Action Plan to Combat Agricultural Land Degradation","National action plan to combating agricultural land degradation preparation and consultation (on-going).",""],[1,"135","28","Agricultural Conservation Policy and Strategic Plan Formulation","Policy and strategic plan for agriculture conservation formulation.",""],[1,"135","30","Soil and Land Use Management for Climate and Disaster Risk Reduction","Researching and implementing soil/land use and management in mitigation and adaption to climate change and disaster risk reduction.",""],[1,"135","33","Agricultural Land Use Planning and Zoning","Developing agricultural land use plan and zoning.",""],[1,"136","10","Land Management and Utilization Law Reform","Furthering the drafted law on crop protection and phyto-sanitary law and the on land management and utilization.",""]],"172":[[1,"138","3","Animal Manure Biogas Promotion","Promote the use of animal manures for bio-gas production.",""],[1,"138","5","Biogas Credit Support Scheme","Improve credit services for establishing bio-gas.",""]],"173":[[1,"136","12","Gender Mainstreaming Training in Agriculture Sector","Organizing training on gender mainstreaming in the agriculture sector.",""],[1,"137","16","Legal and Regulatory Reform","Promote laws and regulations.",""],[1,"138","7","Collaboration for Technical Assistance and Funding","Continue collaborating with national and international organizations, DPs, and the private sector, for both technical assistance and funds.",""],[1,"138","11","Enforcement of Economic Land Concession Laws","Enforce laws for economic land concession companies.",""],[1,"138","13","Legal and Regulatory Strengthening","Strengthen law and regulations.",""],[1,"138","14","Institutional and Staff Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen institutional and staff capacity.",""]],"174":[[1,"140","7","Land and Natural Resource Governance Enforcement","Further ensuring transparent and efficient management, conservation and use of land and natural resources to ensure the sustainability of the environment and socio- economic development, prevention of illegal forest encroachments and enforcement of strict measures against those who illegally grab state land or keep land idle for speculative purposes, intensification of drive for confiscation of economic land concessions in case of violation of contract agreement or regulations, and cessation of granting new economic land concessions.",""],[1,"140","8","Social Land Concessions and Land Grants","Further distributing and using state land, especially the confiscated economic land concessions and cleared minefields, in a transparent and equitable manner, for development purposes that respond to the needs of the poor, disabled veterans, families of deceased soldiers and veterans who have genuine need to use the land, through the implementation of social land concessions and land grants.",""],[1,"140","9","Household Farm Land Tax Exemption and Productivity Support","Further exempting land tax on household farms and supporting the farmers in enhancing the productivity of land use through the construction of transport networks, irrigation systems and other essential infrastructure.",""],[1,"142","5","National Land Distribution Policy Development","Preparing the national policy on the distribution of land in Cambodia.",""],[1,"142","6","Social Land Concession Land Identification and Stock Preparation","Find and identify available land for social land concessions such as unused land, land contractually cancelled from economic land concessions (ELCs) due to non- operation/non-production, and demining land by preparing land stocks for the purpose of land distribution program under the long, medium and short terms goal.",""],[1,"142","7","Farm Partnership Policy Development","Speed up the development of a policy on partnership between small, medium and large-scale farms between social land concessions and economic land concessions.",""],[1,"142","8","Small Loan Access for Social Land Concessionaires","Provide opportunities for acquiring small (credit) loans service to social land concessionaires and recipients receiving land gifts from various programs of the RGC, including the implementation of RGC's Directive 01 (2012)",""],[1,"142","9","Strengthening of the Social Land Concessions Mechanism","Strengthen the social land concessions mechanism, especially the committee in charge of using and distributing land at the municipal and provincial levels must encourage the implementation of procedures related to land use and state land distribution in provinces where lands are available for social land concessions program, and the provinces where lands are not available but where land recipients have been carefully selected.",""],[1,"142","9","Acceleration of Social Land Concessions Distribution Program","At the same time, the countrywide acceleration of implementing the social land concessions distribution program will be continued based on stock of state land (state land inventory) in the implementation of new action under the existing policies for the land sector to ban on irregularities of illegal occupation/ encroachment on state land.",""],[1,"145","5","Indigenous Land Titling and NTFP Access Support","Continue formalizing titles to the indigenous peoples and permit them access to NTFP.",""]],"175":[[1,"130","9","Comprehensive Environmental Management Approach","Ministry of Environment (MOE) will continue to take a comprehensive development approach toward environmental management in Cambodia, through:","Ministry of Environment (MOE)"],[1,"144","1","Natural Resources Management and Conservation Programme","The Royal Government of the Fifth Legislature will reinforce and broaden the management of natural resources to strike a \"balance between development and conservation\"",""],[1,"144","2","Natural Resource Ownership Clarification and Conservation Incentive Scheme","the Royal Government will implement a comprehensive and cross cutting approach, aimed at improving the effectiveness and equity in the exploitation of natural resources, by (1) clearly determining the ownership of natural resources; (2) developing an appropriate incentive scheme for the conservation of natural resources and empowering the sub-national government, communities and individuals to participate in their conservation by focusing on training, information sharing as well as strengthening social capital, and institutional accountability and transparency; and (3) stepping up cooperation with concerned stakeholders under the framework of green growth and climate change.",""],[1,"144","3","Sustainable Forest and Wildlife Resource Management Programme","Further managing forest and wildlife resources in a sustainable and equitable manner, in accordance with the \"National Forest Program 2010-2029\", in particular through better law enforcement and governance, demarcation, classification and registration of forest, effective management and exploitation of state and private forests, implementation of measures for improving the livelihoods of and promoting participation from forest-dependent communities, enhancement of management and effectiveness of conservation measures, reduction of deforestation and degradation of forests, intensified tree planting and forest rehabilitation, strengthening the conservation of wildlife and wildlife sanctuaries, development of institutional and human capacity, and promotion of research studies and their dissemination.",""],[1,"144","4","Sustainable Fisheries Resource Management and Conservation","Further strengthening the management and conservation of fishery resources in a sustainable manner in line with the \"Strategic Planning Framework for Fisheries Sector 2010-2019\" and the \"Declaration on the National Policy for Fisheries Sector\", especially through the suppression of all violations of laws, rules and regulations related to fisheries including tightened control of fishing gears and fishing period, elimination of overfishing, strengthening fishing communities' capacity for the management, use and conservation of fisheries resources, protection of biodiversity and aquatic-animal habitats, control of freshwater and seawater quality through pollution minimization, protection and replanting of flooded forests and mangroves, demarcation of flooded forest and fisheries conservation zones, development of institutional and human capacity, and preparing research studies and their dissemination.",""],[1,"144","5","Ecosystem Sustainability and Protected Areas Management Measures","Intensifying the implementation of necessary measures to ensure the sustainability of the ecosystem, aimed at ensuring the quality of soil, and surface and underground water for serving the agriculture sector and the livelihood of Cambodian people by promoting the preparation and effective implementation of policies and regulations, as well as related action plans and programs for the management of protected natural areas such as national parks, wildlife sanctuaries, protected landscape areas, multiple use areas, wetlands, biodiversity conservation areas, natural heritage conservation areas, and maritime parks, and in particular, strengthening the implementation of \"Law",""],[1,"145","2","Protected Areas and Biodiversity Management Strengthening","strengthening the management of protected natural areas including protection of biodiversity, rain forests, and wetland areas",""],[1,"145","3","National Forest Program Action Plan","the Forestry Administration (FA) has prepared an action plan to implement the National Forest Program effectively","Forestry Administration (FA)"],[1,"145","9","National Forest Program Implementation Capacity and Awareness Support","Raise awareness, capacity of institutions and quality of education, to enable sustainable implementation of the National Forest Program.",""],[1,"145","10","Environmental Protection and Forest Conservation Measures","Ensure environmental protection and conservation of forest resources.",""],[1,"145","11","Sustainable Forestry Management Models","Apply sustainable management models adapted to different forestry contexts.",""],[1,"145","13","National Forestry Program","The National Forestry Program consists of six major programs, which can be implemented and monitored over 20 years.",""],[1,"145","14","Forest Demarcation, Classification and Registration","Forest demarcation, classification and registration.",""],[1,"145","19","National Forest Program Action Plan","FA has prepared an action plan to implement the National Forest Program effectively, which includes eight priorities strategic sub-programs for annual implementation as below:",""],[1,"145","21","Forest Plantation Development","Development of Forest Plantation.",""],[1,"146","4","Wildlife Rescue, Rehabilitation, Breeding, and Reintroduction Programme","Wildlife rescue, rehabilitate, breeding and reintroduction/reinforcement into the natural forest.",""],[1,"146","8","National Resource Conservation and Eco-Tourism Linkage","RGC will further strengthen national resource conservation, especially promoting the linkage of conservation to eco-tourism.",""],[1,"147","24","Protected Areas Management Strengthening","Strengthen the management of protected areas to eliminate illegal exploitation of natural resources, and curb illegal land and forest clearings.",""],[1,"148","30","Protected Areas Boundary Demarcation and Data Management","Produce maps, install boundary poles, demarcate the boundary of controlled areas, and carry out data management in Protected Areas (PA).",""],[1,"148","31","National Flora Park and National Marine Park Establishment","Establish National Flora Park and National Marine Park.",""],[1,"149","1","Wetlands, Biosphere, and Coastal Zone Management and Conservation","Strengthen management and conservation of wetlands, biosphere, and coastal zones",""],[1,"149","18","Adjustment of Natural Protected Area Management Structures","Adjust management structures of natural protected areas to be consistent with the D&D Policies.",""],[1,"149","19","Management of Investment Projects in Natural Protected Areas","Increase effectiveness of the management of investment projects within the natural protected areas in conjunction with Green Growth policies.",""],[1,"149","20","Reforestation Strategy Development","Develop strategies to increase forest cover through reforestation.",""],[1,"149","21","Community Natural Protected Areas Management Strengthening","Strengthen management of green belts through strengthening the management of community natural protected areas.",""],[1,"150","1","Biodiversity Conservation Capacity Building","Build conservation capacity by creating biodiversity research centers, national parks, plant nursery fields, and modernization of advanced technologies.",""],[1,"150","3","National Biodiversity and Access and Benefit-Sharing Policy and Regulations","Develop a national policy and regulations on biodiversity and access and benefit- sharing (ABS) of genetic resources.",""],[1,"150","4","National Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plan Update","Update national biodiversity strategy and action plan (NBSAP).",""],[1,"150","5","UN Convention on Biodiversity Implementation","Implement UN Convention on Biodiversity.",""],[1,"150","6","Mainstream Biodiversity into Sector Development Plans","Mainstream biodiversity issues into the development plans of each sector.",""],[1,"150","7","Biodiversity Information System Development and Management","Develop and manage a biodiversity information system.",""]],"176":[[1,"152","16","Integrated Rural Development Programme","RGC will further foster implementation of integrated rural development programs, focusing on the factors that have positive impact on rural poor people, viz. institutional capacity strengthening and human resource development, implementation of the Integrated Rural Accessibility Planning (IRAP), rural road construction, rural water supply, primary health care and rural sanitation, community development, and development of rural economy.",""],[1,"153","2","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Rural Development Institutions","Institutional capacity strengthening by means of further consolidating and developing institutions through developing physical facilities and legal and regulatory framework, as well as concerned institutions, at all levels through strengthening Provincial/Capital- City Rural Development Departments and District/Khan Rural Development Offices.",""],[1,"153","3","Human Resource Development Training Programme","Human resource development through continued provision of training in different skills.",""],[1,"153","4","IRAP Preparation and Rural Public Investment Programme","Further implementing IRAP preparation and other public investment programs on rural services and infrastructure.",""],[1,"153","5","Rural Transport Infrastructure Provision","Provision of rural transport infrastructure to improve rural people's accessibility to services and facilitate transport of rural products to markets.",""],[1,"153","6","Support for Commune/Sangkat Small-Scale Rural Infrastructure Projects","Further provision of support to commune/sangkat councils for implementing small- scale rural infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"153","9","One Village One Product Scheme","Promote \"one village one product\" schemes to encourage development of high value- added products and attract the private sector.",""],[1,"153","10","Community-Based Participatory Village Development Support","Support the commune/sangkat councils to lead community-based participatory village development processes, and foster participation of citizens, particularly the armed- forces families living along western and northern borders, to transform the former battlefields into regions of peace and development.",""],[1,"153","12","Rural Microfinance Expansion and Low-Interest Rural Credit","Further promoting rural development through an increase of the scope of micro- finance and fostering effective use of low interest rate rural credit.",""],[1,"153","19","Rural Investment Attraction Initiative","Attract investors to invest in the rural areas having water, roads and electricity, to reduce immigration and create employment opportunities locally.",""],[1,"154","5","National Rural Development Center or Institute Establishment","Establish National Rural Development Center or Institute.",""]],"177":[[1,"153","14","PFMR Phases 2 and 3 Implementation","Continue implementing PFMR Phases 2 and 3 by promoting the establishment of budget units in MRD.",""],[1,"153","15","Financial Management Information System Implementation","Start to implement the Financial Management Information System (FMIS).",""],[1,"153","16","Budget Strategic Plan and Public Investment Planning Updates","Continue to update the budget strategic plan, 3-year rolling and annual public investment plans.",""],[1,"153","17","Project and Program Monitoring and Evaluation Systems","Continue to improve and put into operation, follow up, monitor and evaluate systems for the ministry's projects and programs.",""],[1,"153","18","District Rural Development Office Capacity Building and Facilities Upgrade","Continue to train officials of the District Rural Development Office, and repair/ construct Departments and Offices of Rural Development in provinces.",""],[1,"153","21","Public Administration Reform Program","Continue implementing the public administration reform program.",""],[1,"153","22","Decentralization and Deconcentration Programs","Continue preparing and implementing D&D programs.",""],[1,"153","23","Human Resources Improvement in the Ministry of Rural Development","Continue to improve human resources in the Ministry of Rural Development.","Ministry of Rural Development"],[1,"154","1","Civil Service Capacity Building and Training Programme","Continue to build capacity and train civil servants at all levels.",""],[1,"154","3","Ministerial Information Dissemination through Magazines and Newsletters","Continue disseminate information about ministerial affairs through magazines and newsletters.",""]],"178":[[1,"154","11","Village Development Committee Climate Change Adaptation Training","Train Village Development Committee (VDC) in adaptations to climate change and use of appropriate scientific knowledge acceptable locally.",""],[1,"154","12","Rural Disaster Risk Reduction and Preparedness Mainstreaming","Mainstream preparedness and reduction of disaster risk in the rural community;",""],[1,"155","9","Village Development Committee Capacity Building for Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation","Building the capacity of the VDCs in the option of adapting to and reduction of climate change and the use of appropriate and scientific knowledge acceptable at the locality",""]],"179":[[1,"154","13","Village Development Plan Training for VDCs","Continue to train VDC in creating village development plans.",""],[1,"154","14","Rural Development Centers Strengthening","Continue to strengthen activities of the Rural Development Centers in Takeo, Kampong Speu, Svay Rieng, Prey Veng, Kampong Cham, Battambang and Pursat provinces.",""]],"180":[[1,"157","16","Garage Management Sub-Decree Enforcement","Continue enforcing the sub-decree on management of repair garage and processing/ assembling garage.",""],[1,"157","17","Road Transport Business Sub-Decree Enforcement","Continue enforcing the sub-decree on road transport business.",""],[1,"157","18","Vehicle Registration Procedure Enforcement","Continue enforcing the Prakas on the Procedure of Vehicle Registration.",""],[1,"157","19","Road Transport Contract Law Enforcement","Continue enforcing the law on road transport contracts.",""],[1,"158","1","Road Traffic Law Reform","Formulate a new draft law on road traffic.",""],[1,"158","2","Vehicle Registration and Licensing Processing Time Reduction","Reduce the time for issuing vehicle registration, license plate, and driving license.",""],[1,"158","4","Vehicle Registration and Inspection System Modernization","Modernize the vehicle registration and inspection system using IT system.",""],[1,"159","30","Road Traffic Law Implementation","Implement Road Traffic Law.",""]],"181":[[1,"161","8","International Water Sector Cooperation Initiative","Stepping up involvement in international cooperation in the water sector to ensure the sustainability and effectiveness of water resources use as well as to address negative impacts arising from floods, droughts and climate change.",""],[1,"161","9","Water Ecosystem Preservation Measures","will also preserve the ecosystem of unpolluted water and clean environment",""],[1,"161","9","Mekong Basin Water Use Rationalization","RGC will continue taking measures to rationalize water use in all water bodies: rivers, lakes and the Tonle Sap",""],[1,"163","9","Water Resources Law Enforcement and Project Monitoring","Enforce the Law on Water Resources Management and other related regulations to monitor projects that might have adverse impact on water and the ecosystem.",""],[1,"163","11","Landfill and Coastal Area Remediation","Deal with landfills, excavations or permanently inundated areas / coastal areas adversely impacting water resources and the ecosystem.",""],[1,"163","13","Sub-decree on Irrigation System and Reservoir Demarcation","Prepare a Sub-decree on Demarcation of Geographical Positions of Irrigation System and Reservoir for taking measures to prevent potential water logging in the irrigation command areas.",""],[1,"164","10","Clean Water Access and Water Resource Studies","Prioritize access to clean water; ensure food security; achieve CMDGs; secure a clean ecosystem and unpolluted water in the Mekong River Basin; and continue studies on water resources in rivers, lakes and the Tonle Sap River.",""],[1,"164","14","Water Pollution Abatement for Ecosystem Protection","Abate polluting of waters to protect ecosystems, especially fish resources.",""]],"182":[[1,"171","2","Press Freedom and Freedom of Expression Promotion","Encouraging use of press freedom and freedom of expression such that it is in line with the principles of a pluralistic democracy, the rule of law, and protection of human rights and dignity.",""],[1,"171","6","Technical Facilities Modernization Plan","Developing plans for the modernization of technical facilities (national radio, national TV and news agency).",""],[1,"171","7","Sub-national Radio and Television Station Development","Continuing to encourage the building of radio and TV stations at the sub-national levels, with priority to the northwestern and northeastern provinces.",""],[1,"171","8","Sub-national Technical Training and Skills Improvement for Broadcasting","Promoting technical training and skill improvement at the sub-national levels, so that the radio and TV stations may be able to broadcast national events and produce programs to educate society on topics of interest.",""],[1,"171","9","Institutional Capacity Strengthening and Technical Facilities Modernization","Working towards strengthening the institutional capacities and modernization of technical facilities to ensure a comfortable and effective work performance.",""],[1,"171","10","Information and Broadcasting Sector Regulatory Framework Development","Continuing to work towards developing legal instruments to regulate the information and broadcasting sector.",""],[1,"171","11","Private Sector and Civil Society Participation in Information and Broadcasting","Continuing to open doors for the private sector, civil society and non-governmental organizations in the information and broadcasting sector.",""],[1,"171","12","News Program Quality Improvement","Improving the quality of the news programs.",""],[1,"171","13","Public Awareness and Educational Programming","Producing programs on a wide range of educational topics about society, laws, gender and children, and awareness programs for all circles and the community.",""]],"183":[[1,"173","8","Rural Investment Promotion Initiative","Encouraging investments in rural areas that will contribute to the development of the rural economy, reduce the gap between urban and rural areas, and improve the living standards of people as well as reduce migration from rural to urban areas and to foreign countries to seek jobs.",""]],"184":[[1,"172","13","Self-Supporting Industry Development Initiative","Development of Self-Supporting Industry: Development of Self-Supporting Industry: Promotes the competitive industries through self-reliance of energy and promoting the high value added industries and fostering the engineering manpower.",""]],"185":[[1,"173","5","Human Capital Promotion and Labor Law Enforcement","It would also help promote human capital; facilitate trade; enforce labor laws; and strengthen the dispute settlement mechanism.",""]],"186":[[1,"177","15","Industrial Corridor Development Along Main National Roads","Promoting industrial corridor development along the main national roads, linking key economic poles in Cambodia and connecting the Cambodian economy with the",""],[1,"178","3","Industrial Skills Training and Tertiary Education Reform","Human resource development especially the skill training for industrial sector through enhanced quality of education in all areas and at all levels, especially the reform of tertiary education, technical and vocational training, giving priority to training of engineers, technicians and workers to acquire appropriate skills as demanded by the markets with a pro-active approach using public-private sector partnerships.",""],[1,"178","5","Investment Environment Improvement and SME Linkage Development","Improving the investment environment for both large industries and SMEs, and establishes links and chains between large industries and SMEs.",""],[1,"178","8","Regulatory Review and Business Impact Assessment","Continuing to review regulations and assess the impact on business by the new regulations, to ensure that regulation promotes business within the domain of desirability.",""],[1,"178","9","Inter-Ministerial Industrial Facilitation Mechanism","Continuing to support industry through inter-ministerial facilitation mechanisms and through eliminating overlapped duties.",""],[1,"178","10","Public-Private Forum Mechanism","Continuing to promote the Public-Private Forum Mechanism for enhancing the reforms programs and promoting the private sector.",""],[1,"178","11","Sub-National Institutional Capacity Building and Delegation of Authority","Continuing to build the capacity of sub-national institutions and delegate authority to them for a closer access to the clients.",""],[1,"178","13","Business Development and Support Services through Industrial Institutions","Offer business development and supporting services through institutions like Cambodia Industrial Laboratory Center, National Productivity Center, Hatching Technology Center, Industrial Training Center, Cambodia Standard Center, National Metrological Center, etc.",""],[1,"178","14","SME Technical and Business Skills Support Programme","Supporting SMEs through imparting technical and business skills to them.",""],[1,"178","15","Knowledge Dissemination through National Movements","Disseminating knowledge through the National Production Movement, Entrepreneurship Movement, Business Potential Movement and the like.",""],[1,"178","16","Institutional Capacity Building for Property Rights, Research, and Creativity","Continuing to build institutional capacities in enforcing property rights, promoting research and creativity, and establishing support mechanisms.",""],[1,"179","1","SME Capacity-Building Technical Assistance","Providing technical assistance to build SME's capacities in formulating business plans, developing accounting systems, and generating information necessary to raise finances.",""],[1,"179","9","Enterprise Cluster Development for SMEs","Creating enterprise clusters for SMEs.",""]],"187":[[1,"178","2","Extractive Industry Regulatory and Supervision Strengthening","Further strengthening the development process in extractive industry, especially technical regulation and supervision including risk management, and social and environmental impact management from inception of operations to post operations;",""],[1,"178","2","Extractive Revenue Management Reform","and the management of fiscal revenue from this activity through development of policy, strengthening regulatory framework, capacity building, institutional coordination and human resource development.",""]],"188":[[1,"194","13","Mental Health Education and Service Expansion","Promote health education and practice of preventive measures for mental-health related illnesses, with expansion of primary and complementary mental health services, including addictive substance treatment.",""],[1,"194","19","Integrated Primary Prevention and Elderly Care Services","Provide integrated primary prevention for non-communicable and chronic diseases, including injury and disability, and elderly care services.",""],[1,"194","20","Early Cancer Detection, Diagnosis, and Treatment Services","Increase access to early detection, diagnosis, especially cervical cancer and breast cancer, and provide treatment services, including palliative care, nursing care, rehabilitation and kinesis therapy services.",""],[1,"194","21","Non-Communicable and Chronic Disease Care Improvement","Improve quality of care and treatment for non-communicable and chronic diseases at public and private health facilities (including having drug stocks).",""],[1,"194","23","Integrated Non-Communicable Disease Management at Health Facilities","Expand integrated management of non-communicable diseases at health facilities: counseling on preventing cancer, diabetes, blood pressure, etc.",""],[1,"194","25","Integration of Elderly Care and Occupational Health into Pre-Service Training","Include elderly care, environment health and vocational health, in pre-service training programs at public and private training institutions.",""],[1,"195","1","In-Service NCD Management Training and Coaching","Provide in-service training, coaching and post-training follow-up at the service delivery level on management of non-communicable diseases.",""],[1,"195","3","Mental Health Services Expansion and Harm Reduction Programme","Strengthen and expand coverage of mental health services, health education, prevention, counseling, and treatment (including harm reduction of drug addicts).",""],[1,"195","5","Medium- and Long-Term Disease Control Planning","Develop/update medium- and long-term plans for controlling non-communicable/chronic diseases, mental health, and substance abuse.",""],[1,"195","6","Oral Health Services and Hygiene Promotion","Increase access to quality oral health services, promote hygiene and sanitation practice and food safety.",""],[1,"195","7","Quit Smoking Campaigns","Step-up 'quit smoking' campaigns.",""],[1,"195","8","Tobacco and Alcohol Control Regulatory Measures","Implement legislation and regulations related to tobacco and alcohol control; restrict tobacco and alcohol advertisements; and bring sub-degree on occupational health risks and a sub-degree on smoke-free environment.",""],[1,"195","9","Health and Risk Factor Survey and Assessment Programme","Conduct surveys/assessments/studies related to non-communicable/chronic disease interventions (including STEPS Survey), adult tobacco use, alcohol use, chemical use, behavioral change toward injury and violence, environment health, and climate change.",""]],"189":[[1,"190","10","Expansion of the Equity Fund and Pro-Poor Health Financing Schemes","Further improving equity in access to health services through expansion of the equity fund and pro-poor health financing payment schemes for the poor; and development of health insurance system keeping in view Cambodia's socio-economic context and to promote the welfare of the people particularly by protecting the poor from the risk of excessive health spending.",""],[1,"195","12","Universal Social Health Protection Expansion","Ensure universal coverage by effective and appropriate use of resources and expansion of social health protection.",""],[1,"196","10","Health Equity Funds and Community-Based Health Insurance Expansion","Scale up Health Equity Funds, voucher schemes and other social assistance mechanisms and community-based Health Insurance; ensure comprehensive coverage of services through financing schemes, with a particular focus on reproductive health.",""],[1,"196","11","Standard Benefit Packages and Provider Payment Mechanisms for Pro-Poor Health Financing","Develop and implement standard benefit packages and appropriate provider payment mechanisms for pro-poor health financing schemes.",""],[1,"196","12","Universal Health Coverage and Social Health Protection Oversight","Move towards universal health coverage, including establishing institutional structures and capacity building for oversight of social health protection.",""],[1,"196","13","National Health Accounts and Social Health Protection Database Development","Develop national health account and comprehensive database for social health protection schemes' reporting and management systems.",""],[1,"196","14","Health Financing Policy Impact Evaluation","Conduct evaluation/analysis of impact of health financing policy interventions.",""],[1,"196","20","Facility-Managed Incentive Supplementation Management Improvement","Improve management of facility-managed incentive supplementation from user fees, Health Equity Funds and other demand-side financing mechanisms.",""]],"190":[[1,"203","12","Child Registration for Programme Entry and Monitoring","Central to this will be a call for registration of children to ease programe entry and monitoring.",""],[1,"204","5","Strengthening the National Targeting Mechanism (ID-Poor)","Strengthening the existing national targeting mechanism (ID-Poor) is a priority in the coming years.",""],[1,"204","6","Urban Social Protection Targeting Tool","an urban SP targeting tool needs designing, to allow social protection programs to be targeted on to the urban poor, including the mobile poor who are often the most excluded.",""],[1,"204","7","Climate-Vulnerability-Responsive Social Assistance Targeting","Incorporating climate vulnerability in the existing targeting system so that the most vulnerable to climate hazards can get social assistance.",""],[1,"204","9","One Window Service Office Social Protection Delivery Mechanism","The social service delivery mechanism using the One Window Service Office will be tested and applied to ensure coordination between different components of social protection at the sub-national level in rural areas.",""],[1,"204","10","Social Protection Outcome Monitoring System","Effective systems for social protection outcome monitoring need to be developed to allow harmonized program implementation.",""],[1,"204","10","Common Monitoring Framework for Social Protection","Evidence-based decisions on social protection provision will be developed through a common monitoring framework for the NSPS.",""],[1,"208","6","Population Policy Monitoring and Updating Mechanism","Strengthening institutional capacity to identify emerging population issues by periodically carrying out analyses and to monitor and update population policy.",""]],"191":[[1,"202","15","Disaster Response Mechanism Strengthening","Further strengthening mechanisms to respond to disasters, with focus on protection of victims during and after disasters through further strengthened relevant institutions and",""],[1,"203","1","Natural Disaster Management Coordination Mechanism","mechanisms, in particular Committee for Natural Disaster Management, by further increasing collaboration, cooperation and coordination with all related stakeholders such as the Cambodian Red Cross, various international humanitarian aid agencies, private sector, donors and other partners.",""],[1,"203","2","Cambodia Food Reserve Management Committee Strengthening","Further strengthening food security, especially the mechanism of \"Cambodia Food Reserve Management Committee\".",""],[1,"204","14","Social Assistance for Disaster-Affected Poor and Vulnerable People","Increase social intervention to help the poor and vulnerable victims of natural disasters.",""]],"192":[[1,"203","4","Technical, Professional, and Entrepreneurship Skills Training Support","Taking further initiatives in creating job opportunities through support provided to poor people to receive training and retraining in technical, professional, and entrepreneurship skills, that will help self-employment of workers or facilitate their job search in the market.",""],[1,"203","13","Public Works Program Expansion","Scaling up public works programs would help address vulnerability to shocks and seasonal unemployment.",""]],"193":[[1,"203","5","Flexible Social Protection Measures for Economic Crises","Introducing a package of flexible measures according to prevalent circumstances to provide protection to the vulnerable during future economic crises which may be faced by the country.",""],[1,"203","7","Financial Inclusion Expansion through Microfinance and Micro-Insurance","Enhancing financial inclusion through expansion of coverage and intermediation of microfinance and micro-insurance services at affordable prices and favorable terms and conditions, including state assistance in financing business creation through the \"National Fund for Training and Poverty Reduction\".",""],[1,"204","8","Local Social Protection Planning and Delivery","Localizing Social Protection planning and delivery so that assistance could be tailored to local needs.",""],[1,"204","15","Poverty and Vulnerability Support Programme Expansion","Continue expanding the program to help the poor and vulnerable and prevent the vulnerability of poor people.",""],[1,"205","4","Pro-Poor Policy Development and Implementation","Prepare and implement policies for the betterment of the poor communities.",""]],"194":[[1,"204","1","School Feeding Expansion Programme","Scaling up school feeding meals (including for pre-schools) to improve educational outcomes, especially among poor children.",""],[1,"204","2","Poverty-Targeted Scholarship Expansion","Scaling up poverty-targeted scholarship programs to improve food security and nutrition and education outcomes, especially among poor children.",""],[1,"209","6","Scholarships and Support for Female Students","its policy aiming at increasing educational opportunities for female students through increased scholarships, additional training programs, accommodation and safe transportation, and increasing the number of female teachers",""],[1,"209","7","Education for Women and Girls Initiative","Specifically, the RGC will put strong focus on women's economic empowerment, gender and climate change and green growth, women's decision making in public and political spheres, legal protection for women and girls, women's health, and education for women and girls.",""],[1,"210","17","Girls' Scholarship Expansion","Increase scholarship for girls in upper secondary and higher educations.",""],[1,"210","18","Parental Awareness Campaign for Girls' Education","Raise awareness of parents in order increase girls' access to education.",""]],"195":[[1,"205","13","Youth Rehabilitation and Juvenile Justice Program","Promote youth rehabilitation and implement the juvenile justice program, and continue providing legal services to protect the rights of juveniles who have violated the law.",""],[1,"205","13","Legal Services for Juveniles","continue providing legal services to protect the rights of juveniles who have violated the law.",""],[1,"205","14","Rehabilitation Treatment Center Policy","Continue to implement the policy on rehabilitation treatment center to help victims of addictive substances.",""]],"196":[[1,"207","9","Human Resources Development Measures","Further developing human resources with focus on strengthening the quality, ability and work ethic standards, through implementing a variety of interconnected measures in education, research, science, technology, technical and vocational training, and health.",""],[1,"207","10","Youth Vocational and Entrepreneurial Skills Development Programme","Promoting youth through strengthening vocational training programs and equipping them with technical and entrepreneurial skills.",""]],"197":[[1,"210","6","Gender Representation Monitoring and Audit Framework","Develop a monitoring and evaluation framework and carry out periodic gender audits on representation and participation of men and women in politics and decision making positions.",""],[1,"210","7","Women's Political Representation and Leadership Promotion","Develop and strengthen policies, legal provisions and programes, to increase women's representation in politics and other key decision making positions.",""],[1,"210","8","Women Leaders Capacity Building and Political Participation Support Programme","Formulate and implement capacity building programes for sitting and aspiring women leaders and support initiatives, including resource mobilisation efforts that seek to promote women in politics and other governance structures.",""],[1,"210","9","Young Women Leadership and Assertiveness Programme","Invest in programes aimed at enhancing assertiveness and leadership confidence in young women to ensure equal participation in leadership in schools, tertiary institutions and youth groups and other community based organisations.",""],[1,"210","10","Affirmative Action Measures for Gender Equality","Set affirmative action measures in areas where sharp gender disparities exist, (e.g. Increasing quota for women on electoral candidates list).",""],[1,"210","11","Parliament Gender Focal Point and Working Group","Create and support a focal point/gender working group in Parliament for women in parliament to communicate with each other and organisations in civil society, promote the application of gender lens to decisions taken by all Parliamentary Committees.",""]],"198":[[1,"212","1","Government Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Efficient Service Delivery","Finally, effort will be made to strengthen the capacities of government institutions for them to deliver services efficiently; in this regard, priority will be attached to e-governance and e-services for improving efficiency and reducing costs.",""],[1,"214","8","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Efficient Service Delivery","resources required to strengthen the capacity of RGC institutions to deliver their programs and services efficiently at 3,781.73 billion Riels or USD 922.3 million",""],[1,"241","5","Government Capacity and E-Governance Improvement Initiative","Improving capacities within the government (both at the national and sub- national levels) to deliver quality services through better inter-ministry/agency communication and sharing of information, improved (vertical) integration between the sub-national levels and the apex ministries/agencies, and promoting e-governance.",""]],"199":[[1,"235","1","Village Development Committee Capacity Building for Climate Change Resilience and Science Awareness","Capacity Building for Village development Committee on the option of resistant and reduce climate change and the on acceptable science awareness in the rural areas.",""]],"200":[[1,"212","1","Human Capacity Development and Resource Targeting for Poorer and Hinterland Populations","Among other priorities, effort will be made to use the said resources to build human capacities at all levels-with a focus at the sub-national levels-and also to target resources towards improving the lot of the poorer populations and of the hinterland.",""]]}});